{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TemB7bG96Hg4ZXXmBNnCEy","type":"tool_result","content":"400\t### 7.1 Rail camera (`11-rail.js`)\n401\t\n402\t- Rail knots become an `E.Path` (catmull). The camera's distance `d` advances at `speed × T.railSpeed` and eases to 0\n403\t  over .6 s at a **hold** (and back up over .8 s after it). Holds wait for `until`: `beat:<id>` (that beat's enemies are\n404\t  dead or gone), `vehicle`/`air`/`boat` (that quota's live units are gone), `escort` (the escort is resolved), `quota` (all\n405\t  quotas met), or `boss` (the boss is dead). A hold with `max` lets go after that many seconds; a unit still alive then\n406\t  leaves and comes back in the reinforcement loop (7.14).\n407\t- Per-knot tweens: `angle` (yaw), `h`, `pitch`, `fov`. River bob: `h ± 1.2` and `pitch ± .5°` at .35 Hz. Walking sway on\n408\t  land: `h ± .4` at the step rate (1.6 Hz), and no sway while held.\n409\t- **Segment cuts** (Op 6's takeoff): `rail.cut(nextRail, { fade: 'wipe' })` swaps rails behind a .4 s transition.\n410\t- Camera shake is the engine's `game.shake` (screen space), scaled by the standard shake setting.\n411\t\n412\t### 7.2 Projection and hit testing (`10-view3d.js`, `12-hit.js`)\n413\t\n414\t- At the start of every step: `view.begin(cam)`. Every hittable thing produces **hit shapes** in buffer pixels, each with\n415\t  a depth (distance along the view direction).\n416\t  - **Humanoids** (standing height `h` from the calibration table, 9.2): head is a circle at `z + .885h`, radius `.085h`;\n417\t    body is a rectangle from `z + .45h` to `z + .80h`, half-width `.17h`; legs are a rectangle from `z` to `z + .45h`,\n418\t    half-width `.12h`. Kneeling: heights × .72. Behind cover: anything below the cover's top `z` is removed. In a window or\n419\t    door: everything is clipped to the opening's projected rectangle. Dying: no shapes. Minimum size: body 4×8 px, head\n420\t    radius 2 px.\n421\t  - **Vehicles, boats, aircraft:** the convex hull of the 8 projected corners of the hull box, plus each weak point as a\n422\t    circle (a local offset turned by facing, radius in units, at least 4 px).\n423\t  - **Projectiles and pickups:** circles, radius `r × k`, at least 5 px for projectiles and 6 px for pickups (fairness).\n424\t  - **Cover and props:** a hull of the projected box. Cover stops bullets; props take damage.\n425\t- **A shot** at point `p` (the crosshair plus bloom, 7.4) hits the **nearest** shape containing `p`. If that is cover, the\n426\t  bullet stops there (sparks or dust). With no shape, the floor point `toFloor(p)` gets a dust puff, or nothing if `p` is\n427\t  above the horizon.\n428\t- **Explosions** query by world distance (3D) to every entity and prop, civilians and hostages included.\n429\t- **Calibrate in M0:** draw each rig preset with the engine at view scale 1, in standing, kneeling and crouching poses, to\n430\t  an offscreen canvas; measure the bounding box; and write `WP.RIG_H` from it. A dev toggle draws every hit shape over the\n431\t  scene to check alignment (section 11).\n432\t\n433\t### 7.3 Crosshair and aiming (`30-players.js`)\n434\t\n435\t- **Mouse:** absolute. The crosshair equals the pointer, clamped to the playfield. Mouse play gets no aim assist.\n436\t- **Stick:** velocity = `T.padSpeed` (520 px/s) × setting multiplier (.5–2) × `curve(|s|) = |s|^2.0`. After .3 s held\n437\t  above .95 deflection, ×1.5 (turbo). Stick vector = left + .5 × right (`input.padMove`, `input.padAim`). The d-pad nudges\n438\t  at 90 px/s.\n439\t- **Keys:** 300 px/s, ramping to 520 over .4 s.\n440\t- **Aim assist** for pads and keys (`assist` = Off 0 / Low .35 / Medium .6 / High .85; RECRUIT adds .15):\n441\t  - *Friction:* inside a hostile's hit shapes grown by 6 px, crosshair speed × (1 − .55 × assist).\n442\t  - *Magnetism:* while the stick is moving and a hostile's body center is within 28 px with direction dot > .3, pull\n443\t    toward it at 160 × assist px/s.\n444\t  - *Snap* (L1/Q): ease .08 s to the highest-priority threat (a projectile about to hit, then the telegraph closest to\n445\t    firing, then the nearest hostile), preferring the stick's direction. .2 s cooldown.\n446\t  - Never toward civilians, hostages or animals.\n447\t- Co-op start positions: P1 at 42% of the width, P2 at 58%, P3 at 30%, P4 at 70%, all at 55% of the height.\n448\t\n449\t### 7.4 Weapon: the WOLF-9 SMG (`31-weapon.js`)\n450\t\n451\t- **Fire:** `T.fireRate` 11 rounds a second while fire is held. The first round fires on the press step; the rest follow\n452\t  on a fixed interval, so the count is exact for the tests.\n453\t- **Bloom:** offset radius `T.spreadBase` 1.5 px, +`T.bloomPerShot` .8 px a shot, up to `T.bloomMax` 7 px, recovering at\n454\t  18 px/s. Each shot's offset comes from the `sim` stream (uniform in a disc).\n455\t- **Damage:** `T.bulletDmg` 1 a hit; a head hit does ×2, and ×4 on BRUTES and TUSK.\n456\t- **Magazines:** `mag` (rounds in the gun, `T.magSize` 30) and `spares`, a list of round counts (start 5 full spares, so 6\n457\t  magazines; pouch limit `T.maxMags` 9, or 11 after Op 4's perk). **Reload** (`T.reloadTime` 1.0 s) loads the fullest\n458\t  spare; a part-used magazine goes back into the pouch with its rounds (no waste, no merging). Auto-reload starts .12 s\n459\t  after the gun runs dry. Manual reload works whenever `mag < magSize` and a spare exists. Firing on empty clicks.\n460\t- **FURY** (pickup): `T.furySeconds` 10 s, fire rate ×2, damage ×1.5, no ammo used, golden tracers, a music sting, and a\n461\t  ring timer around the crosshair.\n462\t- **Accuracy stat:** shots that hit a hostile, projectile, pickup or prop ÷ shots fired.\n463\t- **Tracers and impacts:** each round draws a 1-frame tracer from the gun's muzzle (the overlay, or the player's edge of\n464\t  the screen in co-op) to the impact point, plus impact FX by material (dust, sparks on metal, splinters on wood, splashes\n465\t  on water).\n466\t\n467\t### 7.5 Grenades and explosions\n468\t\n469\t- Start with `T.startGrenades` 4; pouch limit 9. On a press, the target is the entity under the crosshair (its 3D point,\n470\t  so helicopters can be air-burst) if it is within `T.grenadeRange` 420 units. Otherwise it is the floor point under the\n471\t  crosshair, clamped to range; above the horizon, the point at range along the view ray.\n472\t- Flight time `.55 + .0015 × distance` s along an `E.arc` lob from the camera's lower front (`h − 6`). A small sprite\n473\t  spins on the way, with a shadow dot on the floor. You can't throw another for .5 s.\n474\t- **Blast:** radius `T.grenadeRadius` 52 units, damage `T.grenadeDmg` 12 at the center falling to 6 at the edge. Every\n475\t  infantry type inside dies except BRUTES, which take the damage. Vehicles and weak points take the damage. Enemies within\n476\t  1.5 × radius are stunned for 1 s. **Civilians and hostages inside are hurt** (penalties apply). Props in range take the\n477\t  damage, which chains barrels and tanks. Supply animals in range drop their items and flee.\n478\t- **Explosion feel:** a fireball, smoke, debris and a shock ring on the floor; `game.flash('#fff0c0', .08)`; `game.shake(3)`;\n479\t  .04 s hit-stop (`game.freeze`); rumble; boom plus a low sine thump.\n480\t- **DYNAMITE** (pickup, shot to trigger): a screen-wide blast. Every non-boss enemy in view dies; vehicles and bosses take\n481\t  30; **civilians and hostages in view take a penalty hit each**. White flash, big shake.\n482\t\n483\t### 7.6 Enemy AI (`21-infantry.js`, `22-enemyfire.js`)\n484\t\n485\tEach infantry entity runs a small state machine: `enter` → `move` → `cover`/`stand` → `telegraph` → `attack` → `recover`,\n486\trepeated `cycles` times, then `exit` (runs off) or `advance`. Its reactions: `hurt` (a .25 s flinch that cancels a\n487\ttelegraph; for HP > 1 types), `stun` (1 s, from nearby grenades), and `die` (the `die` pose; the body falls and fades after\n488\t2.5 s). Speeds: walk 32, run 70, sprint 110 u/s.\n489\t\n490\t| Behavior | What it does |\n491\t|---|---|\n492\t| `cross` | runs from one edge to the other at a depth; with `stops`, stops once or twice to fire |\n493\t| `sprint` | a fast cross that never fires (quota fodder, and practice) |\n494\t| `popup` | hides behind a cover prop and stands every 2–3 s to fire (`cycles` 2–4); between pops only the head shows |\n495\t| `window` / `door` | the same inside a building opening, clipped to it (shutters open first: .3 s) |\n496\t| `advance` | walks toward the camera to depth 70, then fires (or throws knives) from there |\n497\t| `para` | parachutes from z 160 at 22 u/s. The chute (2 px+ circle above) and the body are both hittable; a shot chute drops him fast to his death. On landing he becomes `cross` |\n498\t| `dismount` | leaves a truck, APC or boat and fans out (`cross` or `popup` on nearby cover) |\n499\t| `chase` | follows a hostage; within 10 units for 1 s he grabs and drags the hostage back (7.11) |\n500\t| `mortar` | a crew of two behind sandbags far away; launches every 6 s |\n501\t| `snipe` | stationary at a tower, window or tree; a lens glint telegraph |\n502\t| `officer` | blows a whistle for 2 s (an icon over his head); if he finishes, 3 riflemen arrive (2 after Op 1's perk). Kill him during the whistle to cancel it |\n503\t\n504\t**Enemy fire** (`22-enemyfire.js`):\n505\t\n506\t- When the telegraph starts, the enemy picks a target player: a random living one, from the `ai` stream. The ring is drawn\n507\t  in that player's seat color, so in co-op everyone sees who is targeted. Ring radius 22 → 6 px over the telegraph time,\n508\t  shifting yellow → orange → red, with a tick that rises in pitch.\n509\t- When it closes, if the enemy is alive and not stunned, it fires `bullets` hitscan rounds .1 s apart. Each one hits with\n510\t  chance `accuracy(type) × depthFactor × difficulty × T.enemyAccuracy × spotted` (`depthFactor`: 1 at depth ≤ 150, falling\n511\t  linearly to .55 at 500 and beyond; `spotted` is 1.5 while a searchlight is on the camera). A hit adds `damage ×\n512\t  T.enemyDamage` to the target. Hit or miss, the enemy shows a muzzle flash and a tracer to the screen's lower edge; a miss\n513\t  makes a whiz.\n514\t- Direction cue: every hit flashes a red arc on the screen edge toward the shooter (left, right or center).\n515\t\n516\t### 7.7 Projectiles (`23-projectiles.js`)\n517\t\n518\t| Kind | Thrown or fired by | Motion | Flight | Shootable | Damage | Intercept score |\n519\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n520\t| grenade | GRENADIER, boss decks | an `E.arc` lob to a point 12 units in front of the camera (±20 sideways) | 1.3 s | yes, 1 hit, r 4 | 12 | 50 |\n521\t| knife | KNIFE | straight and spinning (the sprite's `rot`) | .65 s | yes, 1 hit, r 3 | 8 | 100 |\n522\t| rocket | RPG, APC, BIG EAR, IRON HOG | straight, ±2 u wobble, a smoke trail | 1.6 s | yes, 1 hit, r 4 | 16 | 150 |\n523\t| missile | VULTURE, HYENA ONE | slight homing toward the camera | 1.8 s | yes, 1 hit, r 4 | 18 | 200 |\n524\t| mortar shell | mortar crews, CROCODILE, IRON HOG | a high arc from far away, a falling whistle, a landing marker on the HUD's top edge | 2.6 s | yes, 1 hit, r 4 | 14 | 100 |\n525\t| tank shell | MAULER, WARTHOG's cannon, HYENA ONE's nose cannon | fast and straight, a big glow | .8 s | yes, 2 hits, r 6 | 22 | 250 |\n526\t| flame wave | WARTHOG | rolls along the ground toward the camera | 1.2 s | no (stop it at the source) | 15 | n/a |\n527\t\n528\tA projectile \"hits\" when its depth drops below 14. Shot down, it pops in the air (a small explosion, or sparks for a\n529\tknife), scores, and counts as an intercept (a stat and an award).\n530\t\n531\t### 7.8 Vehicles and aircraft (`24-vehicles.js`)\n532\t\n533\tVehicles are shapes-as-data drawn by `m7.shape` (quantized to 16 facings), moving along paths, with overlays for moving\n534\tparts (wheels, rotors, turrets as separate shapes with their own facing, dishes, propellers). Damage states: under 50%\n535\tsmoking, under 25% burning, at 0 an explosion chain (3 blasts over .6 s, `explosion(..., { debris })`). The wreck (charred\n536\tmaterials) stays as cover for 6 s, then fades (on water, it sinks). A vehicle with a gunner (a separate rig, HP 1) stops\n537\tfiring when the gunner dies. Vehicles that leave the screen alive come back in the reinforcement loop.\n538\t\n539\t### 7.9 Bosses (`25-bosses.js`)\n540\t\n541\tThe boss framework is `{ phases: [{ weak: [...], attacks: [...], onEnd }], intro, defeat }`. The boss bar is the sum of\n542\tthe current phase's weak points. Weak points that can be hurt blink at 3 Hz with a white outline; armored parts spark and\n543\tshow \"ARMORED\" once. Intro: a klaxon, the card `WARNING!` + name (`E.Arcade.card`), a radio line, music to `boss`.\n544\tDefeat: .5 s at `timeScale .3`, the explosion chain, a white flash, a victory sting, then the tally. Each boss is in 8.7.\n545\t\n546\t### 7.10 Player damage, DOWN, continue\n547\t\n548\t- `damage` runs 0–100; at 100 the player is **DOWN**. Solo: a death beat (camera h → 8 and pitch −10 over .8 s, a red\n549\t  tint, a fade), then **CONTINUE?** (`E.Arcade.continue(10, done)`). Continuing restarts the current operation from its\n550\t  start, with damage 0, the score kept, `continues + 1` (it affects the rank), and the ammo the player had when the op\n551\t  began (at least 4 magazines and 3 grenades). Without a continue comes the GAME OVER card (\"THE HUNT IS OVER... FOR\n552\t  NOW.\" and the score), then initials if the score qualifies, then the title. This is not the 0-hostage ending, which\n553\t  only follows Op 6.\n554\t- **Co-op:** a DOWN player's crosshair turns grey and their panel shows \"DOWN\". They come back at the next operation with\n555\t  damage 50. All players DOWN brings up the continue screen for everyone.\n556\t- **DRY rule** (mag 0, no spares, no grenades). On ARCADE it is the source's rule: DOWN. On VETERAN and RECRUIT an\n557\t  **emergency drop** parachutes in within 4 s and delivers 2 full magazines to that player when it lands (score −2000,\n558\t  \"RESUPPLY FEE\"), at most once every 30 s. RECRUIT also refills a 15-round magazine 3 s after going dry.\n559\t- Healing: RATION −15, MEDKIT −35, stage clear −`clearHeal` (10; Op 3: 40).\n560\t\n561\t### 7.11 Civilians, hostages, animals (`26-friendlies.js`)\n562\t\n563\t- **Civilians** (villagers, medic pairs with a stretcher, a reporter) cross on paths and **panic** when shots land within\n564\t  40 units: they run 1.5× faster with their hands over their heads. **A player hit** on a civilian adds `T.civilianDamage`\n565\t  (8) to that player, costs 1000 points and the streak, and shows a big red \"CIVILIAN HIT!\". The civilian falls (wounded,\n566\t  not killed), crawls off-screen and doesn't return. A civilian who crosses unharmed while enemies are on screen tosses a\n567\t  small gift 10% of the time (\"THANK YOU!\": a RATION or MAG).\n568\t- **Hostages** (Ops 5 and 6): each has HP 3 against enemy fire, shown as pips over its head. A player hit costs +10\n569\t  damage, −2000 points and −1 hostage HP. Each hostage follows an escort path at 46 u/s. A `chase` enemy within 10 units\n570\t  for 1 s **grabs** it and drags it back toward its spawn at 20 u/s; shoot him within 3 s and the hostage runs on, or it is\n571\t  **lost**. At 0 HP it falls and is lost. Reaching the goal counts it rescued (+5000, a cheer, its portrait lit on the HUD).\n572\t- **Supply animals** (never killed): goats, chickens, pigs, parrots, monkeys, seagulls, built with `E.Blob`. Any hit or\n573\t  nearby blast makes one squawk, drop the item it carries (shown as a pack on its back or a bundle in its beak), and bolt.\n574\t- **Friendly markers** (setting, on by default): a small green ▼ over a civilian or hostage while a crosshair is within 36\n575\t  px of it.\n576\t\n577\t### 7.12 Destructibles and cover (`27-props.js`)\n578\t\n579\t| Prop | HP | Blocks shots | On destruction |\n580\t|---|---|---|---|\n581\t| wooden crate | 3 | no | splinters; drop roll (60%) |\n582\t| ammo crate (olive, stenciled) | 3 | no | drop from {MAG 50, AMMO CRATE 20, GRENADE 20, GRENADE BOX 10} |\n583\t| red fuel barrel | 4 | no | explosion r 48, damage 10 (it chains) |\n584\t| sandbag wall | 40 (grenade 15) | yes, below its top | chips through 3 visual stages; gone at 0 |\n585\t| wreck | n/a | yes | fades after 6 s |\n586\t| radio mast (Op 1) | 25 at its junction box | no | sparks, then topples over 1.2 s (shape tilt steps), dust |\n587\t| fuel tank (Op 4) | 20 | yes | a big explosion r 90, damage 20, chains |\n588\t| searchlight (Ops 5, 6) | 2 | no | glass pops; its beam goes out |\n589\t| bridge rope (Op 2) | 6 each end | no | the bridge drops: every soldier on it falls (+300 each, \"BRIDGE OUT!\") |\n590\t| ammo wagon (Op 4) | 4 | no | explosion r 70, damage 30 (hits the train car next to it) |\n591\t| window shutters | 1 | no | swing open (snipers can't hide behind them) |\n592\t\n593\t### 7.13 Pickups and the supply director (`28-pickups.js`)\n594\t\n595\t| Pickup | Sprite | Effect | Where it comes from |\n596\t|---|---|---|---|\n597\t| MAG | olive magazine | +1 full spare (at the pouch limit: +300 points) | crates, animals, gifts, carriers |\n598\t| AMMO CRATE | stenciled box | +3 full spares | ammo crates, supply parachutes |\n599\t| GRENADE | pineapple | +1 grenade | crates, animals |\n600\t| GRENADE BOX | box of 3 | +3 grenades | ammo crates, monkeys |\n601\t| RATION | tin | damage −15 | crates, animals, gifts |\n602\t| MEDKIT | white box, green cross | damage −35 | rare; more after Op 3's perk |\n603\t| FURY | golden SMG | FURY mode for 10 s (7.4) | rare; scripted once per op |\n604\t| DYNAMITE | bundle of red sticks | screen blast (7.5) | scripted, once per op from Op 3 |\n605\t| FLARE | red flare | lights the night scene for 12 s and outlines snipers (Op 5) | Op 5 crates |\n606\t| INTEL | folder | +1500 | officers, the reporter |\n607\t| WOLF FANG | white fang | +500 | rare animal drop |\n608\t\n609\t- Dropped items pop up, bounce twice, hover with a glow, last 6 s (blinking for the final 1.5), and are collected by\n610\t  shooting them once. In co-op, the player who shot it gets it.\n611\t- **Supply director** (`loot` stream, deterministic): a crate's base drop chance is 60%, and carriers always drop.\n612\t  Weights adjust to need: lowest player's total rounds (mag + spares × 30) under 60 → MAG ×3; grenades 0 → GRENADE ×2;\n613\t  damage over 60 → RATION/MEDKIT ×2. At most one FURY per beat. Below 1 magazine and 0 grenades, a **supply parachute**\n614\t  (AMMO CRATE) arrives mid-screen within 2 s, at most once every 20 s.\n615\t\n616\t### 7.14 Quotas, beats, reinforcements, clear, perks (`33-sim.js`)\n617\t\n618\t- Quotas count kills by class (`soldier`, `vehicle`, `air`, `boat`) and show as counters counting down. Masts (Op 1) are\n619\t  an objective chip.\n620\t- **The boss comes when the rail's end is reached and every quota is met.** When a quota is met early, its counter shows a\n621\t  check and later spawns still score. When the rail ends with quota left, the **reinforcement loop** runs at the final\n622\t  hold: every 3–5 s it spawns from a weighted list biased toward the missing classes (a jeep if vehicles are missing, a\n623\t  VULTURE if air is) until the quotas are met, with a radio line: \"MORE OF THEM ARE COMING!\". Scripted spawns total about\n624\t  quota ÷ .85, so a careful player needs few or no reinforcements.\n625\t- Enemies that leave the screen (more than 60 px past the edge for 2 s) despawn as escaped, which doesn't count toward the\n626\t  quota.\n627\t- **Clear:** the tally (10.2 `tally`), then the perk card, then the heal, then the map.\n628\t\n629\t| Perk | From | Effect for the rest of the run |\n630\t|---|---|---|\n631\t| COMMS DOWN | Op 1 | quotas ×.8 in later ops; whistles call 2, not 3 |\n632\t| CAMP LOCATED (intel) | Op 2 | the interrogation; snipers and mortars in later ops show a red marker for their first 1.5 s |\n633\t| VILLAGE LIBERATED | Op 3 | damage −40 now; MEDKIT weight ×2 |\n634\t| SUPPLIES SEIZED | Op 4 | spares and grenades refilled to the limits now; pouch limit +2 magazines (11) |\n635\t| HOSTAGES FREED (n/5) | Op 5 | n hostages come to Op 6 |\n636\t\n637\t### 7.15 Scoring, streaks, ranks, high scores (`32-scoring.js`)\n638\t\n639\t- **Kills:** RIFLEMAN 100, GRENADIER 150, KNIFE 200, BRUTE 500, RPG 300, SNIPER 400, MORTAR 200 each, OFFICER 600,\n640\t  PARATROOPER 150 (+100 while airborne). Jeep 1000, truck 1200, APC 2000, tank 3000, skiff 800, patrol boat 1500, VULTURE\n641\t  3000. Bosses 10000 (Op 1) to 30000 (Op 6). Headshot +50%. Intercepts per 7.7.\n642\t- **Streak:** +1 a kill; multiplier = 1 + ⌊streak ÷ 8⌋, at most ×4. Taking damage, or hitting a civilian or hostage,\n643\t  resets it; so do 4 s without a kill. At ×4: \"PACK FURY!\" and a howl.\n644\t- **Tally per op:** soldiers and vehicles, accuracy (accuracy% × 100 × op number), headshots × 200, intercepts × 100,\n645\t  CIVILIANS SPARED +5000 (or −1000 for each hit), op bonus 10000 × op number, hostages × 5000 (Ops 5, 6). One line at a\n646\t  time, big numbers.\n647\t- **Ranks:** ALPHA WOLF (5 hostages, 0 continues, accuracy ≥ 55%), PACK LEADER (≥ 4 hostages), TIMBER WOLF (≥ 3), LONE\n648\t  WOLF (1–2), WOLF PUP (0). Loop 2 and later put `BLACK MOON` before the rank.\n649\t- **High scores:** `E.Arcade` (`id: 'wolfpack'`, mode `'campaign'`; Mission Select uses `'op1'` … `'op6'`), top ten with\n650\t  initials on the letter wheel. In co-op, everyone who qualifies enters theirs in turn. Hub rounds save nothing (the hub\n651\t  gives the game a throwaway storage anyway).\n652\t\n653\t### 7.16 Difficulty and co-op scaling (`01-tuning.js`)\n654\t\n655\t| | RECRUIT | VETERAN (default) | ARCADE |\n656\t|---|---|---|---|\n657\t| Enemy accuracy | ×.6 | ×1 | ×1.25 |\n658\t| Telegraph time | ×1.35 | ×1 | ×.85 |\n659\t| Enemy damage | ×.7 | ×1 | ×1.2 |\n660\t| Drop chances | ×1.4 | ×1 | ×.8 |\n661\t| Quotas | ×.85 | ×1 | ×1.1 |\n662\t| Aim assist | +.15 | ±0 | magnetism off |\n663\t| DRY | refill after 3 s + emergency drop | emergency drop | DOWN (the source's rule) |\n664\t\n665\tCo-op with n players: quotas and spawn counts both × (1 + .3(n − 1)) (rounded, deterministic, so the quota-to-spawn\n666\tratio stays about .85), and each player has their own damage, ammo, grenades and score. Loop 2 and later: ARCADE multipliers × 1.15 on top of the chosen level.\n667\t\n668\t---\n669\t\n670\t## 8. Content\n671\t\n672\t### 8.1 Setting and cast\n673\t\n674\t- **The Brimstone Coast:** a fictional tropical coast under a smoking volcano, Mount Brimstone. Jungle, mangrove rivers,\n675\t  fishing villages, a munitions depot, an old cliff-top prison, an airfield. The time is unstated; the feel is 1987.\n676\t- **General Hugo Kragg, \"the Hyena\":** a bulky mercenary general with a peaked cap, a greatcoat and gold trim. He laughs a\n677\t  high hyena cackle and rides the gunship HYENA ONE.\n678\t- **The Hyena Legion:** tan uniforms with brown spots (a custom `spots` pattern), red armbands with a grinning hyena\n679\t  emblem (original art), caps, helmets and bandanas.\n680\t- **The Wolfpack:** callsigns only. WOLF 1 **LOBO** (the leader; red headband, black hair, stubble), WOLF 2 **FANG**\n681\t  (backward cap, crew cut), WOLF 3 **TUNDRA** (white ponytail, green beret), WOLF 4 **MOONSHINE** (yellow bandana). Solo,\n682\t  you are LOBO.\n683\t- **DEN MOTHER:** the handler on the radio (grey short hair, green beret, coat).\n684\t- **MAJOR TUSK:** the warden of the Kennel (bulky, helmet, armor, a riot shield).\n685\t- **PRIVATE GIGGS:** a nervous Hyena who giggles under interrogation.\n686\t- **The five hostages** (relief convoy, each with its own clothes and colors, hands bound): DR. AMARA OKONJO (a doctor;\n687\t  white coat), HAL BRODY (an engineer; glasses, rolled sleeves), LUCIA MARCH (a reporter; vest), \"SKIP\" TANAKA (a pilot;\n688\t  flight jacket; aboard OLD HOWLER, he takes the co-pilot's seat in the ending), AMBASSADOR GRANT WHITFIELD (a torn suit).\n689\t- **OLD HOWLER:** the Wolfpack's twin-prop cargo plane with a rear ramp.\n690\t\n691\t### 8.2 Writing style (like the source's)\n692\t\n693\tALL CAPS for cards, radio subtitles and HUD words. Short lines: 2–9 words, at most 2 lines per box. Plain military words\n694\t(COPY, INBOUND, MOVE OUT). Exclamations for alerts. Now and then a little of the stiff, earnest 80s arcade-translation\n695\tvoice (\"ENEMY AIR SUPPORT IS COMING!\", \"YOU ARE OUR LAST HOPE.\"), charming and never mocking. The villain is theatrical\n696\tand laughs. Nothing graphic. Every line has a speaker, a gibberish voice and a subtitle (the text is the subtitle). Every\n697\tstring lives in `WP.TEXT`.\n698\t\n699\t### 8.3 Story beats and key lines (these exact lines; add more in the same voice)\n700\t\n701\t- **Intro (`briefing`, skippable):** cards over a slow pan of the coast at night:\n702\t  \"THE BRIMSTONE COAST.\" · \"GENERAL KRAGG AND HIS HYENA LEGION HAVE TAKEN IT.\" · \"FIVE RELIEF WORKERS ARE HIS PRISONERS.\" ·\n703\t  \"NO ARMY WILL GO IN. SO THEY SENT THE PACK.\"\n704\t  DEN: \"WOLFPACK, THIS IS DEN MOTHER. YOUR MISSION: RESCUE THE FIVE HOSTAGES.\" · DEN: \"AMMUNITION IS LIMITED. SHOOT\n705\t  SUPPLY CRATES TO RESTOCK.\" · DEN: \"DO NOT SHOOT CIVILIANS. GOOD HUNTING.\" · LOBO: \"AWOOOO!\" (the howl).\n706\t- **Op cards:** OP 1 RADIO HILL, \"DESTROY THE ENEMY RADIO STATION\" · OP 2 MANGROVE RUN, \"BREAK THROUGH THE RIVER PATROL\" ·\n707\t  OP 3 PALM VILLAGE, \"FREE THE VILLAGE. SPARE THE PEOPLE.\" · OP 4 POWDER KEG DEPOT, \"TAKE THE SUPPLIES. BLOW THE REST.\" ·\n708\t  OP 5 THE KENNEL, \"RESCUE THE HOSTAGES\" · OP 6 LAST FLIGHT OUT, \"GET THEM ON THE PLANE\".\n709\t- **First-time tips** (radio, each once per save; see 8.6): \"SHOOT ITEMS TO COLLECT THEM!\" · \"GRENADE INCOMING! SHOOT IT\n710\t  DOWN!\" · \"{reload} TO RELOAD. DON'T RUN DRY!\" · \"{grenade} THROWS A GRENADE.\" · \"KNIVES CAN BE SHOT OUT OF THE AIR!\" ·\n711\t  \"STOP THAT WHISTLE!\" · \"BIG ONES GO DOWN FASTER WITH A HEADSHOT.\" · \"CIVILIANS! WATCH YOUR FIRE!\" ({reload} and {grenade}\n712\t  are `input.label` values, filled in when spoken.)\n713\t- **Boss warnings:** \"WARNING! SIGNAL TRUCK 'BIG EAR' APPROACHING!\" · \"WARNING! GUNBOAT 'CROCODILE' DEAD AHEAD!\" ·\n714\t  \"WARNING! HALF-TRACK 'WARTHOG' IN THE PLAZA!\" · \"WARNING! ARMORED TRAIN 'IRON HOG' INBOUND!\" · \"WARNING! THE WARDEN, MAJOR\n715\t  TUSK!\" · \"WARNING! GUNSHIP 'HYENA ONE'! KRAGG IS ABOARD!\"\n716\t- **Clears:** Op 1 \"RADIO HILL IS SILENT. THE HYENAS CANNOT CALL FOR HELP!\" · Op 2 \"THE RIVER IS OURS. AND WE CAUGHT ONE\n717\t  ALIVE.\" · Op 3 \"THE VILLAGE IS FREE! THE VILLAGE DOCTOR PATCHES YOU UP.\" · Op 4 \"WE TAKE WHAT WE CAN CARRY. THE REST GOES\n718\t  BOOM.\" · Op 5 \"{n} OF 5 HOSTAGES ARE FREE. KRAGG IS RUNNING FOR THE AIRFIELD!\"\n719\t- **Interrogation (after Op 2, a cutscene in a dim tent: LOBO holds GIGGS by the collar):** LOBO \"WHERE ARE THE\n720\t  HOSTAGES?\" · GIGGS \"HEE... HEE... I KNOW NOTHING!\" · LOBO \"WRONG ANSWER.\" (a shake, a thump) · GIGGS \"OKAY! OKAY! THE\n721\t  KENNEL! THE OLD PRISON ON THE CLIFFS!\" · GIGGS \"BUT THE ROAD GOES THROUGH PALM VILLAGE AND THE DEPOT. YOU WILL NEVER MAKE\n722\t  IT!\" · DEN \"WE WILL SEE ABOUT THAT. WOLFPACK, MOVE OUT.\"\n723\t- **Kragg's taunts (radio, his portrait):** \"HA HA HA HA! NOBODY LEAVES MY COAST!\" · \"RUN, LITTLE WOLVES! RUN!\" · \"MY\n724\t  HYENAS ARE HUNGRY!\" · on defeat: \"NOOO! MY BEAUTIFUL GUNSHIP!\"\n725\t- **Hostages:** freed, \"YOU CAME FOR US!\" · grabbed, \"HELP! THEY HAVE ME!\" · boarding, \"GO, GO, GO!\"\n726\t- **Endings** (`#ending/n`; each over the plane at sunrise, with the hostages' portraits lit or dark):\n727\t  - 5: \"ALL FIVE HOSTAGES ARE SAFE. THE COAST IS FREE.\" · \"THE PACK HOWLS AT THE RISING SUN.\" · \"CONGRATULATIONS! YOUR\n728\t    MISSION IS A PERFECT SUCCESS.\"\n729\t  - 3–4: \"{n} HOSTAGES ARE SAFE. NOT EVERYONE CAME HOME.\" · \"BUT KRAGG WILL NEVER HURT ANYONE AGAIN.\" · \"MISSION\n730\t    ACCOMPLISHED.\"\n731\t  - 1–2: \"ONLY {n} MADE IT. THE PACK WILL REMEMBER THE REST.\" · \"MISSION OVER.\"\n732\t  - 0: \"THE PLANE FLIES HOME WITH EMPTY SEATS.\" · \"THE HUNT IS NOT OVER.\" · \"MISSION FAILED.\"\n733\t  - Then the rank, \"THE HUNT CONTINUES...\" with the choices **LOOP 2** (keeps the score, harder) and **TITLE**, then the\n734\t    credits and initials.\n735\t\n736\t### 8.4 Bestiary: the Hyena Legion (VETERAN values)\n737\t\n738\t| Type | Rig | HP | Behaviors | Attack (telegraph → effect) | Score | Quota | First op |\n739\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n740\t| RIFLEMAN | Humanoid 1.3, cap, `gun` | 1 | cross, popup, window, door, advance, dismount, chase | 1.3 s ring → 1–3 bullets, accuracy .45, 4 each | 100 | soldier | 1 |\n741\t| GRENADIER | 1.3, helmet, no weapon (a grenade sprite at `rig.hand()`) | 2 | popup, roof, cross with stops | `throw` move (.6 s) → grenade | 150 | soldier | 1 |\n742\t| KNIFE | 1.25, bandana, a knife sprite at the hand | 1 | popup at depth 55–90, branches (Op 2), doorways | `throw` move (.45 s) → knife | 200 | soldier | 1 |\n743\t| BRUTE | 1.55 `bulky`, blond crew cut, helmet off, `gun` | 8 (head ×4) | popup behind sandbags, stand | 1.6 s ring → 5-round burst, accuracy .30, 4 each | 500 | soldier | 1 |\n744\t| RPG | 1.3, cap, a tube over the shoulder (custom pose) | 2 | kneel on cover, roof | 1.5 s ring → rocket | 300 | soldier | 4 |\n745\t| SNIPER | 1.3, cap, `gun` | 1 | snipe (tower, window, tree) | 2.4 s glint → 1 shot, accuracy .85, 10 | 400 | soldier | 1 |\n746\t| MORTAR | two 1.2s behind sandbags | 1 each | mortar | a launch every 6 s → mortar shell | 200 each | soldier | 1 |\n747\t| OFFICER | 1.35, peaked cap, coat | 2 | officer (whistle) | 2 s whistle → 3 riflemen | 600 + INTEL | soldier | 1 |\n748\t| PARATROOPER | 1.3, helmet, chute sprite | 1 (chute 1) | para → cross | as RIFLEMAN once landed | 150 (+100 airborne) | soldier | 1 |\n749\t\n750\t### 8.5 Vehicles, boats, aircraft\n751\t\n752\t| Type | Shape | HP | Movement | Attacks | Score | Quota |\n753\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n754\t| Jeep SCAVENGER | `jeep` + gunner rig | 14 (gunner 1) | crosses at 80 u/s, may stop | gunner: 1.2 s ring → 3 bullets | 1000 | vehicle |\n755\t| Truck HAULER | `truck` | 20 | drives in, stops, unloads 4 | none | 1200 | vehicle |\n756\t| APC BADGER | `apc` (turret separate) | 32 | crosses at 40, stops | 1.8 s turret glow → rocket; unloads 3 | 2000 | vehicle |\n757\t| Tank MAULER | `tank` (turret separate) | 48 | rolls out of a hangar, turret tracks the camera | 2.0 s barrel glow → tank shell | 3000 | vehicle |\n758\t| Skiff | `skiff` + 2 gunner rigs | 10 | river: from ahead, from side channels | gunners: 1.3 s rings | 800 | boat |\n759\t| Patrol boat | `gunboat` (small) | 26 | river | turret: 1.4 s ring → 4 bullets | 1500 | boat |\n760\t| Gunship VULTURE | `heli` + a rotor overlay | 34 | flies in from far at z 60–90, hovers, strafes, leaves when damaged (and returns) | 1.6 s ring → MG burst (6 × 3); missiles every 7 s | 3000 | air |\n761\t| Cargo plane | `cargoPlane` | n/a | scenery overhead (Op 4), drops paratroopers and crates | none | n/a | n/a |\n762\t\n763\t### 8.6 The six operations\n764\t\n765\tEvery op follows the same frame: the card (3 s, quotas shown with icons), \"GO!\", the beats, the boss, the tally. Each one\n766\tintroduces something new so that the whole game teaches itself. Beats are listed by rail distance `d`, and their ids are\n767\t`b1`, `b2`, … in table order (the `d 0` row is `b1`). \"×n\" means count, \"@D\" means depth, L/R means the edge spawned\n768\tfrom. Scenery positions are world x (along the rail) and depth. Fill every screen: 3–8 props near, a midground and a far\n769\tlayer. Keep each op's scripted soldiers at about its soldier quota ÷ .85 when you edit beats."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0704575-f16b-44ea-a24d-907e9c278025","uuid":"747449f9-c9a6-4f48-b276-be613ef643f4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:30:24.323Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183009__xe162c9/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 7.1 Rail camera (`11-rail.js`)\n\n- Rail knots become an `E.Path` (catmull). The camera's distance `d` advances at `speed × T.railSpeed` and eases to 0\n  over .6 s at a **hold** (and back up over .8 s after it). Holds wait for `until`: `beat:<id>` (that beat's enemies are\n  dead or gone), `vehicle`/`air`/`boat` (that quota's live units are gone), `escort` (the escort is resolved), `quota` (all\n  quotas met), or `boss` (the boss is dead). A hold with `max` lets go after that many seconds; a unit still alive then\n  leaves and comes back in the reinforcement loop (7.14).\n- Per-knot tweens: `angle` (yaw), `h`, `pitch`, `fov`. River bob: `h ± 1.2` and `pitch ± .5°` at .35 Hz. Walking sway on\n  land: `h ± .4` at the step rate (1.6 Hz), and no sway while held.\n- **Segment cuts** (Op 6's takeoff): `rail.cut(nextRail, { fade: 'wipe' })` swaps rails behind a .4 s transition.\n- Camera shake is the engine's `game.shake` (screen space), scaled by the standard shake setting.\n\n### 7.2 Projection and hit testing (`10-view3d.js`, `12-hit.js`)\n\n- At the start of every step: `view.begin(cam)`. Every hittable thing produces **hit shapes** in buffer pixels, each with\n  a depth (distance along the view direction).\n  - **Humanoids** (standing height `h` from the calibration table, 9.2): head is a circle at `z + .885h`, radius `.085h`;\n    body is a rectangle from `z + .45h` to `z + .80h`, half-width `.17h`; legs are a rectangle from `z` to `z + .45h`,\n    half-width `.12h`. Kneeling: heights × .72. Behind cover: anything below the cover's top `z` is removed. In a window or\n    door: everything is clipped to the opening's projected rectangle. Dying: no shapes. Minimum size: body 4×8 px, head\n    radius 2 px.\n  - **Vehicles, boats, aircraft:** the convex hull of the 8 projected corners of the hull box, plus each weak point as a\n    circle (a local offset turned by facing, radius in units, at least 4 px).\n  - **Projectiles and pickups:** circles, radius `r × k`, at least 5 px for projectiles and 6 px for pickups (fairness).\n  - **Cover and props:** a hull of the projected box. Cover stops bullets; props take damage.\n- **A shot** at point `p` (the crosshair plus bloom, 7.4) hits the **nearest** shape containing `p`. If that is cover, the\n  bullet stops there (sparks or dust). With no shape, the floor point `toFloor(p)` gets a dust puff, or nothing if `p` is\n  above the horizon.\n- **Explosions** query by world distance (3D) to every entity and prop, civilians and hostages included.\n- **Calibrate in M0:** draw each rig preset with the engine at view scale 1, in standing, kneeling and crouching poses, to\n  an offscreen canvas; measure the bounding box; and write `WP.RIG_H` from it. A dev toggle draws every hit shape over the\n  scene to check alignment (section 11).\n\n### 7.3 Crosshair and aiming (`30-players.js`)\n\n- **Mouse:** absolute. The crosshair equals the pointer, clamped to the playfield. Mouse play gets no aim assist.\n- **Stick:** velocity = `T.padSpeed` (520 px/s) × setting multiplier (.5–2) × `curve(|s|) = |s|^2.0`. After .3 s held\n  above .95 deflection, ×1.5 (turbo). Stick vector = left + .5 × right (`input.padMove`, `input.padAim`). The d-pad nudges\n  at 90 px/s.\n- **Keys:** 300 px/s, ramping to 520 over .4 s.\n- **Aim assist** for pads and keys (`assist` = Off 0 / Low .35 / Medium .6 / High .85; RECRUIT adds .15):\n  - *Friction:* inside a hostile's hit shapes grown by 6 px, crosshair speed × (1 − .55 × assist).\n  - *Magnetism:* while the stick is moving and a hostile's body center is within 28 px with direction dot > .3, pull\n    toward it at 160 × assist px/s.\n  - *Snap* (L1/Q): ease .08 s to the highest-priority threat (a projectile about to hit, then the telegraph closest to\n    firing, then the nearest hostile), preferring the stick's direction. .2 s cooldown.\n  - Never toward civilians, hostages or animals.\n- Co-op start positions: P1 at 42% of the width, P2 at 58%, P3 at 30%, P4 at 70%, all at 55% of the height.\n\n### 7.4 Weapon: the WOLF-9 SMG (`31-weapon.js`)\n\n- **Fire:** `T.fireRate` 11 rounds a second while fire is held. The first round fires on the press step; the rest follow\n  on a fixed interval, so the count is exact for the tests.\n- **Bloom:** offset radius `T.spreadBase` 1.5 px, +`T.bloomPerShot` .8 px a shot, up to `T.bloomMax` 7 px, recovering at\n  18 px/s. Each shot's offset comes from the `sim` stream (uniform in a disc).\n- **Damage:** `T.bulletDmg` 1 a hit; a head hit does ×2, and ×4 on BRUTES and TUSK.\n- **Magazines:** `mag` (rounds in the gun, `T.magSize` 30) and `spares`, a list of round counts (start 5 full spares, so 6\n  magazines; pouch limit `T.maxMags` 9, or 11 after Op 4's perk). **Reload** (`T.reloadTime` 1.0 s) loads the fullest\n  spare; a part-used magazine goes back into the pouch with its rounds (no waste, no merging). Auto-reload starts .12 s\n  after the gun runs dry. Manual reload works whenever `mag < magSize` and a spare exists. Firing on empty clicks.\n- **FURY** (pickup): `T.furySeconds` 10 s, fire rate ×2, damage ×1.5, no ammo used, golden tracers, a music sting, and a\n  ring timer around the crosshair.\n- **Accuracy stat:** shots that hit a hostile, projectile, pickup or prop ÷ shots fired.\n- **Tracers and impacts:** each round draws a 1-frame tracer from the gun's muzzle (the overlay, or the player's edge of\n  the screen in co-op) to the impact point, plus impact FX by material (dust, sparks on metal, splinters on wood, splashes\n  on water).\n\n### 7.5 Grenades and explosions\n\n- Start with `T.startGrenades` 4; pouch limit 9. On a press, the target is the entity under the crosshair (its 3D point,\n  so helicopters can be air-burst) if it is within `T.grenadeRange` 420 units. Otherwise it is the floor point under the\n  crosshair, clamped to range; above the horizon, the point at range along the view ray.\n- Flight time `.55 + .0015 × distance` s along an `E.arc` lob from the camera's lower front (`h − 6`). A small sprite\n  spins on the way, with a shadow dot on the floor. You can't throw another for .5 s.\n- **Blast:** radius `T.grenadeRadius` 52 units, damage `T.grenadeDmg` 12 at the center falling to 6 at the edge. Every\n  infantry type inside dies except BRUTES, which take the damage. Vehicles and weak points take the damage. Enemies within\n  1.5 × radius are stunned for 1 s. **Civilians and hostages inside are hurt** (penalties apply). Props in range take the\n  damage, which chains barrels and tanks. Supply animals in range drop their items and flee.\n- **Explosion feel:** a fireball, smoke, debris and a shock ring on the floor; `game.flash('#fff0c0', .08)`; `game.shake(3)`;\n  .04 s hit-stop (`game.freeze`); rumble; boom plus a low sine thump.\n- **DYNAMITE** (pickup, shot to trigger): a screen-wide blast. Every non-boss enemy in view dies; vehicles and bosses take\n  30; **civilians and hostages in view take a penalty hit each**. White flash, big shake.\n\n### 7.6 Enemy AI (`21-infantry.js`, `22-enemyfire.js`)\n\nEach infantry entity runs a small state machine: `enter` → `move` → `cover`/`stand` → `telegraph` → `attack` → `recover`,\nrepeated `cycles` times, then `exit` (runs off) or `advance`. Its reactions: `hurt` (a .25 s flinch that cancels a\ntelegraph; for HP > 1 types), `stun` (1 s, from nearby grenades), and `die` (the `die` pose; the body falls and fades after\n2.5 s). Speeds: walk 32, run 70, sprint 110 u/s.\n\n| Behavior | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `cross` | runs from one edge to the other at a depth; with `stops`, stops once or twice to fire |\n| `sprint` | a fast cross that never fires (quota fodder, and practice) |\n| `popup` | hides behind a cover prop and stands every 2–3 s to fire (`cycles` 2–4); between pops only the head shows |\n| `window` / `door` | the same inside a building opening, clipped to it (shutters open first: .3 s) |\n| `advance` | walks toward the camera to depth 70, then fires (or throws knives) from there |\n| `para` | parachutes from z 160 at 22 u/s. The chute (2 px+ circle above) and the body are both hittable; a shot chute drops him fast to his death. On landing he becomes `cross` |\n| `dismount` | leaves a truck, APC or boat and fans out (`cross` or `popup` on nearby cover) |\n| `chase` | follows a hostage; within 10 units for 1 s he grabs and drags the hostage back (7.11) |\n| `mortar` | a crew of two behind sandbags far away; launches every 6 s |\n| `snipe` | stationary at a tower, window or tree; a lens glint telegraph |\n| `officer` | blows a whistle for 2 s (an icon over his head); if he finishes, 3 riflemen arrive (2 after Op 1's perk). Kill him during the whistle to cancel it |\n\n**Enemy fire** (`22-enemyfire.js`):\n\n- When the telegraph starts, the enemy picks a target player: a random living one, from the `ai` stream. The ring is drawn\n  in that player's seat color, so in co-op everyone sees who is targeted. Ring radius 22 → 6 px over the telegraph time,\n  shifting yellow → orange → red, with a tick that rises in pitch.\n- When it closes, if the enemy is alive and not stunned, it fires `bullets` hitscan rounds .1 s apart. Each one hits with\n  chance `accuracy(type) × depthFactor × difficulty × T.enemyAccuracy × spotted` (`depthFactor`: 1 at depth ≤ 150, falling\n  linearly to .55 at 500 and beyond; `spotted` is 1.5 while a searchlight is on the camera). A hit adds `damage ×\n  T.enemyDamage` to the target. Hit or miss, the enemy shows a muzzle flash and a tracer to the screen's lower edge; a miss\n  makes a whiz.\n- Direction cue: every hit flashes a red arc on the screen edge toward the shooter (left, right or center).\n\n### 7.7 Projectiles (`23-projectiles.js`)\n\n| Kind | Thrown or fired by | Motion | Flight | Shootable | Damage | Intercept score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| grenade | GRENADIER, boss decks | an `E.arc` lob to a point 12 units in front of the camera (±20 sideways) | 1.3 s | yes, 1 hit, r 4 | 12 | 50 |\n| knife | KNIFE | straight and spinning (the sprite's `rot`) | .65 s | yes, 1 hit, r 3 | 8 | 100 |\n| rocket | RPG, APC, BIG EAR, IRON HOG | straight, ±2 u wobble, a smoke trail | 1.6 s | yes, 1 hit, r 4 | 16 | 150 |\n| missile | VULTURE, HYENA ONE | slight homing toward the camera | 1.8 s | yes, 1 hit, r 4 | 18 | 200 |\n| mortar shell | mortar crews, CROCODILE, IRON HOG | a high arc from far away, a falling whistle, a landing marker on the HUD's top edge | 2.6 s | yes, 1 hit, r 4 | 14 | 100 |\n| tank shell | MAULER, WARTHOG's cannon, HYENA ONE's nose cannon | fast and straight, a big glow | .8 s | yes, 2 hits, r 6 | 22 | 250 |\n| flame wave | WARTHOG | rolls along the ground toward the camera | 1.2 s | no (stop it at the source) | 15 | n/a |\n\nA projectile \"hits\" when its depth drops below 14. Shot down, it pops in the air (a small explosion, or sparks for a\nknife), scores, and counts as an intercept (a stat and an award).\n\n### 7.8 Vehicles and aircraft (`24-vehicles.js`)\n\nVehicles are shapes-as-data drawn by `m7.shape` (quantized to 16 facings), moving along paths, with overlays for moving\nparts (wheels, rotors, turrets as separate shapes with their own facing, dishes, propellers). Damage states: under 50%\nsmoking, under 25% burning, at 0 an explosion chain (3 blasts over .6 s, `explosion(..., { debris })`). The wreck (charred\nmaterials) stays as cover for 6 s, then fades (on water, it sinks). A vehicle with a gunner (a separate rig, HP 1) stops\nfiring when the gunner dies. Vehicles that leave the screen alive come back in the reinforcement loop.\n\n### 7.9 Bosses (`25-bosses.js`)\n\nThe boss framework is `{ phases: [{ weak: [...], attacks: [...], onEnd }], intro, defeat }`. The boss bar is the sum of\nthe current phase's weak points. Weak points that can be hurt blink at 3 Hz with a white outline; armored parts spark and\nshow \"ARMORED\" once. Intro: a klaxon, the card `WARNING!` + name (`E.Arcade.card`), a radio line, music to `boss`.\nDefeat: .5 s at `timeScale .3`, the explosion chain, a white flash, a victory sting, then the tally. Each boss is in 8.7.\n\n### 7.10 Player damage, DOWN, continue\n\n- `damage` runs 0–100; at 100 the player is **DOWN**. Solo: a death beat (camera h → 8 and pitch −10 over .8 s, a red\n  tint, a fade), then **CONTINUE?** (`E.Arcade.continue(10, done)`). Continuing restarts the current operation from its\n  start, with damage 0, the score kept, `continues + 1` (it affects the rank), and the ammo the player had when the op\n  began (at least 4 magazines and 3 grenades). Without a continue comes the GAME OVER card (\"THE HUNT IS OVER... FOR\n  NOW.\" and the score), then initials if the score qualifies, then the title. This is not the 0-hostage ending, which\n  only follows Op 6.\n- **Co-op:** a DOWN player's crosshair turns grey and their panel shows \"DOWN\". They come back at the next operation with\n  damage 50. All players DOWN brings up the continue screen for everyone.\n- **DRY rule** (mag 0, no spares, no grenades). On ARCADE it is the source's rule: DOWN. On VETERAN and RECRUIT an\n  **emergency drop** parachutes in within 4 s and delivers 2 full magazines to that player when it lands (score −2000,\n  \"RESUPPLY FEE\"), at most once every 30 s. RECRUIT also refills a 15-round magazine 3 s after going dry.\n- Healing: RATION −15, MEDKIT −35, stage clear −`clearHeal` (10; Op 3: 40).\n\n### 7.11 Civilians, hostages, animals (`26-friendlies.js`)\n\n- **Civilians** (villagers, medic pairs with a stretcher, a reporter) cross on paths and **panic** when shots land within\n  40 units: they run 1.5× faster with their hands over their heads. **A player hit** on a civilian adds `T.civilianDamage`\n  (8) to that player, costs 1000 points and the streak, and shows a big red \"CIVILIAN HIT!\". The civilian falls (wounded,\n  not killed), crawls off-screen and doesn't return. A civilian who crosses unharmed while enemies are on screen tosses a\n  small gift 10% of the time (\"THANK YOU!\": a RATION or MAG).\n- **Hostages** (Ops 5 and 6): each has HP 3 against enemy fire, shown as pips over its head. A player hit costs +10\n  damage, −2000 points and −1 hostage HP. Each hostage follows an escort path at 46 u/s. A `chase` enemy within 10 units\n  for 1 s **grabs** it and drags it back toward its spawn at 20 u/s; shoot him within 3 s and the hostage runs on, or it is\n  **lost**. At 0 HP it falls and is lost. Reaching the goal counts it rescued (+5000, a cheer, its portrait lit on the HUD).\n- **Supply animals** (never killed): goats, chickens, pigs, parrots, monkeys, seagulls, built with `E.Blob`. Any hit or\n  nearby blast makes one squawk, drop the item it carries (shown as a pack on its back or a bundle in its beak), and bolt.\n- **Friendly markers** (setting, on by default): a small green ▼ over a civilian or hostage while a crosshair is within 36\n  px of it.\n\n### 7.12 Destructibles and cover (`27-props.js`)\n\n| Prop | HP | Blocks shots | On destruction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| wooden crate | 3 | no | splinters; drop roll (60%) |\n| ammo crate (olive, stenciled) | 3 | no | drop from {MAG 50, AMMO CRATE 20, GRENADE 20, GRENADE BOX 10} |\n| red fuel barrel | 4 | no | explosion r 48, damage 10 (it chains) |\n| sandbag wall | 40 (grenade 15) | yes, below its top | chips through 3 visual stages; gone at 0 |\n| wreck | n/a | yes | fades after 6 s |\n| radio mast (Op 1) | 25 at its junction box | no | sparks, then topples over 1.2 s (shape tilt steps), dust |\n| fuel tank (Op 4) | 20 | yes | a big explosion r 90, damage 20, chains |\n| searchlight (Ops 5, 6) | 2 | no | glass pops; its beam goes out |\n| bridge rope (Op 2) | 6 each end | no | the bridge drops: every soldier on it falls (+300 each, \"BRIDGE OUT!\") |\n| ammo wagon (Op 4) | 4 | no | explosion r 70, damage 30 (hits the train car next to it) |\n| window shutters | 1 | no | swing open (snipers can't hide behind them) |\n\n### 7.13 Pickups and the supply director (`28-pickups.js`)\n\n| Pickup | Sprite | Effect | Where it comes from |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| MAG | olive magazine | +1 full spare (at the pouch limit: +300 points) | crates, animals, gifts, carriers |\n| AMMO CRATE | stenciled box | +3 full spares | ammo crates, supply parachutes |\n| GRENADE | pineapple | +1 grenade | crates, animals |\n| GRENADE BOX | box of 3 | +3 grenades | ammo crates, monkeys |\n| RATION | tin | damage −15 | crates, animals, gifts |\n| MEDKIT | white box, green cross | damage −35 | rare; more after Op 3's perk |\n| FURY | golden SMG | FURY mode for 10 s (7.4) | rare; scripted once per op |\n| DYNAMITE | bundle of red sticks | screen blast (7.5) | scripted, once per op from Op 3 |\n| FLARE | red flare | lights the night scene for 12 s and outlines snipers (Op 5) | Op 5 crates |\n| INTEL | folder | +1500 | officers, the reporter |\n| WOLF FANG | white fang | +500 | rare animal drop |\n\n- Dropped items pop up, bounce twice, hover with a glow, last 6 s (blinking for the final 1.5), and are collected by\n  shooting them once. In co-op, the player who shot it gets it.\n- **Supply director** (`loot` stream, deterministic): a crate's base drop chance is 60%, and carriers always drop.\n  Weights adjust to need: lowest player's total rounds (mag + spares × 30) under 60 → MAG ×3; grenades 0 → GRENADE ×2;\n  damage over 60 → RATION/MEDKIT ×2. At most one FURY per beat. Below 1 magazine and 0 grenades, a **supply parachute**\n  (AMMO CRATE) arrives mid-screen within 2 s, at most once every 20 s.\n\n### 7.14 Quotas, beats, reinforcements, clear, perks (`33-sim.js`)\n\n- Quotas count kills by class (`soldier`, `vehicle`, `air`, `boat`) and show as counters counting down. Masts (Op 1) are\n  an objective chip.\n- **The boss comes when the rail's end is reached and every quota is met.** When a quota is met early, its counter shows a\n  check and later spawns still score. When the rail ends with quota left, the **reinforcement loop** runs at the final\n  hold: every 3–5 s it spawns from a weighted list biased toward the missing classes (a jeep if vehicles are missing, a\n  VULTURE if air is) until the quotas are met, with a radio line: \"MORE OF THEM ARE COMING!\". Scripted spawns total about\n  quota ÷ .85, so a careful player needs few or no reinforcements.\n- Enemies that leave the screen (more than 60 px past the edge for 2 s) despawn as escaped, which doesn't count toward the\n  quota.\n- **Clear:** the tally (10.2 `tally`), then the perk card, then the heal, then the map.\n\n| Perk | From | Effect for the rest of the run |\n|---|---|---|\n| COMMS DOWN | Op 1 | quotas ×.8 in later ops; whistles call 2, not 3 |\n| CAMP LOCATED (intel) | Op 2 | the interrogation; snipers and mortars in later ops show a red marker for their first 1.5 s |\n| VILLAGE LIBERATED | Op 3 | damage −40 now; MEDKIT weight ×2 |\n| SUPPLIES SEIZED | Op 4 | spares and grenades refilled to the limits now; pouch limit +2 magazines (11) |\n| HOSTAGES FREED (n/5) | Op 5 | n hostages come to Op 6 |\n\n### 7.15 Scoring, streaks, ranks, high scores (`32-scoring.js`)\n\n- **Kills:** RIFLEMAN 100, GRENADIER 150, KNIFE 200, BRUTE 500, RPG 300, SNIPER 400, MORTAR 200 each, OFFICER 600,\n  PARATROOPER 150 (+100 while airborne). Jeep 1000, truck 1200, APC 2000, tank 3000, skiff 800, patrol boat 1500, VULTURE\n  3000. Bosses 10000 (Op 1) to 30000 (Op 6). Headshot +50%. Intercepts per 7.7.\n- **Streak:** +1 a kill; multiplier = 1 + ⌊streak ÷ 8⌋, at most ×4. Taking damage, or hitting a civilian or hostage,\n  resets it; so do 4 s without a kill. At ×4: \"PACK FURY!\" and a howl.\n- **Tally per op:** soldiers and vehicles, accuracy (accuracy% × 100 × op number), headshots × 200, intercepts × 100,\n  CIVILIANS SPARED +5000 (or −1000 for each hit), op bonus 10000 × op number, hostages × 5000 (Ops 5, 6). One line at a\n  time, big numbers.\n- **Ranks:** ALPHA WOLF (5 hostages, 0 continues, accuracy ≥ 55%), PACK LEADER (≥ 4 hostages), TIMBER WOLF (≥ 3), LONE\n  WOLF (1–2), WOLF PUP (0). Loop 2 and later put `BLACK MOON` before the rank.\n- **High scores:** `E.Arcade` (`id: 'wolfpack'`, mode `'campaign'`; Mission Select uses `'op1'` … `'op6'`), top ten with\n  initials on the letter wheel. In co-op, everyone who qualifies enters theirs in turn. Hub rounds save nothing (the hub\n  gives the game a throwaway storage anyway).\n\n### 7.16 Difficulty and co-op scaling (`01-tuning.js`)\n\n| | RECRUIT | VETERAN (default) | ARCADE |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Enemy accuracy | ×.6 | ×1 | ×1.25 |\n| Telegraph time | ×1.35 | ×1 | ×.85 |\n| Enemy damage | ×.7 | ×1 | ×1.2 |\n| Drop chances | ×1.4 | ×1 | ×.8 |\n| Quotas | ×.85 | ×1 | ×1.1 |\n| Aim assist | +.15 | ±0 | magnetism off |\n| DRY | refill after 3 s + emergency drop | emergency drop | DOWN (the source's rule) |\n\nCo-op with n players: quotas and spawn counts both × (1 + .3(n − 1)) (rounded, deterministic, so the quota-to-spawn\nratio stays about .85), and each player has their own damage, ammo, grenades and score. Loop 2 and later: ARCADE multipliers × 1.15 on top of the chosen level.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Content\n\n### 8.1 Setting and cast\n\n- **The Brimstone Coast:** a fictional tropical coast under a smoking volcano, Mount Brimstone. Jungle, mangrove rivers,\n  fishing villages, a munitions depot, an old cliff-top prison, an airfield. The time is unstated; the feel is 1987.\n- **General Hugo Kragg, \"the Hyena\":** a bulky mercenary general with a peaked cap, a greatcoat and gold trim. He laughs a\n  high hyena cackle and rides the gunship HYENA ONE.\n- **The Hyena Legion:** tan uniforms with brown spots (a custom `spots` pattern), red armbands with a grinning hyena\n  emblem (original art), caps, helmets and bandanas.\n- **The Wolfpack:** callsigns only. WOLF 1 **LOBO** (the leader; red headband, black hair, stubble), WOLF 2 **FANG**\n  (backward cap, crew cut), WOLF 3 **TUNDRA** (white ponytail, green beret), WOLF 4 **MOONSHINE** (yellow bandana). Solo,\n  you are LOBO.\n- **DEN MOTHER:** the handler on the radio (grey short hair, green beret, coat).\n- **MAJOR TUSK:** the warden of the Kennel (bulky, helmet, armor, a riot shield).\n- **PRIVATE GIGGS:** a nervous Hyena who giggles under interrogation.\n- **The five hostages** (relief convoy, each with its own clothes and colors, hands bound): DR. AMARA OKONJO (a doctor;\n  white coat), HAL BRODY (an engineer; glasses, rolled sleeves), LUCIA MARCH (a reporter; vest), \"SKIP\" TANAKA (a pilot;\n  flight jacket; aboard OLD HOWLER, he takes the co-pilot's seat in the ending), AMBASSADOR GRANT WHITFIELD (a torn suit).\n- **OLD HOWLER:** the Wolfpack's twin-prop cargo plane with a rear ramp.\n\n### 8.2 Writing style (like the source's)\n\nALL CAPS for cards, radio subtitles and HUD words. Short lines: 2–9 words, at most 2 lines per box. Plain military words\n(COPY, INBOUND, MOVE OUT). Exclamations for alerts. Now and then a little of the stiff, earnest 80s arcade-translation\nvoice (\"ENEMY AIR SUPPORT IS COMING!\", \"YOU ARE OUR LAST HOPE.\"), charming and never mocking. The villain is theatrical\nand laughs. Nothing graphic. Every line has a speaker, a gibberish voice and a subtitle (the text is the subtitle). Every\nstring lives in `WP.TEXT`.\n\n### 8.3 Story beats and key lines (these exact lines; add more in the same voice)\n\n- **Intro (`briefing`, skippable):** cards over a slow pan of the coast at night:\n  \"THE BRIMSTONE COAST.\" · \"GENERAL KRAGG AND HIS HYENA LEGION HAVE TAKEN IT.\" · \"FIVE RELIEF WORKERS ARE HIS PRISONERS.\" ·\n  \"NO ARMY WILL GO IN. SO THEY SENT THE PACK.\"\n  DEN: \"WOLFPACK, THIS IS DEN MOTHER. YOUR MISSION: RESCUE THE FIVE HOSTAGES.\" · DEN: \"AMMUNITION IS LIMITED. SHOOT\n  SUPPLY CRATES TO RESTOCK.\" · DEN: \"DO NOT SHOOT CIVILIANS. GOOD HUNTING.\" · LOBO: \"AWOOOO!\" (the howl).\n- **Op cards:** OP 1 RADIO HILL, \"DESTROY THE ENEMY RADIO STATION\" · OP 2 MANGROVE RUN, \"BREAK THROUGH THE RIVER PATROL\" ·\n  OP 3 PALM VILLAGE, \"FREE THE VILLAGE. SPARE THE PEOPLE.\" · OP 4 POWDER KEG DEPOT, \"TAKE THE SUPPLIES. BLOW THE REST.\" ·\n  OP 5 THE KENNEL, \"RESCUE THE HOSTAGES\" · OP 6 LAST FLIGHT OUT, \"GET THEM ON THE PLANE\".\n- **First-time tips** (radio, each once per save; see 8.6): \"SHOOT ITEMS TO COLLECT THEM!\" · \"GRENADE INCOMING! SHOOT IT\n  DOWN!\" · \"{reload} TO RELOAD. DON'T RUN DRY!\" · \"{grenade} THROWS A GRENADE.\" · \"KNIVES CAN BE SHOT OUT OF THE AIR!\" ·\n  \"STOP THAT WHISTLE!\" · \"BIG ONES GO DOWN FASTER WITH A HEADSHOT.\" · \"CIVILIANS! WATCH YOUR FIRE!\" ({reload} and {grenade}\n  are `input.label` values, filled in when spoken.)\n- **Boss warnings:** \"WARNING! SIGNAL TRUCK 'BIG EAR' APPROACHING!\" · \"WARNING! GUNBOAT 'CROCODILE' DEAD AHEAD!\" ·\n  \"WARNING! HALF-TRACK 'WARTHOG' IN THE PLAZA!\" · \"WARNING! ARMORED TRAIN 'IRON HOG' INBOUND!\" · \"WARNING! THE WARDEN, MAJOR\n  TUSK!\" · \"WARNING! GUNSHIP 'HYENA ONE'! KRAGG IS ABOARD!\"\n- **Clears:** Op 1 \"RADIO HILL IS SILENT. THE HYENAS CANNOT CALL FOR HELP!\" · Op 2 \"THE RIVER IS OURS. AND WE CAUGHT ONE\n  ALIVE.\" · Op 3 \"THE VILLAGE IS FREE! THE VILLAGE DOCTOR PATCHES YOU UP.\" · Op 4 \"WE TAKE WHAT WE CAN CARRY. THE REST GOES\n  BOOM.\" · Op 5 \"{n} OF 5 HOSTAGES ARE FREE. KRAGG IS RUNNING FOR THE AIRFIELD!\"\n- **Interrogation (after Op 2, a cutscene in a dim tent: LOBO holds GIGGS by the collar):** LOBO \"WHERE ARE THE\n  HOSTAGES?\" · GIGGS \"HEE... HEE... I KNOW NOTHING!\" · LOBO \"WRONG ANSWER.\" (a shake, a thump) · GIGGS \"OKAY! OKAY! THE\n  KENNEL! THE OLD PRISON ON THE CLIFFS!\" · GIGGS \"BUT THE ROAD GOES THROUGH PALM VILLAGE AND THE DEPOT. YOU WILL NEVER MAKE\n  IT!\" · DEN \"WE WILL SEE ABOUT THAT. WOLFPACK, MOVE OUT.\"\n- **Kragg's taunts (radio, his portrait):** \"HA HA HA HA! NOBODY LEAVES MY COAST!\" · \"RUN, LITTLE WOLVES! RUN!\" · \"MY\n  HYENAS ARE HUNGRY!\" · on defeat: \"NOOO! MY BEAUTIFUL GUNSHIP!\"\n- **Hostages:** freed, \"YOU CAME FOR US!\" · grabbed, \"HELP! THEY HAVE ME!\" · boarding, \"GO, GO, GO!\"\n- **Endings** (`#ending/n`; each over the plane at sunrise, with the hostages' portraits lit or dark):\n  - 5: \"ALL FIVE HOSTAGES ARE SAFE. THE COAST IS FREE.\" · \"THE PACK HOWLS AT THE RISING SUN.\" · \"CONGRATULATIONS! YOUR\n    MISSION IS A PERFECT SUCCESS.\"\n  - 3–4: \"{n} HOSTAGES ARE SAFE. NOT EVERYONE CAME HOME.\" · \"BUT KRAGG WILL NEVER HURT ANYONE AGAIN.\" · \"MISSION\n    ACCOMPLISHED.\"\n  - 1–2: \"ONLY {n} MADE IT. THE PACK WILL REMEMBER THE REST.\" · \"MISSION OVER.\"\n  - 0: \"THE PLANE FLIES HOME WITH EMPTY SEATS.\" · \"THE HUNT IS NOT OVER.\" · \"MISSION FAILED.\"\n  - Then the rank, \"THE HUNT CONTINUES...\" with the choices **LOOP 2** (keeps the score, harder) and **TITLE**, then the\n    credits and initials.\n\n### 8.4 Bestiary: the Hyena Legion (VETERAN values)\n\n| Type | Rig | HP | Behaviors | Attack (telegraph → effect) | Score | Quota | First op |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| RIFLEMAN | Humanoid 1.3, cap, `gun` | 1 | cross, popup, window, door, advance, dismount, chase | 1.3 s ring → 1–3 bullets, accuracy .45, 4 each | 100 | soldier | 1 |\n| GRENADIER | 1.3, helmet, no weapon (a grenade sprite at `rig.hand()`) | 2 | popup, roof, cross with stops | `throw` move (.6 s) → grenade | 150 | soldier | 1 |\n| KNIFE | 1.25, bandana, a knife sprite at the hand | 1 | popup at depth 55–90, branches (Op 2), doorways | `throw` move (.45 s) → knife | 200 | soldier | 1 |\n| BRUTE | 1.55 `bulky`, blond crew cut, helmet off, `gun` | 8 (head ×4) | popup behind sandbags, stand | 1.6 s ring → 5-round burst, accuracy .30, 4 each | 500 | soldier | 1 |\n| RPG | 1.3, cap, a tube over the shoulder (custom pose) | 2 | kneel on cover, roof | 1.5 s ring → rocket | 300 | soldier | 4 |\n| SNIPER | 1.3, cap, `gun` | 1 | snipe (tower, window, tree) | 2.4 s glint → 1 shot, accuracy .85, 10 | 400 | soldier | 1 |\n| MORTAR | two 1.2s behind sandbags | 1 each | mortar | a launch every 6 s → mortar shell | 200 each | soldier | 1 |\n| OFFICER | 1.35, peaked cap, coat | 2 | officer (whistle) | 2 s whistle → 3 riflemen | 600 + INTEL | soldier | 1 |\n| PARATROOPER | 1.3, helmet, chute sprite | 1 (chute 1) | para → cross | as RIFLEMAN once landed | 150 (+100 airborne) | soldier | 1 |\n\n### 8.5 Vehicles, boats, aircraft\n\n| Type | Shape | HP | Movement | Attacks | Score | Quota |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Jeep SCAVENGER | `jeep` + gunner rig | 14 (gunner 1) | crosses at 80 u/s, may stop | gunner: 1.2 s ring → 3 bullets | 1000 | vehicle |\n| Truck HAULER | `truck` | 20 | drives in, stops, unloads 4 | none | 1200 | vehicle |\n| APC BADGER | `apc` (turret separate) | 32 | crosses at 40, stops | 1.8 s turret glow → rocket; unloads 3 | 2000 | vehicle |\n| Tank MAULER | `tank` (turret separate) | 48 | rolls out of a hangar, turret tracks the camera | 2.0 s barrel glow → tank shell | 3000 | vehicle |\n| Skiff | `skiff` + 2 gunner rigs | 10 | river: from ahead, from side channels | gunners: 1.3 s rings | 800 | boat |\n| Patrol boat | `gunboat` (small) | 26 | river | turret: 1.4 s ring → 4 bullets | 1500 | boat |\n| Gunship VULTURE | `heli` + a rotor overlay | 34 | flies in from far at z 60–90, hovers, strafes, leaves when damaged (and returns) | 1.6 s ring → MG burst (6 × 3); missiles every 7 s | 3000 | air |\n| Cargo plane | `cargoPlane` | n/a | scenery overhead (Op 4), drops paratroopers and crates | none | n/a | n/a |\n\n### 8.6 The six operations\n\nEvery op follows the same frame: the card (3 s, quotas shown with icons), \"GO!\", the beats, the boss, the tally. Each one\nintroduces something new so that the whole game teaches itself. Beats are listed by rail distance `d`, and their ids are\n`b1`, `b2`, … in table order (the `d 0` row is `b1`). \"×n\" means count, \"@D\" means depth, L/R means the edge spawned\nfrom. Scenery positions are world x (along the rail) and depth. Fill every screen: 3–8 props near, a midground and a far\nlayer. Keep each op's scripted soldiers at about its soldier quota ÷ .85 when you edit beats.","numLines":370,"startLine":400,"totalLines":1519}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TemB7bG96Hg4ZXXmBNnCEy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
