{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UdPnCQSVW9FobvbjrAz4pi","type":"tool_result","content":"770\t\n771\t#### OP 1: RADIO HILL (dawn; teaches everything)\n772\t- **Look:** a pink and orange dawn; dry hill grass with a dirt road band (depth 70–110) and rocks; a sea and mountains on\n773\t  the horizon. Floor painter `hill` (E.tex.grass and E.tex.dirt by noise; the road's ruts). Music `op1` (D minor, 140 bpm).\n774\t- **Rail:** sideways from x 0 to 2700 at 16 u/s; cam h 28, pitch 6. Holds at 520 (jeep), 1720 (air), 2700 (boss).\n775\t- **Scenery:** sandbag lines (depth 90–130); barbed wire posts; tents (x 300–700 @260); ammo crates; a wrecked jeep (x 1000\n776\t  @150, cover); **three radio masts** (x 900 @380, x 1500 @420, x 2150 @360: lattices 130 tall with blinking red lights);\n777\t  the radar building with its dish (x 2550 @420); goats (supply carriers) at x 200 and 1200; seagulls; palms and rocks far\n778\t  away.\n779\t- **Quotas:** soldier 36, vehicle 3, air 1; objective MASTS 3 (scripted: 43 soldiers, 3 vehicles, 1 aircraft). **Boss:**\n780\t  BIG EAR. **Perk:** COMMS DOWN.\n781\t\n782\t| d | Spawns | Notes |\n783\t|---|---|---|\n784\t| 0 | none | card; DEN \"OPERATION WOLFPACK IS GO. GOOD HUNTING.\"; tip chip \"AIM · {fire} FIRE\" |\n785\t| 40 | RIFLEMAN ×3 R @200, cross, gap .8 s | they fire late; the first kills |\n786\t| 160 | RIFLEMAN ×2 popup (sandbags sbA @110); goat carrying a MAG @130 | tip \"SHOOT ITEMS TO COLLECT THEM!\" on the goat's drop |\n787\t| 300 | GRENADIER ×1 @160; RIFLEMAN ×2 L @240 cross | tip \"GRENADE INCOMING! SHOOT IT DOWN!\" |\n788\t| 420 | crates ×3 @120 (MAG, GRENADE, RATION) | tip \"{reload} TO RELOAD\" when below 10 rounds |\n789\t| 520 | jeep R @250 with gunner; **hold** ≤ 15 s | tip \"{grenade} THROWS A GRENADE.\" |\n790\t| 680 | KNIFE ×1 popup @65 (rock); RIFLEMAN ×2 sprint @300 | tip \"KNIVES CAN BE SHOT OUT OF THE AIR!\" |\n791\t| 820 | mast 1 in view; SNIPER on its platform (z 90); RIFLEMAN ×3 popup by the tents | objective chip MASTS 0/3 |\n792\t| 1000 | truck stops @300 → RIFLEMAN ×4 dismount | |\n793\t| 1180 | OFFICER @180 (whistle); RIFLEMAN ×2 | tip \"STOP THAT WHISTLE!\" |\n794\t| 1350 | mast 2; MORTAR crew @620 behind sandbags | landing markers |\n795\t| 1500 | RIFLEMAN ×4, both edges @150–260; red barrels ×2 beside them | the first barrel chain |\n796\t| 1720 | VULTURE from far (z 70); **hold** until air or 30 s | |\n797\t| 1900 | BRUTE behind sandbags @170; GRENADIER ×2 @200 | tip \"BIG ONES GO DOWN FASTER WITH A HEADSHOT.\" |\n798\t| 2080 | mast 3; PARATROOPER ×4 (from the VULTURE if alive, else a cargo plane) | |\n799\t| 2250 | jeep @220; RIFLEMAN ×3; a crate holding FURY @140 | FURY's first showing |\n800\t| 2450 | KNIFE ×2 popup @70; RIFLEMAN ×3 | |\n801\t| 2700 | **hold**: reinforcements until the quotas are met, then BIG EAR | |\n802\t\n803\t#### OP 2: MANGROVE RUN (misty morning; forward rail on a river)\n804\t- **Look:** green mist, a brown-green river with moving ripples (the floor painter reads `WP.time`), muddy banks with\n805\t  roots, dense mangroves and palms, ferns. Fog near 200, far 1100. Music `op2` (E minor, 132 bpm, toms).\n806\t- **Rail:** forward (north) from y 0 to −3000 at 20 u/s; cam h 20, pitch 4, river bob. Holds at 1000 (air; the boat slows\n807\t  to 8 u/s, not a stop) and 2600 (boss, on a sandbar).\n808\t- **Scenery:** the river 220 wide (|x| < 110); stilt huts and docks on the banks; wrecked boats; side channels at d 700\n809\t  (right) and d 2100 (left); a **rope bridge** at d 1300 (y −1500, z 40, ropes hittable); a waterfall far away at the end;\n810\t  parrots and monkeys (carriers) in the trees.\n811\t- **Quotas:** soldier 28, boat 6, air 1 (scripted: 33 soldiers, 6 boats, 1 aircraft). **Boss:** CROCODILE. **Perk:** CAMP\n812\t  LOCATED (and the interrogation).\n813\t\n814\t| d | Spawns | Notes |\n815\t|---|---|---|\n816\t| 0 | none | DEN \"STAY LOW. THE RIVER IS CRAWLING WITH THEM.\" |\n817\t| 60 | RIFLEMAN ×3 popup in the bank roots @200–260, lx ±120 | |\n818\t| 200 | skiff from ahead @400 with 2 gunners, passing on the left | the first boat |\n819\t| 380 | KNIFE ×2 dropping from branches @70, lx ±60 | close threats |\n820\t| 520 | monkey carrying a GRENADE BOX in a tree; RIFLEMAN ×3 on a dock @250 | |\n821\t| 700 | skiff ×2 out of the right side channel @300, crossing | |\n822\t| 860 | GRENADIER ×2 on stilt huts @220; crates on the dock | |\n823\t| 1000 | VULTURE ahead (z 60) drops PARATROOPER ×3 onto the banks; the boat slows | |\n824\t| 1250 | the bridge: RIFLEMAN ×5 on it (z 40) @250 | shoot a rope: \"BRIDGE OUT!\" |\n825\t| 1500 | patrol boat @350; MORTAR bunker on the bank @700 | |\n826\t| 1700 | parrot flock (one carries FURY); RIFLEMAN ×4 on the banks | |\n827\t| 1900 | skiff; BRUTE and RIFLEMAN ×2 on a barge @300 | |\n828\t| 2100 | left channel: RIFLEMAN ×3; SNIPER in a tree @500 | |\n829\t| 2350 | KNIFE ×2 @70; red barrels on a floating dock; a skiff from ahead | the sixth boat |\n830\t| 2600 | **hold**: reinforcements, then CROCODILE from ahead | |\n831\t\n832\t#### OP 3: PALM VILLAGE (noon; civilians and windows)\n833\t- **Look:** bright noon; sand street with cobble patches, whitewashed houses with terracotta roofs, thatched stilt huts,\n834\t  market stalls with awnings, laundry lines, a well, palms, a teal sea with fishing boats behind. Music `op3` (G minor, 150\n835\t  bpm, syncopated).\n836\t- **Rail:** sideways 0 → 3000 at 15 u/s. Holds at 1600 (APC) and 2600 (the plaza, boss).\n837\t- **Scenery:** house fronts with **window and door openings** (enemy pop-ups clipped to them); a chapel with a bell tower\n838\t  (x 1800 @450, snipers); the plaza with a fountain (x 2600–3000); carts, crates, barrels; chickens and pigs (carriers).\n839\t  Civilians: about 20 villager crossings, two medic pairs with stretchers, one reporter.\n840\t- **Quotas:** soldier 38, vehicle 4 (scripted: 45 soldiers, 4 vehicles). **Boss:** WARTHOG. **Perk:** VILLAGE LIBERATED\n841\t  (damage −40).\n842\t\n843\t| d | Spawns | Notes |\n844\t|---|---|---|\n845\t| 0 | none | DEN \"THE VILLAGERS ARE STILL INSIDE. WATCH YOUR FIRE!\" |\n846\t| 50 | villagers ×2 fleeing @140; RIFLEMAN ×3 window pop-ups @200 | tip \"CIVILIANS! WATCH YOUR FIRE!\" |\n847\t| 200 | chickens ×3 (MAG, RATION, none); RIFLEMAN ×2 cross | |\n848\t| 350 | jeep @230; a civilian crossing in front of it @120 | a line-of-fire test |\n849\t| 500 | GRENADIER ×2 on roofs (z 30) @240; medic pair crossing @110 | |\n850\t| 680 | OFFICER and RIFLEMAN ×4 popping up behind the market stalls | |\n851\t| 850 | pig carrying a GRENADE BOX; KNIFE ×2 from doorways @80 | |\n852\t| 1000 | truck → dismount ×4; villagers ×3 run | |\n853\t| 1200 | BRUTE in the street @160; the reporter crosses | spare him: \"THE PRESS THANKS YOU!\" + INTEL |\n854\t| 1400 | RIFLEMAN ×5 crossing both ways, with civilians ×2 mixed in | tension |\n855\t| 1600 | APC @300 (rockets) → dismount ×3; **hold** ≤ 30 s | |\n856\t| 1800 | SNIPER ×2 in the bell tower (z 60) @450; RIFLEMAN ×3 | |\n857\t| 2000 | jeep; PARATROOPER ×3 | |\n858\t| 2200 | a crate holding DYNAMITE, civilians far off; RIFLEMAN ×6 | tip \"DYNAMITE HITS EVERYONE ON SCREEN!\" |\n859\t| 2400 | KNIFE ×2; GRENADIER ×2; villagers ×2 | |\n860\t| 2600 | **hold** (plaza): reinforcements, then WARTHOG | |\n861\t\n862\t#### OP 4: POWDER KEG DEPOT (dusk; explosions)\n863\t- **Look:** a purple and orange dusk; concrete and dirt; stacked ammo crates, big red fuel tanks, metal sheds, cranes,\n864\t  floodlights coming on, a water tower, embers in the air. Music `op4` (C minor, 146 bpm, industrial noise hits).\n865\t- **Rail:** sideways 0 → 3000 at 16 u/s. Holds at 950 and 2000 (air) and 2700 (boss).\n866\t- **Scenery:** **railway tracks** at depth 260 along the whole rail (the boss arena), flatcars, three ammo wagons on a\n867\t  siding (x 2500–2900 @250), the water tower (x 1600 @400), a warehouse with doors (x 2400 @300), barbed wire, a cargo\n868\t  plane overhead at d 560.\n869\t- **Quotas:** soldier 37, vehicle 3, air 2 (scripted: 43 soldiers, 3 vehicles, 2 aircraft). **Boss:** IRON HOG.\n870\t  **Perk:** SUPPLIES SEIZED.\n871\t\n872\t| d | Spawns | Notes |\n873\t|---|---|---|\n874\t| 0 | none | DEN \"THIS PLACE IS A POWDER KEG. LIGHT IT UP!\" |\n875\t| 60 | RIFLEMAN ×4 cross @220 beside fuel tank A | shoot the tank: a chain |\n876\t| 220 | RPG ×2 kneeling on crates @200 | the first RPG troopers |\n877\t| 400 | jeep @240; MORTAR crew @650 | |\n878\t| 560 | the cargo plane drops PARATROOPER ×5 and a supply chute (AMMO CRATE) | |\n879\t| 760 | BRUTE and RIFLEMAN ×3 behind sandbags @150 | |\n880\t| 950 | VULTURE #1; **hold** ≤ 25 s | |\n881\t| 1150 | a forklift carrying a GRENADE BOX crate crosses @160; RIFLEMAN ×3 | |\n882\t| 1350 | APC @300 → dismount ×3 | |\n883\t| 1600 | SNIPER on the water tower (z 70); RIFLEMAN ×4 | |\n884\t| 1800 | a row of 3 fuel tanks with RIFLEMAN ×6 beside them | \"CHAIN!\" bonus +1000 for 4+ kills in one blast |\n885\t| 2000 | VULTURE #2; RPG ×2; **hold** ≤ 25 s | |\n886\t| 2200 | KNIFE ×2; OFFICER | |\n887\t| 2400 | jeep; RIFLEMAN ×4 from the warehouse doors | |\n888\t| 2700 | **hold**: reinforcements, then IRON HOG on the tracks | |\n889\t\n890\t#### OP 5: THE KENNEL (night and rain; the breakout)\n891\t- **Look:** a black-blue night, rain, mud with puddle glints, a double barbed-wire fence (depth 80 and 100), wooden\n892\t  barracks, four watchtowers with **sweeping searchlights**, fire barrels, floodlights, the cage block (\"the kennel\"), a\n893\t  flagpole with the hyena flag. Darkness .75 (10.1 `53-fx`). Music `op5` (F# minor, 120 bpm, sparse, a heartbeat kick)\n894\t  under rain.\n895\t- **Rail:** sideways 0 → 2800 at 14 u/s; a yaw pan from −90° to −75° over d 1500–1700 to look into the yard. Holds at 1450\n896\t  (escort, ≤ 70 s) and 2500 (boss).\n897\t- **Searchlights:** each sweeps an ellipse on the ground (radius 40) along a path. When a beam crosses the camera's\n898\t  position (depth < 30), **SPOTTED** for 3 s (enemy accuracy ×1.5, a white flash, an alarm chirp). Shoot the light (HP 2)\n899\t  to put it out.\n900\t- **Quotas:** soldier 35, vehicle 3 (scripted: 41 soldiers including the 10 chasers, 2 jeeps and the truck).\n901\t  **Hostages:** escort as many as you can (they count toward the ending, not toward clearing the op). **Boss:** MAJOR\n902\t  TUSK. **Perk:** HOSTAGES FREED.\n903\t\n904\t| d | Spawns | Notes |\n905\t|---|---|---|\n906\t| 0 | none | card; LOBO \"THE KENNEL. FIVE HOSTAGES. ZERO MISTAKES.\" |\n907\t| 60 | RIFLEMAN ×3 patrol, cross @160 with flashlights; tower 1 searchlight | |\n908\t| 250 | a crate holding a FLARE @120; RIFLEMAN ×3 | tip \"SHOOT THE FLARE TO LIGHT THE YARD!\" |\n909\t| 420 | jeep with a searchlight @220 | |\n910\t| 600 | SNIPER in tower 1's cabin (z 70); GRENADIER ×2 | |\n911\t| 800 | RIFLEMAN ×4; KNIFE ×2 through a gap in the fence @70 | |\n912\t| 1000 | tower 2's searchlight; BRUTE | |\n913\t| 1200 | the gate opens: truck → dismount ×4 | |\n914\t| 1450 | **BREAKOUT** (**hold**, escort): the cells open one by one, 8 s apart. Each hostage runs from lx +180 to the breach at lx −200 @140–180, chased by 2 `chase` riflemen; tower MGs fire | the hostage pips and portraits on the HUD |\n915\t| 1750 | RIFLEMAN ×4 out of the barracks doors | |\n916\t| 1950 | tower 3; jeep | |\n917\t| 2200 | RIFLEMAN ×5; GRENADIER ×2 | |\n918\t| 2500 | **hold**: reinforcements, then MAJOR TUSK (the central tower, x 2700) | |\n919\t\n920\t#### OP 6: LAST FLIGHT OUT (sunrise storm; boarding, takeoff, the gunship)\n921\t- **Look:** a dark grey sunrise under storm clouds, wind; the apron with painted lines, hangars, a control tower, fuel\n922\t  trucks, a windsock, runway lights. Then the air: Mode 7 at altitude over jungle, coast and sea (Pilotwings-like). Music\n923\t  `op6` (A minor, 156 bpm, lifting into C major at takeoff).\n924\t- **Part A rail:** sideways 0 → 2000 at 18 u/s. Holds at 450 (air), 850 (tank ≤ 40 s), 1500 (escort), 2000 (quota).\n925\t- **Scenery A:** hangars ×3 (x 200, 900, 1600 @320; the tank comes out of hangar 2), the control tower (x 1200 @500;\n926\t  snipers), fuel trucks (explode like barrels), parked prop planes, a radar dish, crates, barrels; OLD HOWLER at x 2050\n927\t  @180 with its ramp down.\n928\t- **Part B rail (takeoff):** cut to the plane's open ramp, looking **back** (south, `angle = +π/2`) while the plane runs\n929\t  north along the runway; speed 30 → 90 over 20 s, liftoff at 20 s, climbing h 28 → 260 and pitch 6 → 28 by 35 s.\n930\t- **Quotas (part A):** soldier 27, vehicle 4, air 2 (scripted: 32 soldiers including the 10 escort attackers, 4\n931\t  vehicles, 2 aircraft). **Boss:** HYENA ONE (part B). **Hostages:** the n freed in Op 5 (5 when the op is played alone).\n932\t\n933\t| d / t | Spawns | Notes |\n934\t|---|---|---|\n935\t| 0 | none | DEN \"OLD HOWLER IS ON THE RUNWAY. GET THEM ABOARD!\" |\n936\t| 60 | RIFLEMAN ×4 popping out of hangar doors @320 | |\n937\t| 250 | jeep ×2 cross @200 | |\n938\t| 450 | VULTURE #1; **hold** ≤ 25 s | |\n939\t| 650 | RPG ×2 on fuel trucks | the trucks explode like barrels |\n940\t| 850 | MAULER rolls out of hangar 2 @320; **hold** ≤ 40 s | the tank |\n941\t| 1100 | PARATROOPER ×5; SNIPER ×2 in the control tower (z 80) | |\n942\t| 1300 | APC @280 → dismount | |\n943\t| 1500 | **ESCORT** (**hold**): a friendly truck drops off the n hostages, who run to the ramp (x 1500 → 2050 @140–200, about 25 s). Always 10 attackers: 2 chasers per hostage, the rest firing from the hangar doors. VULTURE #2 strafes | with 0 hostages, the hold lasts 15 s |\n944\t| 1900 | RIFLEMAN ×4; KNIFE ×2 | the last push |\n945\t| 2000 | **hold** for the quotas; then the cut \"EVERYBODY ON THE PLANE!\" → part B | |\n946\t| B t 0 | jeep ×3 chasing on the runway (`anchor: 'cam'`, depth 60–160), each with a gunner | bonus vehicles, not quota |\n947\t| B t 10 | a SAM truck at the runway's end fires 3 missiles | shoot them down |\n948\t| B t 20 | liftoff; DEN \"HANG ON!\" | |\n949\t| B t 30 | HYENA ONE climbs into view behind the plane → boss | |\n950\t\n951\t### 8.7 Bosses\n952\t\n953\t| Boss | Arena | Phases and weak points (HP) | Attacks | Score |\n954\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n955\t| **BIG EAR** (Op 1): a six-wheel signal truck | drives in from the right @260, parks, shuffles ±120 every 8 s | 1: radar dish (30, rotating), gunners L and R (1 each, each respawns twice after 6 s), rocket pod (15). 2: once the dish is gone, the cab and engine (60) stop being armored | dish up: 2 PARATROOPERS every 12 s; gunners' rings; 2 rockets every 6 s | 10000 |\n956\t| **CROCODILE** (Op 2): a gunboat | ahead, backing up at the camera's speed @160–240, weaving ±80 | front turret (20), rear turret (20), deck mortar (15) → bridge (45) | turret rings (4-round bursts); mortar arcs; 2 skiffs at 50% | 14000 |\n957\t| **WARTHOG** (Op 3): a flamethrower half-track | the plaza @200, moving ±100 | cannon (25), fuel tanks L and R (12 each), SGT. SNARL in the hatch (head 2: each hit stuns the vehicle 2 s) → hull (50) | cannon: 2.0 s glow → tank shell. Flamethrower (while a tank holds out): the nozzle glows 1.5 s, then a flame wave (shoot that side's tank during the glow to stop it). Civilians cross the far side 3 times | 18000 |\n958\t| **IRON HOG** (Op 4): an armored train | the tracks @260, back and forth over 900 units at 45 u/s | MG car (20), rocket car (25), mortar car (20) → boiler (50; its vents glow) | rings; rocket salvos (3); mortar arcs; vent steam (1.5 s glow → 10 damage, unless the boiler takes 10 in the glow). Ammo wagons on the siding deal 30 to the car beside them | 22000 |\n959\t| **MAJOR TUSK** (Op 5): the warden | 1: the central tower @300, cabin at z 80. 2: on foot | 1: tower MG (15), searchlights ×2 (2 each), support legs ×3 (15 each) → the tower falls. 2: TUSK (40; head ×3; a riot shield blocks the body) | 1: MG bursts, SPOTTED. 2: he walks from depth 250 to 90; lowers the shield 1.0 s → shotgun (3 pellets × 6); a grenade knocks the shield aside for 3 s; below depth 90 he charges, and reaching depth 60 hits for 20 and knocks him back to 150 | 26000 |\n960\t| **HYENA ONE** (Op 6): KRAGG's gunship | in the air behind the plane (`anchor: 'cam'`), depth 140–220 | 1: rocket pods L and R (25 each), door gunner (3; respawns). 2: nose cannon (30). 3: KRAGG leaning out with a launcher (head 3: each hit staggers 2 s) and the rotor hub (60) | 1: salvos of 3 rockets every 5 s; door gunner rings. 2: 2.0 s glow → tank shell (2 hits to shoot down). 3: homing missiles; his taunts. Defeat: it spirals into the sea below | 30000 |\n961\t\n962\t### 8.8 Cutscenes (`47-cutscenes.js`)\n963\t\n964\tScripts (`game.script` generators) drive rigs, camera moves, `E.Dialog` (modal, with portraits) and sound. Hold\n965\t✕/Enter/click for 1 s to skip, with a ring that fills. Every cutscene works headless (the tests run them at speed).\n966\t\n967\t1. **Briefing** (40 s): a night coast pan in Mode 7 (the coastline floor, the volcano glow in the Backdrop), cards, DEN's\n968\t   lines, the howl.\n969\t2. **Interrogation** (30 s): a dim tent drawn with px (canvas walls, a hanging lamp swinging, its light), LOBO and GIGGS\n970\t   (rigs), the lines in 8.3, a shake on \"WRONG ANSWER.\"\n971\t3. **Kennel aftermath** (12 s): the freed hostages kneel (`pose: 'kneel'`) as their portraits slide in, lit or dark; \"{n}\n972\t   OF 5 HOSTAGES ARE FREE.\"\n973\t4. **Takeoff cut** (1.5 s): a wipe \"EVERYBODY ON THE PLANE!\"\n974\t5. **Endings** (25 s): OLD HOWLER over the sea at sunrise (Mode 7 at altitude, the plane drawn as a shape from behind),\n975\t   the text of 8.3, the rank, the Wolfpack's howl.\n976\t6. **Credits:** scrolling text over the night coast (the About content, 14.2).\n977\t\n978\t---\n979\t\n980\t## 9. Presentation: art assets, animation, audio\n981\t\n982\t### 9.1 Art direction and assets\n983\t\n984\tThe engine's native style is the base: PS1/SNES-era pixel art, shaded HD Humanoid rigs, shapes-as-data with the house\n985\tshading and outline, `E.tones` ramps, the 5×7 font, `E.font.title` logos. Aim for the look list in `API.md` (backdrop,\n986\ttextured floors, 3–8 props a screen, dressed characters, effects on every hit, lighting, title font). Compare screenshots\n987\twith Metal Slug, not with NES games.\n988\t\n989\t**New shapes** (`50-art-shapes.js`, written to the `docs/ASSETS.md` format, facing south, in units of 16 = 1 m; check each\n990\twith `node engine/tools/asset-sheet.mjs src/50-art-shapes.js#<id>`):\n991\t\n992\t| Group | Shapes |\n993\t|---|---|\n994\t| Field props | `sandbags` (a row of flattened `ball` sacks, burlap, `len` param), `sandbagNest` (a ring), `redBarrel` (a lathe with bands), `ammoCrate` (olive with stencil lines), `medCrate`, `fuelTank` (a horizontal cylinder on legs), `barbedFence` (posts; wire drawn as lines by the renderer), `tent` (a linen prism), `campfireDrum`, `floodlight`, `searchlight` (a cylinder head on a pivot), `windsock`, `runwayLight`, `forklift` |\n995\t| Structures | `radioMast` (a lattice: thin boxes in `row`s with braces, a platform, a red light; `tilt` param for toppling), `radarDish` (a lathe dish; spun by facing), `radarHut`, `stiltHut` (thatch), `villageHouse` (plaster with tile roof; window and door openings as data for the clip system), `marketStall` (an awning wedge), `chapelTower`, `dock`, `ropeBridge`, `barracks`, `watchtower` (4 legs, a cabin, a roof), `cageBlock`, `gate`, `hangar` (an arched roof), `controlTower`, `waterTower`, `crane`, `shed` |\n996\t| Plants and rocks | `palm` (a leaning trunk of `cyl` segments, frond prisms), `mangrove` (a tree on root cylinders), `fern`, plus the core `tree`, `bush`, `rock`, `grass`, `pine` |\n997\t| Vehicles | `jeep`, `truck`, `halftrack` (WARTHOG), `apc` + `apcTurret`, `tank` + `tankTurret`, `skiff`, `gunboat` (small, and CROCODILE big with turrets and a bridge), `heli` (fuselage, tail boom, skids, pods; the rotor is an overlay), `hyenaOne` (bigger, a nose cannon, pods, an open door), `bigEar` (a 6×6 with a dish mount), `locomotive`, `trainCar` (×3 variants), `ammoWagon`, `flatcar`, `cargoPlane` (OLD HOWLER: fuselage, wings, two engines with prop overlays, a ramp), `propPlane` |\n998\t| Materials and patterns | `olive` (painted steel), `hyenaTan`, the `spots` pattern (camouflage), `charred` (wrecks), `thatch` and `burlap` from the core, `asphalt` with painted lines |\n999\t\n1000\t**Rigs** (`51-art-rigs.js`): Humanoid presets for every type in 8.4 and every cast member in 8.1. Each has its own\n1001\t`outfit`, `hair`, `hat`, `sleeves` and full `colors`; never the defaults. Civilians: villagers (tunics, shirts, straw\n1002\thats), medics (white coats, green trim), the reporter (a vest and a camera sprite). Animals are `E.Blob`s: chicken (R 4,\n1003\twhite, wings, feet), pig (pink, `ears: 'cat'`, tail, feet), goat (grey-white, horns, feet), parrot (wings, bright green\n1004\tand red), monkey (brown, ears, tail), seagull (white, wings). A **rig pool** keeps one rig per live entity, posed every\n1005\tupdate from the entity's state and released on despawn.\n1006\t\n1007\t**Sprites** (`52-art-sprites.js`, string sprites designed at 8–16 px): every pickup in 7.13; projectiles (grenade 5×5,\n1008\tknife 7×3, rocket 8×3 with flame frames, mortar shell 4×7, tank shell 5×5); shell casing 2×1; chute; muzzle flash frames\n1009\t(3); HUD icons at 8×8 (soldier, jeep, helicopter, boat, mast, magazine, bullet 2×5, grenade, hostage); the wolf emblem\n1010\t(32×32, for the title, the HUD and the page background) and the hyena emblem (flags and armbands).\n1011\t\n1012\t**The first-person SMG** (`55-gun.js`): a pixel-art submachine gun drawn with `px.poly` from a small 2D vector model at the\n1013\tbottom of the playfield. It slides along the bottom under its crosshair's x and turns toward the crosshair (±25°). Each\n1014\tshot kicks it back 3 px and up 2°, with brass ejecting to the right (screen-space particles that bounce on the HUD bar). The\n1015\treload animation runs .4 s magazine out, .4 s magazine in, .2 s charging handle. Under FURY it glows gold. A grenade throw\n1016\tshows the left hand arcing up. Settings: \"SHOW GUN\" (on). In local co-op each player gets a smaller gun at their panel's\n1017\tposition; online, only your own.\n1018\t\n1019\t### 9.2 Animation (the engine's rig system as the base, plus what this game needs)\n1020\t\n1021\tEngine-native: walks and runs from velocity; `point: true` with `aim` for guns; `E.MOVES.throw` for grenades and knives;\n1022\tposes `kneel`, `crouch`, `die`, `down`, `cheer`, `wave`, `hips`; `hurt`; `expr` faces; `drawPortrait` for the dialog and\n1023\tHUD (blinking, talking mouths).\n1024\t\n1025\tNew animations to build (as `rig.solvePose` wrappers or state mixes, per `API.md` \"Characters\"):\n1026\t\n1027\t| Animation | How |\n1028\t|---|---|\n1029\t| Kneel and aim | `pose: 'kneel'` + `point` + `aim` toward the camera |\n1030\t| Pop-up from cover | `crouch` ↔ stand blended over .2 s; `point` only while up |\n1031\t| Rocket on the shoulder | wrap `solvePose`: both hands up at the shoulder; a tube sprite at `rig.hand()` |\n1032\t| Blown back by a blast | the entity flies with velocity and spin while the rig blends to `down`; it lands and slides |\n1033\t| Parachute descent | `air: true`, legs dangling with a slow sway; the chute sprite above, swaying with it |\n1034\t| Hands up / surrender (TUSK, GIGGS) | wrap `solvePose`: arms raised |\n1035\t| Hostage with bound hands | wrap `solvePose`: hands together behind the back; a hunched run |\n1036\t| Panic run (civilians) | wrap `solvePose`: hands over the head; a faster gait |\n1037\t| Dragged hostage | `kneel` blend while being pulled backward |\n1038\t| Officer's whistle | a hand to the mouth (`solvePose`); the whistle icon bobs |\n1039\t| Sniper glint | a 2-frame star sprite at the head, pulsing over the telegraph |\n1040\t| Heavy gunner's burst | `point` with a recoil shake (±1 px a shot) and `expr: 'shout'` |\n1041\t| Knife and grenade throws | `E.MOVES.throw` with `wind` scaled to the telegraph |\n1042\t| Death variety | `die` with a random facing twist; a headshot snaps the head back; a fall from towers and bridges falls in z |\n1043\t| Cheering hostages, waving villagers | `cheer`, `wave` |\n1044\t| KRAGG's cackle | `expr: 'shout'` + a head bob at 8 Hz for the laugh |\n1045\t\n1046\tVehicles and the rest: wheels turn (an overlay of spokes keyed to distance traveled); suspension bobs; turrets track the\n1047\tcamera (`facing` toward it); rotors spin (an ellipse of 2–4 lines, plus blur arcs); the tail rotor; propellers; the\n1048\tdish's slow turn; boats bob and leave a wake (FX); the train's wheels and smoke puffs; the masts topple (`tilt` steps);\n1049\tthe tower collapses (its parts fall with `E.arc`); the wrecks smoke. UI: cards slide; tally numbers count up; the logo's\n1050\thowl; crosshairs pulse at low ammo.\n1051\t\n1052\tCheck every attack and death with the engine's filmstrip (`node engine/tools/filmstrip.mjs dev/index.html#range --steps\n1053\t\"...\" --seed 1`): a wind-up, a strike and a clean settle, with no backward sweeps. Look at the result; a script can't\n1054\tjudge it.\n1055\t\n1056\t### 9.3 Audio (all in code, no files)\n1057\t\n1058\t**Music** (`61-music.js`), as `game.audio.music({ bpm, steps: 4, tracks })` data with named layers. The director turns\n1059\t`perc` and `lead` layers up with intensity (a boss, a hold, many enemies on screen), ducks the music under radio lines\n1060\t(`audio.duck`), and plays stings (FURY, PACK FURY, boss defeated). Every theme is original. The **howl motif** opens the\n1061\ttitle theme and returns in Op 6 and the ending:\n1062\t\n1063\t```js\n1064\tWP.SONGS.title = { bpm: 128, steps: 4, tracks: [\n1065\t  { name: 'lead', wave: 'square', vol: .13, notes: 'A4 - - - E5 - - - A5 - - - - - G5 - | F5 - E5 - D5 - E5 - - - - - . . . . | A4 - - - E5 - - - A5 - - - C6 - B5 - | A5 - - - - - - - - - - - . . . .' },\n1066\t  { name: 'bass', wave: 'triangle', vol: .2, notes: 'A2 . A2 . A2 . A2 . F2 . F2 . F2 . F2 . | D2 . D2 . E2 . E2 . A2 . A2 . A2 . A2 . | A2 . A2 . A2 . A2 . F2 . F2 . G2 . G2 . | A2 . A2 . E2 . E2 . A2 . . . A2 . . .' },\n1067\t  { name: 'perc', wave: 'drums', vol: .22, notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h h | k . h . s . h . k k h . s . s s | k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h h | k . h . s . k . k . s s s s s s' } ] };\n1068\t```\n1069\t\n1070\t| Song | Mood |\n1071\t|---|---|\n1072\t| `title` | the Wolfpack March (above, extended to 32 bars, with a saw pad layer) |\n1073\t| `briefing` | 90 bpm, pulse arpeggios, radio-noise layer |\n1074\t| `map` | a snare roll and horn calls (the motif's first 4 notes) |\n1075\t| `op1` … `op6` | as in 8.6; each 32–64 bars with `perc`, `bass`, `lead` and `pad` layers |\n1076\t| `boss` | 160 bpm, chromatic menace, double-time kick |\n1077\t| `tally`, `gameover`, `continue` | jingles |\n1078\t| `ending` | the motif in A major, slow, swelling |\n1079\t\n1080\t**Sounds** (`60-audio.js`, `audio.define`): SMG shot (a noise burst .05 s + a square thump 90 → 50 Hz .06 s, pitch vary\n1081\t.05, at most 14 a second per player even under FURY's 22 rounds), dry click, reload (two clicks + a slide), brass tinkles, grenade throw whoosh,\n1082\texplosion (the engine's `explode` + a 60 → 30 Hz sine over .6 s + a noise tail), ricochet (\"pyeeew\", a sine bend), enemy\n1083\trifle crack (filtered noise, quieter with depth), MG burst, whiz (a missed bullet), telegraph tick (rising pitch),\n1084\tprojectile whistle, knife whoosh, rocket hiss, mortar whistle, tank shell boom, helicopter rotor (a loop of noise chops\n1085\tevery .08 s at a volume by distance), truck and tank engine loops, boat motor, rain loop, thunder, searchlight alarm chirp,\n1086\twhistle (officer), pickups (an arpeggio per kind), FURY sting, civilian-hit sting (a dissonant chord), hostage rescued\n1087\t(a fanfare), low-ammo beep (when below 6 rounds and no spares), heartbeat (damage over 75), the menu's move, pick and back.\n1088\tPositional: volume by depth, and pan by screen x if engine change 5 is in.\n1089\t\n1090\t**Voices** (`62-voice.js`): Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Per typed character (the Dialog hook, engine change 1) or\n1091\tper syllable for barks: a vowel plays a blip (`pulse` or `square`, .05–.09 s) whose pitch is the speaker's base ×\n1092\t(vowel offset: a 1.0, e 1.12, i 1.25, o .9, u .8) × a small seeded jitter (seeded by a hash of the line, so a line always\n1093\tsounds the same); a consonant adds a .015 s noise click; \"?\" bends the last blip up, \"!\" makes it louder; spaces are\n1094\tsilent. Profiles: DEN MOTHER 300 Hz `pulse12` with radio crackle bursts at each line's start and end; LOBO 150 square,\n1095\tgruff; FANG 170; TUNDRA 260; MOONSHINE 190; KRAGG 120 saw with slow vibrato, and the cackle (6 \"HA\" blips 220 → 160);\n1096\tTUSK 100; GIGGS 230, fast, with giggles; hostages 220–320; villagers 240–300. Barks: Hyena deaths (\"GWAH!\", \"UGH!\",\n1097\t\"HYAA!\"), the grenade \"HUP!\", civilian \"EEK!\", hostage \"HELP!\". **The howl:** a sine gliding 220 → 440 → 330 Hz over 1.4 s\n1098\twith growing vibrato, used for LOBO's line, PACK FURY and the endings.\n1099\t\n1100\t---\n1101\t\n1102\t## 10. UI and UX (10-foot, controller first)\n1103\t\n1104\t### 10.1 Rules\n1105\t\n1106\t- Design for a TV at 10 feet. Body text is the 5×7 font at scale 1 (28 px on a 1080p TV); key numbers and menus use scale\n1107\t  2; titles use `E.font.title` at scale 3–4. Nothing smaller. High contrast: outlines or shadows on every HUD string.\n1108\t- One idea per screen; no web-style dense panels. Tallies reveal one line at a time. The About screen is pages, not a\n1109\t  scroll of text.\n1110\t- Focus is always visible (a pulsing chevron and a brighter row) and moves with the d-pad, the stick, the arrow keys, and\n1111\t  mouse hover. ✕/Enter/click picks; ○/Esc/Backspace goes back. Every screen shows its prompts in the last-used device's\n1112\t  glyphs at the bottom right (\"✕ SELECT  ○ BACK\").\n1113\t- The standard HTML screens (pause, settings, controls, help, dev) come from `E.Shell` with a theme (ink `#f2ead3`, paper\n1114\t  `rgba(18,22,14,.92)`, accent `#e0b040`, danger `#e05a3a`, line `rgba(224,176,64,.35)`, title font `Impact,\n1115\t  'Arial Black', sans-serif`) and a CSS override for 10-foot sizes: `.esh` font 20px, `h2` 34px, buttons 18px with 14px ×\n1116\t  18px padding, sliders 260px wide.\n1117\t\n1118\t### 10.2 Screens (`71-screens.js`, canvas, pixel art)\n1119\t\n1120\t| Screen | Contents |\n1121\t|---|---|\n1122\t| `title` | the logo \"OPERATION WOLFPACK\" (olive-to-amber gradient, depth), a full moon, four wolf silhouettes on a ridge, sweeping searchlights, a helicopter crossing; the menu: START MISSION, SQUAD (co-op), MISSION SELECT (after a first clear), HIGH SCORES, SETTINGS (`game.menu('settings')`), ABOUT / CREDITS; `E.versionLabel()` and the game's version small at the bottom; \"PRESS {start}\". 10 s idle → attract |\n1123\t| `squad` | four slots (WOLF 1–4), each with its device icon and portrait; \"PRESS OPTIONS ON A CONTROLLER TO JOIN\"; START |\n1124\t| `briefing` | 8.8 #1 |\n1125\t| `map` | a pixel-art map of the Brimstone Coast (coastline polygon, jungle, river, roads, the volcano), six nodes with icons, the route drawn as you go, done ops ticked with their perk icons, the next op pulsing; DEN's line for the next op; \"✕ DEPLOY\". In Mission Select every node can be picked |\n1126\t| `opcard` | \"OPERATION N\", the name, the objective, quota icons with counts, \"GET READY\", then \"GO!\" |\n1127\t| `tally` | 7.15's lines, one at a time, then the perk card, then \"DAMAGE REPAIRED −10\" |\n1128\t| `continue` | \"CONTINUE?\" with a 10-second count (`E.Arcade.continue`), the continue count, the score |\n1129\t| `ending`, `credits`, `initials` | 8.8 #5–6 and `E.Arcade.enter` |\n1130\t| `about` | 14.2 |\n1131\t| `touch` | 14.1 |\n1132\t| `hubcard` | 13.2 |\n1133\t\n1134\t### 10.3 The HUD (`70-hud.js`, the buffer is 480×270)\n1135\t\n1136\t- **Playfield** y 0–233; **HUD bar** y 234–269: a dark olive panel with rivets.\n1137\t- **1–2 players:** P1's panel x 4–176, the quota block x 180–300, P2's panel x 304–476. In solo the P2 area shows \"WOLF 2:\n1138\t  PRESS OPTIONS TO JOIN\" while a free controller is connected, and P1's wide stats otherwise.\n1139\t- **3–4 players:** four panels 118 px wide; the quotas move under the top score row.\n1140\t- **A player panel:** a 24 px portrait (it winces when hit, grins at a streak); the callsign and score; spare magazines as\n1141\t  icons (a part-used one notched); the current magazine as 30 tiny bullets in 2 rows; grenades as icons; the DAMAGE bar (60\n1142\t  px, filling red, flashing over 75); the streak \"×3\"; \"RELOADING\" (the crosshair ring fills too); \"FURY 7\"; \"DOWN\".\n1143\t- **Quota block:** silhouettes with remaining counts (soldier, jeep, helicopter or boat, as the op uses); a check when one\n1144\t  is met.\n1145\t- **Top row** (y 2–12): `1UP 012300   HI 050000   2UP 004500` (3–4 players add 3UP/4UP); in hub sessions the round time\n1146\t  \"TIME 3:42\".\n1147\t- **Boss bar:** under the top row, 200 px, with the boss's name.\n1148\t- **Radio box:** top left, 220×48, the speaker's portrait, 2 lines (`E.Dialog`, non-modal, `auto`).\n1149\t- **Objective chips:** top right (\"MASTS 2/3\", the five hostage portraits).\n1150\t- **In the playfield:** telegraph rings, the sniper glint, mortar landing markers, threat arrows at the edges for\n1151\t  attackers off-screen, the red hit arcs, friendly markers, hit markers (a white ×, a \"HEADSHOT\" ding), floating scores,\n1152\t  crosshairs (each a circle with 4 ticks and a center dot in the seat color with a black outline; it grows with bloom,\n1153\t  turns red over a hostile, and shows the player number in co-op), low-ammo blinking, the grey crosshair of a DOWN player.\n1154\t- **Prompts** (above the HUD bar, glyph first, from `input.label`): `□ RELOAD` below 30%; \"NO AMMO! SHOOT CRATES!\" when the\n1155\t  pouch is empty; tips from 8.3 the first time.\n1156\t\n1157\t### 10.4 Settings (`72-shell.js`, group \"Game\")\n1158\t\n1159\tDifficulty (RECRUIT / VETERAN / ARCADE; asked again on START MISSION, defaulting to the saved one); Aim assist (Off / Low\n1160\t/ Medium / High); Crosshair speed (.5–2); Crosshair size (S / M / L, default L); Button symbols (PlayStation / Xbox,\n1161\tmirroring the engine's setting); Show gun (on); Friendly markers (on); Text size (Normal / Large: scale 2 radio text).\n1162\tStandard ones come free: volumes, mute, reduce motion, screen shake and flashes, pixel scaling, the screen filter (clean,\n1163\tscanlines, CRT), frame rate, vibration, dead zone, rebinding. Pause menu items: RESTART OPERATION, DEV MODE (hidden in hub\n1164\tsessions), and the standard Resume, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Help, Quit to title. Help: the controls per device\n1165\tand \"HOW TO PLAY\" in 6 short lines (fill the quota, beat the boss; shoot items to collect; shoot projectiles; don't shoot\n1166\tcivilians; reload; grenades hit everything nearby).\n1167\t\n1168\t---\n1169\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0704575-f16b-44ea-a24d-907e9c278025","uuid":"c54a306a-d3ff-4f94-945f-690336f35525","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:30:27.842Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183009__xe162c9/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n#### OP 1: RADIO HILL (dawn; teaches everything)\n- **Look:** a pink and orange dawn; dry hill grass with a dirt road band (depth 70–110) and rocks; a sea and mountains on\n  the horizon. Floor painter `hill` (E.tex.grass and E.tex.dirt by noise; the road's ruts). Music `op1` (D minor, 140 bpm).\n- **Rail:** sideways from x 0 to 2700 at 16 u/s; cam h 28, pitch 6. Holds at 520 (jeep), 1720 (air), 2700 (boss).\n- **Scenery:** sandbag lines (depth 90–130); barbed wire posts; tents (x 300–700 @260); ammo crates; a wrecked jeep (x 1000\n  @150, cover); **three radio masts** (x 900 @380, x 1500 @420, x 2150 @360: lattices 130 tall with blinking red lights);\n  the radar building with its dish (x 2550 @420); goats (supply carriers) at x 200 and 1200; seagulls; palms and rocks far\n  away.\n- **Quotas:** soldier 36, vehicle 3, air 1; objective MASTS 3 (scripted: 43 soldiers, 3 vehicles, 1 aircraft). **Boss:**\n  BIG EAR. **Perk:** COMMS DOWN.\n\n| d | Spawns | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | none | card; DEN \"OPERATION WOLFPACK IS GO. GOOD HUNTING.\"; tip chip \"AIM · {fire} FIRE\" |\n| 40 | RIFLEMAN ×3 R @200, cross, gap .8 s | they fire late; the first kills |\n| 160 | RIFLEMAN ×2 popup (sandbags sbA @110); goat carrying a MAG @130 | tip \"SHOOT ITEMS TO COLLECT THEM!\" on the goat's drop |\n| 300 | GRENADIER ×1 @160; RIFLEMAN ×2 L @240 cross | tip \"GRENADE INCOMING! SHOOT IT DOWN!\" |\n| 420 | crates ×3 @120 (MAG, GRENADE, RATION) | tip \"{reload} TO RELOAD\" when below 10 rounds |\n| 520 | jeep R @250 with gunner; **hold** ≤ 15 s | tip \"{grenade} THROWS A GRENADE.\" |\n| 680 | KNIFE ×1 popup @65 (rock); RIFLEMAN ×2 sprint @300 | tip \"KNIVES CAN BE SHOT OUT OF THE AIR!\" |\n| 820 | mast 1 in view; SNIPER on its platform (z 90); RIFLEMAN ×3 popup by the tents | objective chip MASTS 0/3 |\n| 1000 | truck stops @300 → RIFLEMAN ×4 dismount | |\n| 1180 | OFFICER @180 (whistle); RIFLEMAN ×2 | tip \"STOP THAT WHISTLE!\" |\n| 1350 | mast 2; MORTAR crew @620 behind sandbags | landing markers |\n| 1500 | RIFLEMAN ×4, both edges @150–260; red barrels ×2 beside them | the first barrel chain |\n| 1720 | VULTURE from far (z 70); **hold** until air or 30 s | |\n| 1900 | BRUTE behind sandbags @170; GRENADIER ×2 @200 | tip \"BIG ONES GO DOWN FASTER WITH A HEADSHOT.\" |\n| 2080 | mast 3; PARATROOPER ×4 (from the VULTURE if alive, else a cargo plane) | |\n| 2250 | jeep @220; RIFLEMAN ×3; a crate holding FURY @140 | FURY's first showing |\n| 2450 | KNIFE ×2 popup @70; RIFLEMAN ×3 | |\n| 2700 | **hold**: reinforcements until the quotas are met, then BIG EAR | |\n\n#### OP 2: MANGROVE RUN (misty morning; forward rail on a river)\n- **Look:** green mist, a brown-green river with moving ripples (the floor painter reads `WP.time`), muddy banks with\n  roots, dense mangroves and palms, ferns. Fog near 200, far 1100. Music `op2` (E minor, 132 bpm, toms).\n- **Rail:** forward (north) from y 0 to −3000 at 20 u/s; cam h 20, pitch 4, river bob. Holds at 1000 (air; the boat slows\n  to 8 u/s, not a stop) and 2600 (boss, on a sandbar).\n- **Scenery:** the river 220 wide (|x| < 110); stilt huts and docks on the banks; wrecked boats; side channels at d 700\n  (right) and d 2100 (left); a **rope bridge** at d 1300 (y −1500, z 40, ropes hittable); a waterfall far away at the end;\n  parrots and monkeys (carriers) in the trees.\n- **Quotas:** soldier 28, boat 6, air 1 (scripted: 33 soldiers, 6 boats, 1 aircraft). **Boss:** CROCODILE. **Perk:** CAMP\n  LOCATED (and the interrogation).\n\n| d | Spawns | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | none | DEN \"STAY LOW. THE RIVER IS CRAWLING WITH THEM.\" |\n| 60 | RIFLEMAN ×3 popup in the bank roots @200–260, lx ±120 | |\n| 200 | skiff from ahead @400 with 2 gunners, passing on the left | the first boat |\n| 380 | KNIFE ×2 dropping from branches @70, lx ±60 | close threats |\n| 520 | monkey carrying a GRENADE BOX in a tree; RIFLEMAN ×3 on a dock @250 | |\n| 700 | skiff ×2 out of the right side channel @300, crossing | |\n| 860 | GRENADIER ×2 on stilt huts @220; crates on the dock | |\n| 1000 | VULTURE ahead (z 60) drops PARATROOPER ×3 onto the banks; the boat slows | |\n| 1250 | the bridge: RIFLEMAN ×5 on it (z 40) @250 | shoot a rope: \"BRIDGE OUT!\" |\n| 1500 | patrol boat @350; MORTAR bunker on the bank @700 | |\n| 1700 | parrot flock (one carries FURY); RIFLEMAN ×4 on the banks | |\n| 1900 | skiff; BRUTE and RIFLEMAN ×2 on a barge @300 | |\n| 2100 | left channel: RIFLEMAN ×3; SNIPER in a tree @500 | |\n| 2350 | KNIFE ×2 @70; red barrels on a floating dock; a skiff from ahead | the sixth boat |\n| 2600 | **hold**: reinforcements, then CROCODILE from ahead | |\n\n#### OP 3: PALM VILLAGE (noon; civilians and windows)\n- **Look:** bright noon; sand street with cobble patches, whitewashed houses with terracotta roofs, thatched stilt huts,\n  market stalls with awnings, laundry lines, a well, palms, a teal sea with fishing boats behind. Music `op3` (G minor, 150\n  bpm, syncopated).\n- **Rail:** sideways 0 → 3000 at 15 u/s. Holds at 1600 (APC) and 2600 (the plaza, boss).\n- **Scenery:** house fronts with **window and door openings** (enemy pop-ups clipped to them); a chapel with a bell tower\n  (x 1800 @450, snipers); the plaza with a fountain (x 2600–3000); carts, crates, barrels; chickens and pigs (carriers).\n  Civilians: about 20 villager crossings, two medic pairs with stretchers, one reporter.\n- **Quotas:** soldier 38, vehicle 4 (scripted: 45 soldiers, 4 vehicles). **Boss:** WARTHOG. **Perk:** VILLAGE LIBERATED\n  (damage −40).\n\n| d | Spawns | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | none | DEN \"THE VILLAGERS ARE STILL INSIDE. WATCH YOUR FIRE!\" |\n| 50 | villagers ×2 fleeing @140; RIFLEMAN ×3 window pop-ups @200 | tip \"CIVILIANS! WATCH YOUR FIRE!\" |\n| 200 | chickens ×3 (MAG, RATION, none); RIFLEMAN ×2 cross | |\n| 350 | jeep @230; a civilian crossing in front of it @120 | a line-of-fire test |\n| 500 | GRENADIER ×2 on roofs (z 30) @240; medic pair crossing @110 | |\n| 680 | OFFICER and RIFLEMAN ×4 popping up behind the market stalls | |\n| 850 | pig carrying a GRENADE BOX; KNIFE ×2 from doorways @80 | |\n| 1000 | truck → dismount ×4; villagers ×3 run | |\n| 1200 | BRUTE in the street @160; the reporter crosses | spare him: \"THE PRESS THANKS YOU!\" + INTEL |\n| 1400 | RIFLEMAN ×5 crossing both ways, with civilians ×2 mixed in | tension |\n| 1600 | APC @300 (rockets) → dismount ×3; **hold** ≤ 30 s | |\n| 1800 | SNIPER ×2 in the bell tower (z 60) @450; RIFLEMAN ×3 | |\n| 2000 | jeep; PARATROOPER ×3 | |\n| 2200 | a crate holding DYNAMITE, civilians far off; RIFLEMAN ×6 | tip \"DYNAMITE HITS EVERYONE ON SCREEN!\" |\n| 2400 | KNIFE ×2; GRENADIER ×2; villagers ×2 | |\n| 2600 | **hold** (plaza): reinforcements, then WARTHOG | |\n\n#### OP 4: POWDER KEG DEPOT (dusk; explosions)\n- **Look:** a purple and orange dusk; concrete and dirt; stacked ammo crates, big red fuel tanks, metal sheds, cranes,\n  floodlights coming on, a water tower, embers in the air. Music `op4` (C minor, 146 bpm, industrial noise hits).\n- **Rail:** sideways 0 → 3000 at 16 u/s. Holds at 950 and 2000 (air) and 2700 (boss).\n- **Scenery:** **railway tracks** at depth 260 along the whole rail (the boss arena), flatcars, three ammo wagons on a\n  siding (x 2500–2900 @250), the water tower (x 1600 @400), a warehouse with doors (x 2400 @300), barbed wire, a cargo\n  plane overhead at d 560.\n- **Quotas:** soldier 37, vehicle 3, air 2 (scripted: 43 soldiers, 3 vehicles, 2 aircraft). **Boss:** IRON HOG.\n  **Perk:** SUPPLIES SEIZED.\n\n| d | Spawns | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | none | DEN \"THIS PLACE IS A POWDER KEG. LIGHT IT UP!\" |\n| 60 | RIFLEMAN ×4 cross @220 beside fuel tank A | shoot the tank: a chain |\n| 220 | RPG ×2 kneeling on crates @200 | the first RPG troopers |\n| 400 | jeep @240; MORTAR crew @650 | |\n| 560 | the cargo plane drops PARATROOPER ×5 and a supply chute (AMMO CRATE) | |\n| 760 | BRUTE and RIFLEMAN ×3 behind sandbags @150 | |\n| 950 | VULTURE #1; **hold** ≤ 25 s | |\n| 1150 | a forklift carrying a GRENADE BOX crate crosses @160; RIFLEMAN ×3 | |\n| 1350 | APC @300 → dismount ×3 | |\n| 1600 | SNIPER on the water tower (z 70); RIFLEMAN ×4 | |\n| 1800 | a row of 3 fuel tanks with RIFLEMAN ×6 beside them | \"CHAIN!\" bonus +1000 for 4+ kills in one blast |\n| 2000 | VULTURE #2; RPG ×2; **hold** ≤ 25 s | |\n| 2200 | KNIFE ×2; OFFICER | |\n| 2400 | jeep; RIFLEMAN ×4 from the warehouse doors | |\n| 2700 | **hold**: reinforcements, then IRON HOG on the tracks | |\n\n#### OP 5: THE KENNEL (night and rain; the breakout)\n- **Look:** a black-blue night, rain, mud with puddle glints, a double barbed-wire fence (depth 80 and 100), wooden\n  barracks, four watchtowers with **sweeping searchlights**, fire barrels, floodlights, the cage block (\"the kennel\"), a\n  flagpole with the hyena flag. Darkness .75 (10.1 `53-fx`). Music `op5` (F# minor, 120 bpm, sparse, a heartbeat kick)\n  under rain.\n- **Rail:** sideways 0 → 2800 at 14 u/s; a yaw pan from −90° to −75° over d 1500–1700 to look into the yard. Holds at 1450\n  (escort, ≤ 70 s) and 2500 (boss).\n- **Searchlights:** each sweeps an ellipse on the ground (radius 40) along a path. When a beam crosses the camera's\n  position (depth < 30), **SPOTTED** for 3 s (enemy accuracy ×1.5, a white flash, an alarm chirp). Shoot the light (HP 2)\n  to put it out.\n- **Quotas:** soldier 35, vehicle 3 (scripted: 41 soldiers including the 10 chasers, 2 jeeps and the truck).\n  **Hostages:** escort as many as you can (they count toward the ending, not toward clearing the op). **Boss:** MAJOR\n  TUSK. **Perk:** HOSTAGES FREED.\n\n| d | Spawns | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | none | card; LOBO \"THE KENNEL. FIVE HOSTAGES. ZERO MISTAKES.\" |\n| 60 | RIFLEMAN ×3 patrol, cross @160 with flashlights; tower 1 searchlight | |\n| 250 | a crate holding a FLARE @120; RIFLEMAN ×3 | tip \"SHOOT THE FLARE TO LIGHT THE YARD!\" |\n| 420 | jeep with a searchlight @220 | |\n| 600 | SNIPER in tower 1's cabin (z 70); GRENADIER ×2 | |\n| 800 | RIFLEMAN ×4; KNIFE ×2 through a gap in the fence @70 | |\n| 1000 | tower 2's searchlight; BRUTE | |\n| 1200 | the gate opens: truck → dismount ×4 | |\n| 1450 | **BREAKOUT** (**hold**, escort): the cells open one by one, 8 s apart. Each hostage runs from lx +180 to the breach at lx −200 @140–180, chased by 2 `chase` riflemen; tower MGs fire | the hostage pips and portraits on the HUD |\n| 1750 | RIFLEMAN ×4 out of the barracks doors | |\n| 1950 | tower 3; jeep | |\n| 2200 | RIFLEMAN ×5; GRENADIER ×2 | |\n| 2500 | **hold**: reinforcements, then MAJOR TUSK (the central tower, x 2700) | |\n\n#### OP 6: LAST FLIGHT OUT (sunrise storm; boarding, takeoff, the gunship)\n- **Look:** a dark grey sunrise under storm clouds, wind; the apron with painted lines, hangars, a control tower, fuel\n  trucks, a windsock, runway lights. Then the air: Mode 7 at altitude over jungle, coast and sea (Pilotwings-like). Music\n  `op6` (A minor, 156 bpm, lifting into C major at takeoff).\n- **Part A rail:** sideways 0 → 2000 at 18 u/s. Holds at 450 (air), 850 (tank ≤ 40 s), 1500 (escort), 2000 (quota).\n- **Scenery A:** hangars ×3 (x 200, 900, 1600 @320; the tank comes out of hangar 2), the control tower (x 1200 @500;\n  snipers), fuel trucks (explode like barrels), parked prop planes, a radar dish, crates, barrels; OLD HOWLER at x 2050\n  @180 with its ramp down.\n- **Part B rail (takeoff):** cut to the plane's open ramp, looking **back** (south, `angle = +π/2`) while the plane runs\n  north along the runway; speed 30 → 90 over 20 s, liftoff at 20 s, climbing h 28 → 260 and pitch 6 → 28 by 35 s.\n- **Quotas (part A):** soldier 27, vehicle 4, air 2 (scripted: 32 soldiers including the 10 escort attackers, 4\n  vehicles, 2 aircraft). **Boss:** HYENA ONE (part B). **Hostages:** the n freed in Op 5 (5 when the op is played alone).\n\n| d / t | Spawns | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | none | DEN \"OLD HOWLER IS ON THE RUNWAY. GET THEM ABOARD!\" |\n| 60 | RIFLEMAN ×4 popping out of hangar doors @320 | |\n| 250 | jeep ×2 cross @200 | |\n| 450 | VULTURE #1; **hold** ≤ 25 s | |\n| 650 | RPG ×2 on fuel trucks | the trucks explode like barrels |\n| 850 | MAULER rolls out of hangar 2 @320; **hold** ≤ 40 s | the tank |\n| 1100 | PARATROOPER ×5; SNIPER ×2 in the control tower (z 80) | |\n| 1300 | APC @280 → dismount | |\n| 1500 | **ESCORT** (**hold**): a friendly truck drops off the n hostages, who run to the ramp (x 1500 → 2050 @140–200, about 25 s). Always 10 attackers: 2 chasers per hostage, the rest firing from the hangar doors. VULTURE #2 strafes | with 0 hostages, the hold lasts 15 s |\n| 1900 | RIFLEMAN ×4; KNIFE ×2 | the last push |\n| 2000 | **hold** for the quotas; then the cut \"EVERYBODY ON THE PLANE!\" → part B | |\n| B t 0 | jeep ×3 chasing on the runway (`anchor: 'cam'`, depth 60–160), each with a gunner | bonus vehicles, not quota |\n| B t 10 | a SAM truck at the runway's end fires 3 missiles | shoot them down |\n| B t 20 | liftoff; DEN \"HANG ON!\" | |\n| B t 30 | HYENA ONE climbs into view behind the plane → boss | |\n\n### 8.7 Bosses\n\n| Boss | Arena | Phases and weak points (HP) | Attacks | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **BIG EAR** (Op 1): a six-wheel signal truck | drives in from the right @260, parks, shuffles ±120 every 8 s | 1: radar dish (30, rotating), gunners L and R (1 each, each respawns twice after 6 s), rocket pod (15). 2: once the dish is gone, the cab and engine (60) stop being armored | dish up: 2 PARATROOPERS every 12 s; gunners' rings; 2 rockets every 6 s | 10000 |\n| **CROCODILE** (Op 2): a gunboat | ahead, backing up at the camera's speed @160–240, weaving ±80 | front turret (20), rear turret (20), deck mortar (15) → bridge (45) | turret rings (4-round bursts); mortar arcs; 2 skiffs at 50% | 14000 |\n| **WARTHOG** (Op 3): a flamethrower half-track | the plaza @200, moving ±100 | cannon (25), fuel tanks L and R (12 each), SGT. SNARL in the hatch (head 2: each hit stuns the vehicle 2 s) → hull (50) | cannon: 2.0 s glow → tank shell. Flamethrower (while a tank holds out): the nozzle glows 1.5 s, then a flame wave (shoot that side's tank during the glow to stop it). Civilians cross the far side 3 times | 18000 |\n| **IRON HOG** (Op 4): an armored train | the tracks @260, back and forth over 900 units at 45 u/s | MG car (20), rocket car (25), mortar car (20) → boiler (50; its vents glow) | rings; rocket salvos (3); mortar arcs; vent steam (1.5 s glow → 10 damage, unless the boiler takes 10 in the glow). Ammo wagons on the siding deal 30 to the car beside them | 22000 |\n| **MAJOR TUSK** (Op 5): the warden | 1: the central tower @300, cabin at z 80. 2: on foot | 1: tower MG (15), searchlights ×2 (2 each), support legs ×3 (15 each) → the tower falls. 2: TUSK (40; head ×3; a riot shield blocks the body) | 1: MG bursts, SPOTTED. 2: he walks from depth 250 to 90; lowers the shield 1.0 s → shotgun (3 pellets × 6); a grenade knocks the shield aside for 3 s; below depth 90 he charges, and reaching depth 60 hits for 20 and knocks him back to 150 | 26000 |\n| **HYENA ONE** (Op 6): KRAGG's gunship | in the air behind the plane (`anchor: 'cam'`), depth 140–220 | 1: rocket pods L and R (25 each), door gunner (3; respawns). 2: nose cannon (30). 3: KRAGG leaning out with a launcher (head 3: each hit staggers 2 s) and the rotor hub (60) | 1: salvos of 3 rockets every 5 s; door gunner rings. 2: 2.0 s glow → tank shell (2 hits to shoot down). 3: homing missiles; his taunts. Defeat: it spirals into the sea below | 30000 |\n\n### 8.8 Cutscenes (`47-cutscenes.js`)\n\nScripts (`game.script` generators) drive rigs, camera moves, `E.Dialog` (modal, with portraits) and sound. Hold\n✕/Enter/click for 1 s to skip, with a ring that fills. Every cutscene works headless (the tests run them at speed).\n\n1. **Briefing** (40 s): a night coast pan in Mode 7 (the coastline floor, the volcano glow in the Backdrop), cards, DEN's\n   lines, the howl.\n2. **Interrogation** (30 s): a dim tent drawn with px (canvas walls, a hanging lamp swinging, its light), LOBO and GIGGS\n   (rigs), the lines in 8.3, a shake on \"WRONG ANSWER.\"\n3. **Kennel aftermath** (12 s): the freed hostages kneel (`pose: 'kneel'`) as their portraits slide in, lit or dark; \"{n}\n   OF 5 HOSTAGES ARE FREE.\"\n4. **Takeoff cut** (1.5 s): a wipe \"EVERYBODY ON THE PLANE!\"\n5. **Endings** (25 s): OLD HOWLER over the sea at sunrise (Mode 7 at altitude, the plane drawn as a shape from behind),\n   the text of 8.3, the rank, the Wolfpack's howl.\n6. **Credits:** scrolling text over the night coast (the About content, 14.2).\n\n---\n\n## 9. Presentation: art assets, animation, audio\n\n### 9.1 Art direction and assets\n\nThe engine's native style is the base: PS1/SNES-era pixel art, shaded HD Humanoid rigs, shapes-as-data with the house\nshading and outline, `E.tones` ramps, the 5×7 font, `E.font.title` logos. Aim for the look list in `API.md` (backdrop,\ntextured floors, 3–8 props a screen, dressed characters, effects on every hit, lighting, title font). Compare screenshots\nwith Metal Slug, not with NES games.\n\n**New shapes** (`50-art-shapes.js`, written to the `docs/ASSETS.md` format, facing south, in units of 16 = 1 m; check each\nwith `node engine/tools/asset-sheet.mjs src/50-art-shapes.js#<id>`):\n\n| Group | Shapes |\n|---|---|\n| Field props | `sandbags` (a row of flattened `ball` sacks, burlap, `len` param), `sandbagNest` (a ring), `redBarrel` (a lathe with bands), `ammoCrate` (olive with stencil lines), `medCrate`, `fuelTank` (a horizontal cylinder on legs), `barbedFence` (posts; wire drawn as lines by the renderer), `tent` (a linen prism), `campfireDrum`, `floodlight`, `searchlight` (a cylinder head on a pivot), `windsock`, `runwayLight`, `forklift` |\n| Structures | `radioMast` (a lattice: thin boxes in `row`s with braces, a platform, a red light; `tilt` param for toppling), `radarDish` (a lathe dish; spun by facing), `radarHut`, `stiltHut` (thatch), `villageHouse` (plaster with tile roof; window and door openings as data for the clip system), `marketStall` (an awning wedge), `chapelTower`, `dock`, `ropeBridge`, `barracks`, `watchtower` (4 legs, a cabin, a roof), `cageBlock`, `gate`, `hangar` (an arched roof), `controlTower`, `waterTower`, `crane`, `shed` |\n| Plants and rocks | `palm` (a leaning trunk of `cyl` segments, frond prisms), `mangrove` (a tree on root cylinders), `fern`, plus the core `tree`, `bush`, `rock`, `grass`, `pine` |\n| Vehicles | `jeep`, `truck`, `halftrack` (WARTHOG), `apc` + `apcTurret`, `tank` + `tankTurret`, `skiff`, `gunboat` (small, and CROCODILE big with turrets and a bridge), `heli` (fuselage, tail boom, skids, pods; the rotor is an overlay), `hyenaOne` (bigger, a nose cannon, pods, an open door), `bigEar` (a 6×6 with a dish mount), `locomotive`, `trainCar` (×3 variants), `ammoWagon`, `flatcar`, `cargoPlane` (OLD HOWLER: fuselage, wings, two engines with prop overlays, a ramp), `propPlane` |\n| Materials and patterns | `olive` (painted steel), `hyenaTan`, the `spots` pattern (camouflage), `charred` (wrecks), `thatch` and `burlap` from the core, `asphalt` with painted lines |\n\n**Rigs** (`51-art-rigs.js`): Humanoid presets for every type in 8.4 and every cast member in 8.1. Each has its own\n`outfit`, `hair`, `hat`, `sleeves` and full `colors`; never the defaults. Civilians: villagers (tunics, shirts, straw\nhats), medics (white coats, green trim), the reporter (a vest and a camera sprite). Animals are `E.Blob`s: chicken (R 4,\nwhite, wings, feet), pig (pink, `ears: 'cat'`, tail, feet), goat (grey-white, horns, feet), parrot (wings, bright green\nand red), monkey (brown, ears, tail), seagull (white, wings). A **rig pool** keeps one rig per live entity, posed every\nupdate from the entity's state and released on despawn.\n\n**Sprites** (`52-art-sprites.js`, string sprites designed at 8–16 px): every pickup in 7.13; projectiles (grenade 5×5,\nknife 7×3, rocket 8×3 with flame frames, mortar shell 4×7, tank shell 5×5); shell casing 2×1; chute; muzzle flash frames\n(3); HUD icons at 8×8 (soldier, jeep, helicopter, boat, mast, magazine, bullet 2×5, grenade, hostage); the wolf emblem\n(32×32, for the title, the HUD and the page background) and the hyena emblem (flags and armbands).\n\n**The first-person SMG** (`55-gun.js`): a pixel-art submachine gun drawn with `px.poly` from a small 2D vector model at the\nbottom of the playfield. It slides along the bottom under its crosshair's x and turns toward the crosshair (±25°). Each\nshot kicks it back 3 px and up 2°, with brass ejecting to the right (screen-space particles that bounce on the HUD bar). The\nreload animation runs .4 s magazine out, .4 s magazine in, .2 s charging handle. Under FURY it glows gold. A grenade throw\nshows the left hand arcing up. Settings: \"SHOW GUN\" (on). In local co-op each player gets a smaller gun at their panel's\nposition; online, only your own.\n\n### 9.2 Animation (the engine's rig system as the base, plus what this game needs)\n\nEngine-native: walks and runs from velocity; `point: true` with `aim` for guns; `E.MOVES.throw` for grenades and knives;\nposes `kneel`, `crouch`, `die`, `down`, `cheer`, `wave`, `hips`; `hurt`; `expr` faces; `drawPortrait` for the dialog and\nHUD (blinking, talking mouths).\n\nNew animations to build (as `rig.solvePose` wrappers or state mixes, per `API.md` \"Characters\"):\n\n| Animation | How |\n|---|---|\n| Kneel and aim | `pose: 'kneel'` + `point` + `aim` toward the camera |\n| Pop-up from cover | `crouch` ↔ stand blended over .2 s; `point` only while up |\n| Rocket on the shoulder | wrap `solvePose`: both hands up at the shoulder; a tube sprite at `rig.hand()` |\n| Blown back by a blast | the entity flies with velocity and spin while the rig blends to `down`; it lands and slides |\n| Parachute descent | `air: true`, legs dangling with a slow sway; the chute sprite above, swaying with it |\n| Hands up / surrender (TUSK, GIGGS) | wrap `solvePose`: arms raised |\n| Hostage with bound hands | wrap `solvePose`: hands together behind the back; a hunched run |\n| Panic run (civilians) | wrap `solvePose`: hands over the head; a faster gait |\n| Dragged hostage | `kneel` blend while being pulled backward |\n| Officer's whistle | a hand to the mouth (`solvePose`); the whistle icon bobs |\n| Sniper glint | a 2-frame star sprite at the head, pulsing over the telegraph |\n| Heavy gunner's burst | `point` with a recoil shake (±1 px a shot) and `expr: 'shout'` |\n| Knife and grenade throws | `E.MOVES.throw` with `wind` scaled to the telegraph |\n| Death variety | `die` with a random facing twist; a headshot snaps the head back; a fall from towers and bridges falls in z |\n| Cheering hostages, waving villagers | `cheer`, `wave` |\n| KRAGG's cackle | `expr: 'shout'` + a head bob at 8 Hz for the laugh |\n\nVehicles and the rest: wheels turn (an overlay of spokes keyed to distance traveled); suspension bobs; turrets track the\ncamera (`facing` toward it); rotors spin (an ellipse of 2–4 lines, plus blur arcs); the tail rotor; propellers; the\ndish's slow turn; boats bob and leave a wake (FX); the train's wheels and smoke puffs; the masts topple (`tilt` steps);\nthe tower collapses (its parts fall with `E.arc`); the wrecks smoke. UI: cards slide; tally numbers count up; the logo's\nhowl; crosshairs pulse at low ammo.\n\nCheck every attack and death with the engine's filmstrip (`node engine/tools/filmstrip.mjs dev/index.html#range --steps\n\"...\" --seed 1`): a wind-up, a strike and a clean settle, with no backward sweeps. Look at the result; a script can't\njudge it.\n\n### 9.3 Audio (all in code, no files)\n\n**Music** (`61-music.js`), as `game.audio.music({ bpm, steps: 4, tracks })` data with named layers. The director turns\n`perc` and `lead` layers up with intensity (a boss, a hold, many enemies on screen), ducks the music under radio lines\n(`audio.duck`), and plays stings (FURY, PACK FURY, boss defeated). Every theme is original. The **howl motif** opens the\ntitle theme and returns in Op 6 and the ending:\n\n```js\nWP.SONGS.title = { bpm: 128, steps: 4, tracks: [\n  { name: 'lead', wave: 'square', vol: .13, notes: 'A4 - - - E5 - - - A5 - - - - - G5 - | F5 - E5 - D5 - E5 - - - - - . . . . | A4 - - - E5 - - - A5 - - - C6 - B5 - | A5 - - - - - - - - - - - . . . .' },\n  { name: 'bass', wave: 'triangle', vol: .2, notes: 'A2 . A2 . A2 . A2 . F2 . F2 . F2 . F2 . | D2 . D2 . E2 . E2 . A2 . A2 . A2 . A2 . | A2 . A2 . A2 . A2 . F2 . F2 . G2 . G2 . | A2 . A2 . E2 . E2 . A2 . . . A2 . . .' },\n  { name: 'perc', wave: 'drums', vol: .22, notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h h | k . h . s . h . k k h . s . s s | k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h h | k . h . s . k . k . s s s s s s' } ] };\n```\n\n| Song | Mood |\n|---|---|\n| `title` | the Wolfpack March (above, extended to 32 bars, with a saw pad layer) |\n| `briefing` | 90 bpm, pulse arpeggios, radio-noise layer |\n| `map` | a snare roll and horn calls (the motif's first 4 notes) |\n| `op1` … `op6` | as in 8.6; each 32–64 bars with `perc`, `bass`, `lead` and `pad` layers |\n| `boss` | 160 bpm, chromatic menace, double-time kick |\n| `tally`, `gameover`, `continue` | jingles |\n| `ending` | the motif in A major, slow, swelling |\n\n**Sounds** (`60-audio.js`, `audio.define`): SMG shot (a noise burst .05 s + a square thump 90 → 50 Hz .06 s, pitch vary\n.05, at most 14 a second per player even under FURY's 22 rounds), dry click, reload (two clicks + a slide), brass tinkles, grenade throw whoosh,\nexplosion (the engine's `explode` + a 60 → 30 Hz sine over .6 s + a noise tail), ricochet (\"pyeeew\", a sine bend), enemy\nrifle crack (filtered noise, quieter with depth), MG burst, whiz (a missed bullet), telegraph tick (rising pitch),\nprojectile whistle, knife whoosh, rocket hiss, mortar whistle, tank shell boom, helicopter rotor (a loop of noise chops\nevery .08 s at a volume by distance), truck and tank engine loops, boat motor, rain loop, thunder, searchlight alarm chirp,\nwhistle (officer), pickups (an arpeggio per kind), FURY sting, civilian-hit sting (a dissonant chord), hostage rescued\n(a fanfare), low-ammo beep (when below 6 rounds and no spares), heartbeat (damage over 75), the menu's move, pick and back.\nPositional: volume by depth, and pan by screen x if engine change 5 is in.\n\n**Voices** (`62-voice.js`): Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Per typed character (the Dialog hook, engine change 1) or\nper syllable for barks: a vowel plays a blip (`pulse` or `square`, .05–.09 s) whose pitch is the speaker's base ×\n(vowel offset: a 1.0, e 1.12, i 1.25, o .9, u .8) × a small seeded jitter (seeded by a hash of the line, so a line always\nsounds the same); a consonant adds a .015 s noise click; \"?\" bends the last blip up, \"!\" makes it louder; spaces are\nsilent. Profiles: DEN MOTHER 300 Hz `pulse12` with radio crackle bursts at each line's start and end; LOBO 150 square,\ngruff; FANG 170; TUNDRA 260; MOONSHINE 190; KRAGG 120 saw with slow vibrato, and the cackle (6 \"HA\" blips 220 → 160);\nTUSK 100; GIGGS 230, fast, with giggles; hostages 220–320; villagers 240–300. Barks: Hyena deaths (\"GWAH!\", \"UGH!\",\n\"HYAA!\"), the grenade \"HUP!\", civilian \"EEK!\", hostage \"HELP!\". **The howl:** a sine gliding 220 → 440 → 330 Hz over 1.4 s\nwith growing vibrato, used for LOBO's line, PACK FURY and the endings.\n\n---\n\n## 10. UI and UX (10-foot, controller first)\n\n### 10.1 Rules\n\n- Design for a TV at 10 feet. Body text is the 5×7 font at scale 1 (28 px on a 1080p TV); key numbers and menus use scale\n  2; titles use `E.font.title` at scale 3–4. Nothing smaller. High contrast: outlines or shadows on every HUD string.\n- One idea per screen; no web-style dense panels. Tallies reveal one line at a time. The About screen is pages, not a\n  scroll of text.\n- Focus is always visible (a pulsing chevron and a brighter row) and moves with the d-pad, the stick, the arrow keys, and\n  mouse hover. ✕/Enter/click picks; ○/Esc/Backspace goes back. Every screen shows its prompts in the last-used device's\n  glyphs at the bottom right (\"✕ SELECT  ○ BACK\").\n- The standard HTML screens (pause, settings, controls, help, dev) come from `E.Shell` with a theme (ink `#f2ead3`, paper\n  `rgba(18,22,14,.92)`, accent `#e0b040`, danger `#e05a3a`, line `rgba(224,176,64,.35)`, title font `Impact,\n  'Arial Black', sans-serif`) and a CSS override for 10-foot sizes: `.esh` font 20px, `h2` 34px, buttons 18px with 14px ×\n  18px padding, sliders 260px wide.\n\n### 10.2 Screens (`71-screens.js`, canvas, pixel art)\n\n| Screen | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| `title` | the logo \"OPERATION WOLFPACK\" (olive-to-amber gradient, depth), a full moon, four wolf silhouettes on a ridge, sweeping searchlights, a helicopter crossing; the menu: START MISSION, SQUAD (co-op), MISSION SELECT (after a first clear), HIGH SCORES, SETTINGS (`game.menu('settings')`), ABOUT / CREDITS; `E.versionLabel()` and the game's version small at the bottom; \"PRESS {start}\". 10 s idle → attract |\n| `squad` | four slots (WOLF 1–4), each with its device icon and portrait; \"PRESS OPTIONS ON A CONTROLLER TO JOIN\"; START |\n| `briefing` | 8.8 #1 |\n| `map` | a pixel-art map of the Brimstone Coast (coastline polygon, jungle, river, roads, the volcano), six nodes with icons, the route drawn as you go, done ops ticked with their perk icons, the next op pulsing; DEN's line for the next op; \"✕ DEPLOY\". In Mission Select every node can be picked |\n| `opcard` | \"OPERATION N\", the name, the objective, quota icons with counts, \"GET READY\", then \"GO!\" |\n| `tally` | 7.15's lines, one at a time, then the perk card, then \"DAMAGE REPAIRED −10\" |\n| `continue` | \"CONTINUE?\" with a 10-second count (`E.Arcade.continue`), the continue count, the score |\n| `ending`, `credits`, `initials` | 8.8 #5–6 and `E.Arcade.enter` |\n| `about` | 14.2 |\n| `touch` | 14.1 |\n| `hubcard` | 13.2 |\n\n### 10.3 The HUD (`70-hud.js`, the buffer is 480×270)\n\n- **Playfield** y 0–233; **HUD bar** y 234–269: a dark olive panel with rivets.\n- **1–2 players:** P1's panel x 4–176, the quota block x 180–300, P2's panel x 304–476. In solo the P2 area shows \"WOLF 2:\n  PRESS OPTIONS TO JOIN\" while a free controller is connected, and P1's wide stats otherwise.\n- **3–4 players:** four panels 118 px wide; the quotas move under the top score row.\n- **A player panel:** a 24 px portrait (it winces when hit, grins at a streak); the callsign and score; spare magazines as\n  icons (a part-used one notched); the current magazine as 30 tiny bullets in 2 rows; grenades as icons; the DAMAGE bar (60\n  px, filling red, flashing over 75); the streak \"×3\"; \"RELOADING\" (the crosshair ring fills too); \"FURY 7\"; \"DOWN\".\n- **Quota block:** silhouettes with remaining counts (soldier, jeep, helicopter or boat, as the op uses); a check when one\n  is met.\n- **Top row** (y 2–12): `1UP 012300   HI 050000   2UP 004500` (3–4 players add 3UP/4UP); in hub sessions the round time\n  \"TIME 3:42\".\n- **Boss bar:** under the top row, 200 px, with the boss's name.\n- **Radio box:** top left, 220×48, the speaker's portrait, 2 lines (`E.Dialog`, non-modal, `auto`).\n- **Objective chips:** top right (\"MASTS 2/3\", the five hostage portraits).\n- **In the playfield:** telegraph rings, the sniper glint, mortar landing markers, threat arrows at the edges for\n  attackers off-screen, the red hit arcs, friendly markers, hit markers (a white ×, a \"HEADSHOT\" ding), floating scores,\n  crosshairs (each a circle with 4 ticks and a center dot in the seat color with a black outline; it grows with bloom,\n  turns red over a hostile, and shows the player number in co-op), low-ammo blinking, the grey crosshair of a DOWN player.\n- **Prompts** (above the HUD bar, glyph first, from `input.label`): `□ RELOAD` below 30%; \"NO AMMO! SHOOT CRATES!\" when the\n  pouch is empty; tips from 8.3 the first time.\n\n### 10.4 Settings (`72-shell.js`, group \"Game\")\n\nDifficulty (RECRUIT / VETERAN / ARCADE; asked again on START MISSION, defaulting to the saved one); Aim assist (Off / Low\n/ Medium / High); Crosshair speed (.5–2); Crosshair size (S / M / L, default L); Button symbols (PlayStation / Xbox,\nmirroring the engine's setting); Show gun (on); Friendly markers (on); Text size (Normal / Large: scale 2 radio text).\nStandard ones come free: volumes, mute, reduce motion, screen shake and flashes, pixel scaling, the screen filter (clean,\nscanlines, CRT), frame rate, vibration, dead zone, rebinding. Pause menu items: RESTART OPERATION, DEV MODE (hidden in hub\nsessions), and the standard Resume, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Help, Quit to title. Help: the controls per device\nand \"HOW TO PLAY\" in 6 short lines (fill the quota, beat the boss; shoot items to collect; shoot projectiles; don't shoot\ncivilians; reload; grenades hit everything nearby).\n\n---\n","numLines":400,"startLine":770,"totalLines":1519}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UdPnCQSVW9FobvbjrAz4pi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2HNsh2nxZj5DCn4ZT7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NB1qeMnmLTXrxC2ibdsKDA","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183009__xe162c9/work/PLAN.md","offset":1170,"limit":350},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16837,"cache_read_input_tokens":53678,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16837},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0704575-f16b-44ea-a24d-907e9c278025","uuid":"b983c95c-13b1-4d21-ad31-9a3b5d5fc987","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:30:30.651Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2HNdZP4YvwLGsDQa89","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01NB1qeMnmLTXrxC2ibdsKDA":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183009__xe162c9/work/PLAN.md","offset":1170,"limit":350}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NB1qeMnmLTXrxC2ibdsKDA","type":"tool_result","content":"1170\t## 11. Dev mode (`73-devmode.js`)\n1171\t\n1172\tReached from the pause menu (DEV MODE). It is an `E.Shell` screen built with the rows extension (engine change 2), so it\n1173\tworks with the pad, keys and mouse like the rest of the menu. In hub sessions it is hidden.\n1174\t\n1175\t### 11.1 Live sliders (the important balance variables)\n1176\t\n1177\tEach is a setting in group `Dev` (hidden from Settings) whose `apply` writes `WP.T[key]` at once, even mid-fight.\n1178\t**RESET TO DEFAULTS** is `settings.reset('Dev')`. While any value differs from its default, the HUD shows a small \"DEV\"\n1179\tbadge.\n1180\t\n1181\t| Key | Label | Default | Range |\n1182\t|---|---|---|---|\n1183\t| `fireRate` | Fire rate (rounds/s) | 11 | 4–24 |\n1184\t| `magSize` | Magazine size | 30 | 10–60 |\n1185\t| `reloadTime` | Reload time (s) | 1.0 | .2–3 |\n1186\t| `bulletDmg` | Bullet damage | 1 | .5–4 |\n1187\t| `bloomMax` | Max spread (px) | 7 | 0–20 |\n1188\t| `startMags` | Starting magazines | 6 | 1–15 |\n1189\t| `startGrenades` | Starting grenades | 4 | 0–9 |\n1190\t| `grenadeRadius` | Grenade radius | 52 | 20–140 |\n1191\t| `grenadeDmg` | Grenade damage | 12 | 2–40 |\n1192\t| `assist` | Aim assist strength | .6 | 0–1 |\n1193\t| `padSpeed` | Pad crosshair speed (px/s) | 520 | 150–1000 |\n1194\t| `enemyHp` | Enemy HP × | 1 | .25–4 |\n1195\t| `enemyAccuracy` | Enemy accuracy × | 1 | 0–2 |\n1196\t| `telegraph` | Telegraph time × | 1 | .3–2.5 |\n1197\t| `enemyDamage` | Enemy damage × | 1 | 0–3 |\n1198\t| `spawnDensity` | Spawn density × | 1 | .25–2.5 |\n1199\t| `projectileSpeed` | Projectile speed × | 1 | .5–2 |\n1200\t| `railSpeed` | Rail speed × | 1 | .25–3 |\n1201\t| `quota` | Quotas × | 1 | .25–2 |\n1202\t| `dropChance` | Drop chance × | 1 | 0–3 |\n1203\t| `civilianDamage` | Civilian hit damage | 8 | 0–30 |\n1204\t| `clearHeal` | Stage-clear heal | 10 | 0–100 |\n1205\t| `timeScale` | Game speed | 1 | .1–2 |\n1206\t\n1207\t### 11.2 Toggles, tools and actions\n1208\t\n1209\t- **Cheats:** God mode, Infinite ammo, Infinite grenades, One-hit kills, Enemies hold fire, Bot autopilot (P1).\n1210\t- **View:** Show hit shapes, Show paths and spawn markers, Perf overlay (frame ms, entities, particles, rail d, beat,\n1211\t  seed), Slow motion (1, .5, .25, .1), Frame step (while paused: STEP ONE FRAME).\n1212\t- **Jump:** an operation select (1–6), a beat select (that op's beats, plus BOSS and, for Op 6, PART B), GO. Also RANGE (a\n1213\t  target-practice scene with dummies at depths 60–600, a moving target, a projectile thrower, a civilian walker, and a\n1214\t  readout of time-to-target).\n1215\t- **Spawn:** a type select (every `WP.TYPES` id) → SPAWN AT CROSSHAIR. It takes the floor point under P1's crosshair and\n1216\t  converts it to the camera frame.\n1217\t- **Flow:** Fill quotas, Trigger boss, Kill all, Damage self 25, Heal, Give 3 mags / 3 grenades / FURY / DYNAMITE, Set\n1218\t  hostages 0–5, Play ending (n), Play cutscene (each).\n1219\t- **Data (designer tool):** COPY SPAWN LINE and COPY PROP LINE print a ready-to-paste stage entry for the point under the\n1220\t  crosshair (`['rifleman', { lx: 42, dz: 180 }]`, `['crate', 'c?', 1234, -120]`) to the console and an on-screen toast.\n1221\t- **Reset:** RESET TO DEFAULTS (sliders), RESET SAVE (high scores, unlocks, tips seen).\n1222\t\n1223\t---\n1224\t\n1225\t## 12. Attract mode and the bot\n1226\t\n1227\t### 12.1 Attract mode (`81-attract.js`)\n1228\t\n1229\t- On `title` (and every menu screen reached from it), `E.Arcade` with `{ idle: 10, demo: 150, scores: 6 }` counts idle\n1230\t  time. After **10 s** without input it enters `demo`: the attract scene plays a looping **playlist** of each op's\n1231\t  `attract` segments (Op 1 from b4 25 s → Op 2 boss 25 s → Op 3 b14 20 s → Op 4 b11 20 s → Op 5 breakout 25 s → Op 6 part\n1232\t  B and the boss 30 s), each starting by `jump` with cheats on (god, infinite ammo) and the bot playing P1. Then the\n1233\t  high-score table (6 s), then the title, again and again.\n1234\t- A banner reads \"DEMO PLAY · PRESS ANY BUTTON\", and the HUD runs as in play. Audio stays at half volume (and silent until\n1235\t  the page has had a gesture: browsers require it).\n1236\t- **Any input** (a key, a mouse move or click, a pad button or stick) calls `arcade.wake()` and returns to the title with\n1237\t  the menu focused.\n1238\t- It also runs on touch-only devices (14.1), where taps don't count as input to stop it.\n1239\t\n1240\t### 12.2 The bot (`80-bot.js`)\n1241\t\n1242\t`WP.Bot.frame(world, pid, dt) → InputFrame`. One bot serves the attract mode, the dev autopilot and the playthrough\n1243\ttests.\n1244\t\n1245\t- **Target choice** (every .1 s): projectiles that will hit within .8 s, then telegraphs by time left, then vehicle and\n1246\t  boss weak points, then the nearest hostiles, then pickups when low on ammo or health, then props near hostiles\n1247\t  (barrels).\n1248\t- **Aim:** a critically damped spring toward the target's body center (the head for BRUTES and TUSK), at most 900 px/s\n1249\t  (attract) or 600 px/s (`fair` mode, for the tests).\n1250\t- **Fire** when the crosshair is inside the target's shape, but **never** when the frontmost shape at the aim point is a\n1251\t  civilian, hostage or animal-in-the-way (re-check every shot; side-step 10 px).\n1252\t- **Grenades:** at 3+ hostiles within the blast radius, or at a vehicle or boss weak point, with no friendly inside 1.2 ×\n1253\t  radius.\n1254\t- **Reload** when the magazine is under 6 and nothing will fire within .9 s.\n1255\t- **Mistakes** (`fair` mode only): a reaction delay of .15–.3 s and a .5% chance a shot misses by 12 px, so the tests\n1256\t  measure a beatable game, not a perfect machine.\n1257\t\n1258\t---\n1259\t\n1260\t## 13. Multiplayer\n1261\t\n1262\t### 13.1 Local co-op (the game on its own)\n1263\t\n1264\t- `game.allowJoin({ max: 4, onJoin })`: Options on a controller nobody holds joins (anywhere on the title, squad, map or\n1265\t  in play). P1 keeps the keyboard, mouse and first pad. Joining mid-op starts with 6 magazines, 4 grenades and damage 0,\n1266\t  and the scaling of 7.16 updates at the next beat.\n1267\t- Every player has their own crosshair, HUD panel, ammo, grenades, damage, score and streak. Quotas and hostages are\n1268\t  shared. A player who disconnects mid-run is paused out (the engine pauses on a lost controller); \"DROP OUT\" in the pause\n1269\t  menu removes them.\n1270\t- Colors: `E.PLAYER_COLORS` locally (P1 blue, P2 red, P3 green, P4 yellow).\n1271\t\n1272\t### 13.2 AI Hub sessions (`90-net.js`, `91-codec.js`): Session Protocol v1, mode `shared-world`\n1273\t\n1274\t**Head of the bundled page, in this order:**\n1275\t\n1276\t```html\n1277\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n1278\t<script>/* hub/session.js, byte for byte, unmodified */</script>\n1279\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n1280\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n1281\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n1282\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Clear the operation as a team; top score wins\">\n1283\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Aim: mouse or stick · Fire: click/R2 · Grenade: right click/L2 · Reload: R/□\">\n1284\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"5\">\n1285\t<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\"><meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1–4\">\n1286\t<meta name=\"hub:genre\" content=\"Shooter\"><meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"Operation Wolf\"><meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"(the builder's model)\">\n1287\t```\n1288\t\n1289\t**Joining:**\n1290\t- When `AIHub.active` is true (decided before the game builds), create the game with `autoPause: false` and\n1291\t  `menu: { pauses: false, quit: false, items: [] }`. Make `play` non-pausable, disable `allowJoin`, and skip the title,\n1292\t  attract mode, briefing, map and tips.\n1293\t- `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. With `null`, run as if standalone.\n1294\t- The op is `1 + floor(AIHub.rng('stage')() * 6)`, played standalone (default loadout; 5 hostages for Ops 5 and 6; no\n1295\t  perks). The host's sim seed is `floor(AIHub.rng('sim')() * 2^32)`.\n1296\t- Session tempo: rail speed ×1.3 and every hold's `max` ×.6, so an op with its boss takes about 4 minutes (the meta\n1297\t  says 5, to leave margin).\n1298\t- Call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as the op is built, with no key press.\n1299\t\n1300\t**Our card (`hubcard` scene, `card: true`):** the logo; the op's name and card line; the players in seat colors\n1301\t(`info.players[i].color`), each with READY ticks from the `card` event; the goal; this device's controls (from\n1302\t`input.label`); the time left (`card.left`; PAUSED when `paused`). **Enter / ✕ / a click on READY** →\n1303\t`AIHub.answer('ready')`. **△ / M / a click on MORE TIME** → `AIHub.answer('more')` (pressing again takes it back). The\n1304\tcard has no menus or settings, and its cosmetic randomness comes from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n1305\t\n1306\t**Start:** on `start`, show 3-2-1 from `AIHub.time()`; play begins when `AIHub.time() >= 0`. The HUD shows TIME from\n1307\t`AIHub.limitMs - AIHub.time()`.\n1308\t\n1309\t**Roles:**\n1310\t- **The host** (`AIHub.isHost`) runs `WP.Sim` with one player slot per `info.players` entry: its own from local input,\n1311\t  the others from the network. With **`AIHub.server`** (a host with no player of its own), there is no local player,\n1312\t  input or camera, and it draws nothing.\n1313\t- **Clients** run `WP.Mirror`: they draw the world from snapshots, move their own crosshair locally at once, and play their\n1314\t  own muzzle flashes, tracers, sounds, hit sparks and hit markers at once (predicted). Kills, pickups and damage come only\n1315\t  from the host.\n1316\t\n1317\t**Messages** (JSON with short keys; at most 18 a second from any copy, counting everything; a token bucket in `91-codec.js`\n1318\tmirrors the client's limit of 20/s with bursts of 40):\n1319\t\n1320\t| Name | Direction | Delivery | Rate | Contents |\n1321\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1322\t| `i` (input) | client → host | unreliable | 15/s | `{ k:'i', s: seq, a: [x*10|0, y*10|0], b: fireBit, g: grenadeCount, r: reloadCount, n: roundsFired, h: [[seq, [[id, part, dmg], …]], …] }`: the hit batches the host hasn't acked yet (at most 3, so a loss is covered) |\n1323\t| `s` (snapshot) | host → all | unreliable | 15/s | `{ k:'s', t: simMs, d: railD, q: quotas, p: [[pid, x, y, dmg, mag, spares, gren, score, flags]], e: [[id, typeCode, x, y, z, facing16, state, hp%]], j: [[id, kind, x, y, z]], u: [[id, kind, x, y, z]], ack: { pid: seq } }` |\n1324\t| `ev` (events) | host → all | reliable | ≤ 3/s, batched | `{ k:'ev', l: [[type, …args], …] }`: spawn, kill (id, by, part), pickup (id, pid, kind), damage (pid, amount, from), explode, telegraph, radio, boss phase, hostage, clear, fail |\n1325\t\n1326\t- **Size guard:** every unreliable message stays under 1100 bytes, because larger ones travel as several packets and are\n1327\t  lost whole. Quantize to integers and keep keys short. If a snapshot is too big, leave out pickups, then props, then the\n1328\t  farthest entities, round-robin, so each still updates at ≥ 5/s. Over 16 KB is impossible by construction; assert it.\n1329\t- **Hits are the client's call, checked by the host:** a client tests its shots against its interpolated world and\n1330\t  reports the target ids and parts. The host applies them when the target is alive and the report is less than 400 ms old\n1331\t  (co-op, so be generous). The host deducts ammo from `n` and handles grenade and reload counts by their difference. Each\n1332\t  pickup goes to the first reporter.\n1333\t- **Interpolation:** draw remote entities 100 ms behind (`AIHub.time() - 100`), interpolating linearly between snapshots.\n1334\t  Create entities from `spawn` events (types and rigs), play deaths from `kill` events, and drop an entity missing for 3\n1335\t  snapshots.\n1336\t- **Reporting:** the host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won, stats, awards })` once: when the op is cleared\n1337\t  (`won: true`), when everyone is DOWN (`won: false`), or on **`time-up`** at once (`won: false` unless cleared). Standings\n1338\t  are player ids sorted by score, best first (ties share an array), listing every player still in. Stats per player:\n1339\t  kills, accuracy, headshots, intercepts, civilians hit. Awards: SHARPSHOOTER (best accuracy), GUARDIAN (most intercepts),\n1340\t  LIFESAVER (most hostages escorted, or civilians spared).\n1341\t- **`leave`:** the host removes that player's slot, and their crosshair fades on every copy. A host leaving ends the round\n1342\t  (the hub voids it).\n1343\t- **`end`:** stop all input, sound and music (`audio.music(null)`, mute effects), freeze the frame, and send nothing\n1344\t  more.\n1345\t- **Rules for sessions:** no network but `AIHub.send`; no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation; quit,\n1346\t  restart and title do nothing (they're hidden); no chat; names come from the hub and are drawn with the pixel font only\n1347\t  (anything outside ASCII falls back to \"P1\"–\"P4\"); never pause the sim (the menu overlays it); the tab hidden on the host\n1348\t  keeps simulating.\n1349\t\n1350\t---\n1351\t\n1352\t## 14. Touch-only devices, About/Credits, exit interview\n1353\t\n1354\t### 14.1 Touch-only devices\n1355\t\n1356\tAt boot, and whenever input changes: `touchOnly = matchMedia('(any-pointer: coarse)').matches &&\n1357\t!matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0 && no gamepad connected && no key pressed\n1358\tyet`. While it holds: no touch controls (`input.touchEnabled = false`, no `touchButtons`); the title shows a panel\n1359\t\"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\" with a large **SETTINGS** button (`game.menu('settings')`) and the engine's corner menu\n1360\tbutton; the attract mode starts after 10 s and loops, and taps don't stop it. A `gamepadconnected` or `keydown` leaves\n1361\ttouch-only mode and shows the normal title.\n1362\t\n1363\t### 14.2 About/Credits (`about` scene; the same text goes in the chat reply)\n1364\t\n1365\tPages, left/right to turn, ○ to leave:\n1366\t1. **SOURCE INFORMATION (1/2):** Date `2026-11-03 17:47:46`; Source: Operation Wolf (Taito, 1987); Plan: `PLAN.md`;\n1367\t   Genre and perspective: light-gun rail shooter, first person on a scripted rail; Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the full\n1368\t   engine with Mode 7, Arcade and Shell; the version of every edit noted), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, Playwright\n1369\t   (tests), Node (tests and build).\n1370\t2. **SOURCE INFORMATION (2/2):** Art direction; Animation; Audio; Online (AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world co-op\n1371\t   for 1–4; local co-op for 1–4); Testing (what was allowed and used); Research (the planner: Wikipedia and\n1372\t   arcade-history.com on Operation Wolf, plus the engine's and hub's docs; the builder adds their own or \"none\"); Environment\n1373\t   (Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown, or what was used); Model; Usage (an estimate, or \"unknown\").\n1374\t3. **TESTING FEEDBACK:** the four answers.\n1375\t4. **ENGINE FEEDBACK:** the six answers.\n1376\t5. **PROMPT FEEDBACK:** the four answers.\n1377\t6. **CREDITS:** \"OPERATION WOLFPACK, an original game inspired by Operation Wolf (Taito, 1987). Not affiliated with or\n1378\t   endorsed by Taito.\" The engine my-3D2dge (MIT, michaelcrosato), the AI Hub client (michaelcrosato), any CC0 store\n1379\t   assets used (with their credit lines), and the model and harness that built it.\n1380\t\n1381\tFill every field with what is true at the end of the build; write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm. `WP.TEXT.about`\n1382\tholds the text, and the build fails if a field is empty.\n1383\t\n1384\t### 14.3 Exit interview\n1385\t\n1386\tWrite `./exit-interview.json` in the exact shape TASK.md gives. Suggested `aiHub` values: name \"Operation Wolfpack\";\n1387\ttagline \"Every bullet counts. Bring them home.\"; description \"A first-person light-gun rail shooter for 1–4 players:\n1388\tstorm the Brimstone Coast with limited ammo, spare the civilians and rescue five hostages from the Hyena Legion.\"; type\n1389\t\"Game\"; genre \"Shooter\"; source \"Operation Wolf\"; series \"\" (the franchise has the source's own name); players \"1–4\";\n1390\tcontrols \"Mouse or stick aims · click/R2 fires · right click/L2 grenade · R/□ reload\"; tags [\"first-person\", \"arcade\",\n1391\t\"co-op\", \"pixel art\", \"retro\", \"boss fights\"]. `tests/run.mjs` parses the file and checks every key is there.\n1392\t\n1393\t---\n1394\t\n1395\t## 15. Build order and milestones\n1396\t\n1397\tEach milestone ends with the test command green (`npm test`) and the listed checks. Build systems before content, and Op\n1398\t1 completely before the other ops.\n1399\t\n1400\t| # | Milestone | Build | Exit criteria |\n1401\t|---|---|---|---|\n1402\t| **M0** | Setup and spike (**de-risk the renderer, hits and bundle first**) | the dev folder; the engine and hub copies; `manifest.json`; `dev/index.html`; a Mode 7 test scene: floor painter, Backdrop, 30 Humanoids at depths 60–900, a jeep shape driving, palms; the mouse crosshair; hit shapes with the debug overlay; rig height calibration (`WP.RIG_H`); `tools/build.mjs` producing the single file with session.js and the metas; `tests/run.mjs` skeleton | a screenshot shows correct depth scaling; hit shapes line up with rigs at 4 depths and in 3 poses (screenshot); the bundle opens over file:// with no errors; the harness loads the bundle (a stub `connect`/`ready`) |\n1403\t| **M1** | Core loop | input adapters (mouse, pad, keys), aim assist, the weapon (fire, bloom, magazines, reload, auto-reload), grenades and explosions, RIFLEMAN (cross, popup) with telegraph and fire, the damage meter and DOWN, pickups (MAG, GRENADE, RATION), crates and barrels, FX v1 (dust, sparks, explosion), the gun overlay, HUD v1, SFX v1; the `range` scene | the range is playable for 2 minutes; T-core, T-proj, T-weapon, T-hit, T-input pass |\n1404\t| **M2** | The stage framework and Op 1 | the stage schema, rail and holds, beats and spawns, quotas and reinforcements, layout helpers and floor painters, the Op 1 shapes, GRENADIER, KNIFE, OFFICER, SNIPER, MORTAR, BRUTE, PARATROOPER, jeep, truck, VULTURE, the grenade, knife, rocket, missile and mortar projectiles, FURY, props (sandbags, masts), BIG EAR; the radio and voice v1; music `op1`; the op card, tally and continue | Op 1 plays from the card to the tally; T-enemy-*, T-boss-1 and T-stage-1 (god bot, then fair bot on RECRUIT) pass |\n1405\t| **M3** | The game's frame | title (logo art), menus, settings, glyph default and the mirror, pause items, help, briefing, map, high scores (`E.Arcade`), continue, the ending skeleton for all 6 variants, About, the attract mode with the bot, touch-only mode, the dev screen (engine changes 2–4) | the title → Op 1 → tally → map flow works; attract starts at 10 s and any input ends it; dev sliders change play live and reset; T-flow (partial), T-attract, T-touch, T-dev pass |\n1406\t| **M4** | Multiplayer | local co-op (join, panels, crosshairs, shared quotas, DOWN and return); AI Hub: card, roles, codec, rate limiter, interpolation, server mode, time-up, leave, end, finish | T-coop and T-hub-mock pass; **the real harness passes** in all 4 configurations (17.3) |\n1407\t| **M5** | Op 2 and the interrogation | the river floor and forward rail, bob, skiffs, patrol boat, the bridge, carriers in trees, CROCODILE, the interrogation cutscene, music `op2` | T-stage-2, T-boss-2, the cutscene test |\n1408\t| **M6** | Ops 3 and 4 | windows and doors (clip), civilians and their penalties, the reporter, RPG, APC, DYNAMITE, WARTHOG and the village perk; the depot, chains, the cargo plane, forklift, IRON HOG and the refill perk; music `op3`, `op4` | T-stage-3/4, T-boss-3/4, T-perks |\n1409\t| **M7** | Ops 5 and 6 and the endings | the darkness mask, searchlights and SPOTTED, rain, FLARE, the breakout escort, TUSK; the airfield, tank, the boarding escort, the part B cut, altitude Mode 7, HYENA ONE; all endings, credits, loop 2; music `op5`, `op6`, `ending` | T-stage-5/6, T-boss-5/6, T-endings, **T-playthrough** (the whole campaign, headless) |\n1410\t| **M8** | Polish and balance | the full audio pass (every song, sound and voice), animation polish (9.2 list, filmstrips), FX polish, the HUD and 10-foot pass, aim assist tuning in the range, balance from bot statistics (damage taken per op, quota ÷ spawns, ammo curve: no fair-bot DRY on VETERAN), the attract playlist finished, the About text | every op looks right in screenshots (a list: 17.4); a fair bot finishes VETERAN with ≥ 3 hostages in ≥ 2 of 3 seeds; no look notes from `check.mjs` left unhandled |\n1411\t| **M9** | Ship | the final bundle; the whole test command; the harness; the browser smoke on the final file; `exit-interview.json`; the About pages filled; the chat reply | section 18's checklist is all ticked |\n1412\t\n1413\t---\n1414\t\n1415\t## 16. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1416\t\n1417\t| Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk |\n1418\t|---|---|---|\n1419\t| **Mode 7 as a first-person gallery** (scale, sorting, cost) | It was built for karts: rigs at k up to ~4, big set pieces, many shapes; anchors that sort wrongly; the shape sprite cache churning (300 entries) | M0 spike with screenshots at 4 depths; scenery at fixed depth keeps the same k (cache hits); raise the cache size in the engine if needed; give covers and openings their own depth bias; test the worst screen (Op 4 chains + 40 entities) early. Performance has no budget, but frames must still be drawn correctly |\n1420\t| **Hit shapes not matching what is drawn** | Rig heights vary by preset and pose; Mode 7 quantizes the view's scale | calibrate (7.2) instead of guessing; the debug overlay; a test that projects a known rig and checks the head shape lies in the top 15% of its drawn box (using the calibration table) |\n1421\t| **Lighting under Mode 7** | Mode 7 draws as an overlay, so the engine's `game.lights` and particles don't apply | own world FX through `m7.add` and an own screen-space darkness mask with dithered light holes (`px.ddisc`), planned from M1 (FX) and M7 (night); verify Op 5's readability by screenshot |\n1422\t| **Netcode in a shared world** | Rate limits, 1100-byte unreliable messages, host leave, server mode, interpolation | the protocol in 13.2 is the design; M4 builds a Node mock bus first (latency, jitter, loss) with assertions on rate and size, then the real harness in all configurations before any more content |\n1423\t| **Session rules colliding with engine defaults** | The engine pauses on hidden tabs and menus, offers Quit, and may use storage | engine change 3 (non-pausing menu), `autoPause: false`, menu items hidden in sessions; T-hub checks that nothing pauses the host sim |\n1424\t| **Pad aiming feels bad** | A stick is not a light gun | the range scene with a time-to-target readout; acceleration, friction, magnetism and snap; difficulty-scaled assist; tune in M1 and again in M8 |\n1425\t| **Gibberish voices and synthesized guns sound cheap** | Everything is chip synthesis | a dev soundboard (dev screen: PLAY SOUND select) from M1; layered sounds; the per-letter voice hook from M2 |\n1426\t| **Content volume** (6 ops, 6 bosses, about 90 beats) | Time, and stubs creeping in | data-first stage files, beat macros and layout helpers; finish Op 1 to \"done\" in M2 so later ops copy a working pattern; a test that every beat of every op fires and every op clears |\n1427\t| **Bundling** | `session.js` must be first and unmodified; `</script>` inside inlined code breaks the page | the bundler escapes `</script` as `<\\/script` in inlined code only (never inside session.js; check it has none) and compares session.js's hash; T-bundle |\n1428\t| **Determinism drift** | Rigs or FX reading the sim's random stream; `Math.random` sneaking in | separate streams (`sim`, `loot`, `ai`, `fx`); a test that runs the same seed twice and compares a hash of the snapshots; a lint step in `run.mjs` that fails on any `Math.random` in `src/` |\n1429\t| **Touch detection false positives** | Touch laptops have fine pointers and keyboards | the `any-pointer: fine` check, recovery on keydown or gamepadconnected; T-touch with stubbed `matchMedia` |\n1430\t| **Disk space** | `/tmp` was full when this was planned | keep clones, Playwright output and temp files in the dev folder (`TMPDIR=./.tmp` for the test runs) |\n1431\t\n1432\t---\n1433\t\n1434\t## 17. Testing\n1435\t\n1436\t### 17.1 The one command\n1437\t\n1438\t`npm test` (= `node tests/run.mjs`) prints **only failures** and then **one line**: `412 passed, 0 failed (38.2 s)`.\n1439\tOptions: `--quick` (headless suites only), `--only <suite>` (for example `--only weapon`), and `--changed` (only the suites\n1440\twhose `covers` files changed since the last green run; a stamp file in `tests/.last`). Rerun a suite only after changing\n1441\tcode it covers. Each suite declares `covers: ['src/31-weapon.js', …]`. As TASK.md says, don't use subagents or workflows\n1442\tto debate, review, judge or audit; the tests and your own screenshots are the checks.\n1443\t\n1444\tHeadless suites load `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and the `src/` files from `manifest.json` into a `node:vm` context with small\n1445\tstand-ins (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`, `navigator`, `matchMedia`, `performance`), as the handoff's\n1446\t`game/test.mjs` and `kits/test.mjs` do. Then they drive the game with `game.advance(seconds)`, `input.tap/hold/feed`,\n1447\tinjected frames (`game.debug.frames`), and read `game.debug.snapshot()`. Every suite also fails on `game.errors`.\n1448\t\n1449\t### 17.2 Suites (what each proves)\n1450\t\n1451\t| Suite | Checks |\n1452\t|---|---|\n1453\t| T-core | fixed-step determinism: two runs, same seed and the same frames, give the same snapshot hash after 60 s of bot play; no `Math.random` anywhere in `src/` (lint) |\n1454\t| T-proj | `project` and `toFloor` round trips; `halfWidth`; a rig's hit shapes against its calibrated drawn box at depths 60/200/400/800 and in 3 poses |\n1455\t| T-input | mouse (`input.feed('move')`) moves the crosshair absolutely; keyboard movement from `held` codes; stick velocity through an injected stick; aim assist friction and snap pick the right target; `input.label('fire')` gives \"R2\" (PlayStation), \"RT\" (Xbox) and \"Left click\" (mouse) |\n1456\t| T-weapon | 11 rounds in a second held; magazine count; auto-reload after .12 s and a 1.0 s reload; part-used magazines kept; empty clicks; FURY doubles the rate and uses no ammo; bloom stays ≤ 7 px |\n1457\t| T-hit | head vs body vs legs; a headshot ×2 (×4 on BRUTE); cover blocks; nearest first; projectiles intercepted; pickups go to the shooter; the floor puff on misses |\n1458\t| T-grenade | the count; range clamp; the blast kills inside the radius and spares outside; vehicles take damage; civilians inside are penalized; barrel chains |\n1459\t| T-enemy-<type> | every type in 8.4 and 8.5: spawns, telegraphs (ring time per difficulty), fires (ignored → damage rises by the expected amount ± the accuracy roll with a fixed seed), dies when shot, counts toward the right quota; OFFICER calls 3 (2 after the perk); paratrooper chute; vehicles' weak points and wrecks |\n1460\t| T-friendlies | civilian hit: +8 damage, −1000, streak reset; hostage grab and recapture; lost and rescued counts; animals drop and flee, never die |\n1461\t| T-pickups | each effect; expiry at 6 s; the supply director's weights move with need; the emergency drop by difficulty; the DRY rule (DOWN on ARCADE) |\n1462\t| T-boss-1…6 | each boss's phases advance when its weak points die (`debug.tune('oneHit')` or targeted frames); armored parts take no damage; defeat leads to the tally |\n1463\t| T-stage-1…6 | with the god bot: every beat fires, every hold releases, the quotas reach 0, the boss comes, the op clears within its time budget; with damage off for vehicles, the reinforcement loop spawns vehicles until the quota is met |\n1464\t| T-perks | quotas ×.8 after Op 1; −40 after Op 3; the refill and pouch +2 after Op 4; n hostages carried into Op 6 |\n1465\t| T-flow | title → briefing (skip) → map → opcard → play → tally → … → ending → credits → initials → title; continue restores the op-start state; all 6 endings by hostage count; loop 2 raises the multipliers; Mission Select unlocks after a clear |\n1466\t| T-cutscenes | each cutscene runs to its end at speed and can be skipped by holding confirm |\n1467\t| T-coop | `game.addPlayer({ pad: 1 })` gives a second player; separate ammo and damage; pickups to the shooter; quotas scale; DOWN, then back at the next op with 50; all DOWN → continue |\n1468\t| T-attract | 10 s idle on the title → demo; the bot kills enemies and hits no civilian or hostage across the whole playlist; `tap('confirm')` or a mouse move returns to the title; the scores table shows |\n1469\t| T-touch | with stubbed `matchMedia` and `maxTouchPoints`: the notice and the settings button show, taps don't start a game, attract runs; a keydown turns it off |\n1470\t| T-dev | the pause menu has DEV MODE; changing `spawnDensity` to 2 doubles a beat's spawns; `railSpeed` changes the time to reach a beat; RESET TO DEFAULTS restores every slider; JUMP reaches the right op and beat; the cheats work |\n1471\t| T-hub-mock | a Node mock of `AIHub` (connect, ready, card, start, send, on, time, rng, finish) with an in-memory bus (150 ms latency, 50 jitter, 5% loss), 1 host and 3 clients: clients see the host's entities within 250 ms; client hits kill on the host; every unreliable message < 1100 bytes; ≤ 18 messages a second per copy; time-up → exactly one `finish`; a leave removes a slot; server mode runs with no local player; `end` stops input and sound |\n1472\t| T-bundle | the final file exists with the exact name; session.js is the first script right after `<meta charset>`, byte-identical to `hub/session.js`; all `hub:` metas are present; no `WebSocket`, `RTCPeerConnection`, `fetch(`, `XMLHttpRequest`, `alert(`, `confirm(`, `prompt(`, `window.open` in the game's code; `exit-interview.json` parses with every key and no empty value |\n1473\t| T-playthrough | **the whole game:** a fair bot on RECRUIT, no cheats, from the title (press start) through all 6 ops, the cutscenes and the ending, to the initials; asserts the ending is reached, the rank exists, ≥ 3 hostages, no errors. A god-bot run on VETERAN asserts the same, faster |\n1474\t| T-browser (not in `--quick`) | Playwright on the **final file** over `file://`: boot with no console errors; the title canvas isn't empty; attract after 10 s; deep links `#op1`…`#op6`, `#ending/5` load and report the right `debug.snapshot().scene`; `node engine/tools/check.mjs <final>.html#op1` passes with no errors |\n1475\t| T-hub-harness (not in `--quick`) | 17.3 |\n1476\t\n1477\t### 17.3 The real AI Hub harness\n1478\t\n1479\tCopy the final .html and `hub/harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` into `tests/.serve/`. Start\n1480\t`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there, read the port from its first line, and **keep its PID**. With\n1481\tPlaywright, open `http://127.0.0.1:PORT/harness.html?game=<final>.html&…` for each configuration:\n1482\t`players=1&auto=1`, `players=2&auto=1`, `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`,\n1483\t`players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1`, `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. Wait for\n1484\t`document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. First confirm that the frames\n1485\thold our game (`document.title` is \"Operation Wolfpack\" inside a frame) before trusting a result. Print the checklist only\n1486\ton failure. Stop the server by its PID, and only that one: never `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k`, or kill whatever holds a\n1487\tport.\n1488\t\n1489\t### 17.4 Screenshots (only for what a script can't check)\n1490\t\n1491\tLook, readability at 10 feet, animation quality and lighting. Use `node engine/tools/check.mjs` and\n1492\t`node engine/tools/filmstrip.mjs` on deep links into `shots/`, and review: each op's opening screen, each boss, the\n1493\tbreakout at night, the takeoff at altitude, the HUD with 1 and 4 players, the title, the map, the tally, the About pages,\n1494\tthe hub card, the touch notice, plus filmstrips of a rifleman's death, a grenade throw, a knife throw, the reload, an\n1495\texplosion and the mast toppling. Act on every look note `check.mjs` prints. Retake a screenshot only after changing what\n1496\tit shows.\n1497\t\n1498\t---\n1499\t\n1500\t## 18. Definition of done\n1501\t\n1502\t- [ ] `./OperationWolfpack-OperationWolf-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174746.html` is one file that runs over `file://`\n1503\t      and in the AI Hub harness; every dev file is in the dev folder.\n1504\t- [ ] Every system in section 7 and every screen in section 10 works; all six operations, six bosses, every cutscene in\n1505\t      8.8 and all six endings play; no TODO, placeholder text or stubbed feature (`run.mjs` fails on `TODO|FIXME|placeholder|lorem` in\n1506\t      `src/` and on an empty `WP.TEXT` value).\n1507\t- [ ] Keyboard and mouse, keyboard only and a standard pad all play the whole game; prompts follow the last device;\n1508\t      PlayStation glyphs by default and Xbox in Settings; the mouse hovers and clicks every menu.\n1509\t- [ ] Attract mode starts after 10 s idle on the title and menus, shows every op, and stops on any input; touch-only\n1510\t      devices show the notice, the settings button and the attract mode.\n1511\t- [ ] The dev mode opens from the pause menu, with live sliders (11.1), reset to defaults, toggles, jumps, spawns and the\n1512\t      data tools.\n1513\t- [ ] Local co-op for 1–4 and AI Hub shared-world sessions for 1–4; the harness passes in all five configurations.\n1514\t- [ ] All music, sound and voices are synthesized in code (no audio files); voices are gibberish with subtitles.\n1515\t- [ ] `npm test` is green: failures only, plus one count line; the headless whole-game playthrough passes.\n1516\t- [ ] The About/Credits screen and the chat reply carry Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt\n1517\t      Feedback (\"unknown\" where you can't confirm); `./exit-interview.json` parses in the exact shape.\n1518\t- [ ] `engine/CHANGES.md` lists every engine edit; the research clone and any servers you started are cleaned up.\n1519\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0704575-f16b-44ea-a24d-907e9c278025","uuid":"33dbf999-ecbb-403f-b17a-001ad8b70381","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:30:30.789Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183009__xe162c9/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 11. Dev mode (`73-devmode.js`)\n\nReached from the pause menu (DEV MODE). It is an `E.Shell` screen built with the rows extension (engine change 2), so it\nworks with the pad, keys and mouse like the rest of the menu. In hub sessions it is hidden.\n\n### 11.1 Live sliders (the important balance variables)\n\nEach is a setting in group `Dev` (hidden from Settings) whose `apply` writes `WP.T[key]` at once, even mid-fight.\n**RESET TO DEFAULTS** is `settings.reset('Dev')`. While any value differs from its default, the HUD shows a small \"DEV\"\nbadge.\n\n| Key | Label | Default | Range |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `fireRate` | Fire rate (rounds/s) | 11 | 4–24 |\n| `magSize` | Magazine size | 30 | 10–60 |\n| `reloadTime` | Reload time (s) | 1.0 | .2–3 |\n| `bulletDmg` | Bullet damage | 1 | .5–4 |\n| `bloomMax` | Max spread (px) | 7 | 0–20 |\n| `startMags` | Starting magazines | 6 | 1–15 |\n| `startGrenades` | Starting grenades | 4 | 0–9 |\n| `grenadeRadius` | Grenade radius | 52 | 20–140 |\n| `grenadeDmg` | Grenade damage | 12 | 2–40 |\n| `assist` | Aim assist strength | .6 | 0–1 |\n| `padSpeed` | Pad crosshair speed (px/s) | 520 | 150–1000 |\n| `enemyHp` | Enemy HP × | 1 | .25–4 |\n| `enemyAccuracy` | Enemy accuracy × | 1 | 0–2 |\n| `telegraph` | Telegraph time × | 1 | .3–2.5 |\n| `enemyDamage` | Enemy damage × | 1 | 0–3 |\n| `spawnDensity` | Spawn density × | 1 | .25–2.5 |\n| `projectileSpeed` | Projectile speed × | 1 | .5–2 |\n| `railSpeed` | Rail speed × | 1 | .25–3 |\n| `quota` | Quotas × | 1 | .25–2 |\n| `dropChance` | Drop chance × | 1 | 0–3 |\n| `civilianDamage` | Civilian hit damage | 8 | 0–30 |\n| `clearHeal` | Stage-clear heal | 10 | 0–100 |\n| `timeScale` | Game speed | 1 | .1–2 |\n\n### 11.2 Toggles, tools and actions\n\n- **Cheats:** God mode, Infinite ammo, Infinite grenades, One-hit kills, Enemies hold fire, Bot autopilot (P1).\n- **View:** Show hit shapes, Show paths and spawn markers, Perf overlay (frame ms, entities, particles, rail d, beat,\n  seed), Slow motion (1, .5, .25, .1), Frame step (while paused: STEP ONE FRAME).\n- **Jump:** an operation select (1–6), a beat select (that op's beats, plus BOSS and, for Op 6, PART B), GO. Also RANGE (a\n  target-practice scene with dummies at depths 60–600, a moving target, a projectile thrower, a civilian walker, and a\n  readout of time-to-target).\n- **Spawn:** a type select (every `WP.TYPES` id) → SPAWN AT CROSSHAIR. It takes the floor point under P1's crosshair and\n  converts it to the camera frame.\n- **Flow:** Fill quotas, Trigger boss, Kill all, Damage self 25, Heal, Give 3 mags / 3 grenades / FURY / DYNAMITE, Set\n  hostages 0–5, Play ending (n), Play cutscene (each).\n- **Data (designer tool):** COPY SPAWN LINE and COPY PROP LINE print a ready-to-paste stage entry for the point under the\n  crosshair (`['rifleman', { lx: 42, dz: 180 }]`, `['crate', 'c?', 1234, -120]`) to the console and an on-screen toast.\n- **Reset:** RESET TO DEFAULTS (sliders), RESET SAVE (high scores, unlocks, tips seen).\n\n---\n\n## 12. Attract mode and the bot\n\n### 12.1 Attract mode (`81-attract.js`)\n\n- On `title` (and every menu screen reached from it), `E.Arcade` with `{ idle: 10, demo: 150, scores: 6 }` counts idle\n  time. After **10 s** without input it enters `demo`: the attract scene plays a looping **playlist** of each op's\n  `attract` segments (Op 1 from b4 25 s → Op 2 boss 25 s → Op 3 b14 20 s → Op 4 b11 20 s → Op 5 breakout 25 s → Op 6 part\n  B and the boss 30 s), each starting by `jump` with cheats on (god, infinite ammo) and the bot playing P1. Then the\n  high-score table (6 s), then the title, again and again.\n- A banner reads \"DEMO PLAY · PRESS ANY BUTTON\", and the HUD runs as in play. Audio stays at half volume (and silent until\n  the page has had a gesture: browsers require it).\n- **Any input** (a key, a mouse move or click, a pad button or stick) calls `arcade.wake()` and returns to the title with\n  the menu focused.\n- It also runs on touch-only devices (14.1), where taps don't count as input to stop it.\n\n### 12.2 The bot (`80-bot.js`)\n\n`WP.Bot.frame(world, pid, dt) → InputFrame`. One bot serves the attract mode, the dev autopilot and the playthrough\ntests.\n\n- **Target choice** (every .1 s): projectiles that will hit within .8 s, then telegraphs by time left, then vehicle and\n  boss weak points, then the nearest hostiles, then pickups when low on ammo or health, then props near hostiles\n  (barrels).\n- **Aim:** a critically damped spring toward the target's body center (the head for BRUTES and TUSK), at most 900 px/s\n  (attract) or 600 px/s (`fair` mode, for the tests).\n- **Fire** when the crosshair is inside the target's shape, but **never** when the frontmost shape at the aim point is a\n  civilian, hostage or animal-in-the-way (re-check every shot; side-step 10 px).\n- **Grenades:** at 3+ hostiles within the blast radius, or at a vehicle or boss weak point, with no friendly inside 1.2 ×\n  radius.\n- **Reload** when the magazine is under 6 and nothing will fire within .9 s.\n- **Mistakes** (`fair` mode only): a reaction delay of .15–.3 s and a .5% chance a shot misses by 12 px, so the tests\n  measure a beatable game, not a perfect machine.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Multiplayer\n\n### 13.1 Local co-op (the game on its own)\n\n- `game.allowJoin({ max: 4, onJoin })`: Options on a controller nobody holds joins (anywhere on the title, squad, map or\n  in play). P1 keeps the keyboard, mouse and first pad. Joining mid-op starts with 6 magazines, 4 grenades and damage 0,\n  and the scaling of 7.16 updates at the next beat.\n- Every player has their own crosshair, HUD panel, ammo, grenades, damage, score and streak. Quotas and hostages are\n  shared. A player who disconnects mid-run is paused out (the engine pauses on a lost controller); \"DROP OUT\" in the pause\n  menu removes them.\n- Colors: `E.PLAYER_COLORS` locally (P1 blue, P2 red, P3 green, P4 yellow).\n\n### 13.2 AI Hub sessions (`90-net.js`, `91-codec.js`): Session Protocol v1, mode `shared-world`\n\n**Head of the bundled page, in this order:**\n\n```html\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>/* hub/session.js, byte for byte, unmodified */</script>\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Clear the operation as a team; top score wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Aim: mouse or stick · Fire: click/R2 · Grenade: right click/L2 · Reload: R/□\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"5\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\"><meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1–4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:genre\" content=\"Shooter\"><meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"Operation Wolf\"><meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"(the builder's model)\">\n```\n\n**Joining:**\n- When `AIHub.active` is true (decided before the game builds), create the game with `autoPause: false` and\n  `menu: { pauses: false, quit: false, items: [] }`. Make `play` non-pausable, disable `allowJoin`, and skip the title,\n  attract mode, briefing, map and tips.\n- `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. With `null`, run as if standalone.\n- The op is `1 + floor(AIHub.rng('stage')() * 6)`, played standalone (default loadout; 5 hostages for Ops 5 and 6; no\n  perks). The host's sim seed is `floor(AIHub.rng('sim')() * 2^32)`.\n- Session tempo: rail speed ×1.3 and every hold's `max` ×.6, so an op with its boss takes about 4 minutes (the meta\n  says 5, to leave margin).\n- Call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as the op is built, with no key press.\n\n**Our card (`hubcard` scene, `card: true`):** the logo; the op's name and card line; the players in seat colors\n(`info.players[i].color`), each with READY ticks from the `card` event; the goal; this device's controls (from\n`input.label`); the time left (`card.left`; PAUSED when `paused`). **Enter / ✕ / a click on READY** →\n`AIHub.answer('ready')`. **△ / M / a click on MORE TIME** → `AIHub.answer('more')` (pressing again takes it back). The\ncard has no menus or settings, and its cosmetic randomness comes from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n\n**Start:** on `start`, show 3-2-1 from `AIHub.time()`; play begins when `AIHub.time() >= 0`. The HUD shows TIME from\n`AIHub.limitMs - AIHub.time()`.\n\n**Roles:**\n- **The host** (`AIHub.isHost`) runs `WP.Sim` with one player slot per `info.players` entry: its own from local input,\n  the others from the network. With **`AIHub.server`** (a host with no player of its own), there is no local player,\n  input or camera, and it draws nothing.\n- **Clients** run `WP.Mirror`: they draw the world from snapshots, move their own crosshair locally at once, and play their\n  own muzzle flashes, tracers, sounds, hit sparks and hit markers at once (predicted). Kills, pickups and damage come only\n  from the host.\n\n**Messages** (JSON with short keys; at most 18 a second from any copy, counting everything; a token bucket in `91-codec.js`\nmirrors the client's limit of 20/s with bursts of 40):\n\n| Name | Direction | Delivery | Rate | Contents |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `i` (input) | client → host | unreliable | 15/s | `{ k:'i', s: seq, a: [x*10|0, y*10|0], b: fireBit, g: grenadeCount, r: reloadCount, n: roundsFired, h: [[seq, [[id, part, dmg], …]], …] }`: the hit batches the host hasn't acked yet (at most 3, so a loss is covered) |\n| `s` (snapshot) | host → all | unreliable | 15/s | `{ k:'s', t: simMs, d: railD, q: quotas, p: [[pid, x, y, dmg, mag, spares, gren, score, flags]], e: [[id, typeCode, x, y, z, facing16, state, hp%]], j: [[id, kind, x, y, z]], u: [[id, kind, x, y, z]], ack: { pid: seq } }` |\n| `ev` (events) | host → all | reliable | ≤ 3/s, batched | `{ k:'ev', l: [[type, …args], …] }`: spawn, kill (id, by, part), pickup (id, pid, kind), damage (pid, amount, from), explode, telegraph, radio, boss phase, hostage, clear, fail |\n\n- **Size guard:** every unreliable message stays under 1100 bytes, because larger ones travel as several packets and are\n  lost whole. Quantize to integers and keep keys short. If a snapshot is too big, leave out pickups, then props, then the\n  farthest entities, round-robin, so each still updates at ≥ 5/s. Over 16 KB is impossible by construction; assert it.\n- **Hits are the client's call, checked by the host:** a client tests its shots against its interpolated world and\n  reports the target ids and parts. The host applies them when the target is alive and the report is less than 400 ms old\n  (co-op, so be generous). The host deducts ammo from `n` and handles grenade and reload counts by their difference. Each\n  pickup goes to the first reporter.\n- **Interpolation:** draw remote entities 100 ms behind (`AIHub.time() - 100`), interpolating linearly between snapshots.\n  Create entities from `spawn` events (types and rigs), play deaths from `kill` events, and drop an entity missing for 3\n  snapshots.\n- **Reporting:** the host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won, stats, awards })` once: when the op is cleared\n  (`won: true`), when everyone is DOWN (`won: false`), or on **`time-up`** at once (`won: false` unless cleared). Standings\n  are player ids sorted by score, best first (ties share an array), listing every player still in. Stats per player:\n  kills, accuracy, headshots, intercepts, civilians hit. Awards: SHARPSHOOTER (best accuracy), GUARDIAN (most intercepts),\n  LIFESAVER (most hostages escorted, or civilians spared).\n- **`leave`:** the host removes that player's slot, and their crosshair fades on every copy. A host leaving ends the round\n  (the hub voids it).\n- **`end`:** stop all input, sound and music (`audio.music(null)`, mute effects), freeze the frame, and send nothing\n  more.\n- **Rules for sessions:** no network but `AIHub.send`; no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation; quit,\n  restart and title do nothing (they're hidden); no chat; names come from the hub and are drawn with the pixel font only\n  (anything outside ASCII falls back to \"P1\"–\"P4\"); never pause the sim (the menu overlays it); the tab hidden on the host\n  keeps simulating.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Touch-only devices, About/Credits, exit interview\n\n### 14.1 Touch-only devices\n\nAt boot, and whenever input changes: `touchOnly = matchMedia('(any-pointer: coarse)').matches &&\n!matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0 && no gamepad connected && no key pressed\nyet`. While it holds: no touch controls (`input.touchEnabled = false`, no `touchButtons`); the title shows a panel\n\"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\" with a large **SETTINGS** button (`game.menu('settings')`) and the engine's corner menu\nbutton; the attract mode starts after 10 s and loops, and taps don't stop it. A `gamepadconnected` or `keydown` leaves\ntouch-only mode and shows the normal title.\n\n### 14.2 About/Credits (`about` scene; the same text goes in the chat reply)\n\nPages, left/right to turn, ○ to leave:\n1. **SOURCE INFORMATION (1/2):** Date `2026-11-03 17:47:46`; Source: Operation Wolf (Taito, 1987); Plan: `PLAN.md`;\n   Genre and perspective: light-gun rail shooter, first person on a scripted rail; Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the full\n   engine with Mode 7, Arcade and Shell; the version of every edit noted), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, Playwright\n   (tests), Node (tests and build).\n2. **SOURCE INFORMATION (2/2):** Art direction; Animation; Audio; Online (AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world co-op\n   for 1–4; local co-op for 1–4); Testing (what was allowed and used); Research (the planner: Wikipedia and\n   arcade-history.com on Operation Wolf, plus the engine's and hub's docs; the builder adds their own or \"none\"); Environment\n   (Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown, or what was used); Model; Usage (an estimate, or \"unknown\").\n3. **TESTING FEEDBACK:** the four answers.\n4. **ENGINE FEEDBACK:** the six answers.\n5. **PROMPT FEEDBACK:** the four answers.\n6. **CREDITS:** \"OPERATION WOLFPACK, an original game inspired by Operation Wolf (Taito, 1987). Not affiliated with or\n   endorsed by Taito.\" The engine my-3D2dge (MIT, michaelcrosato), the AI Hub client (michaelcrosato), any CC0 store\n   assets used (with their credit lines), and the model and harness that built it.\n\nFill every field with what is true at the end of the build; write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm. `WP.TEXT.about`\nholds the text, and the build fails if a field is empty.\n\n### 14.3 Exit interview\n\nWrite `./exit-interview.json` in the exact shape TASK.md gives. Suggested `aiHub` values: name \"Operation Wolfpack\";\ntagline \"Every bullet counts. Bring them home.\"; description \"A first-person light-gun rail shooter for 1–4 players:\nstorm the Brimstone Coast with limited ammo, spare the civilians and rescue five hostages from the Hyena Legion.\"; type\n\"Game\"; genre \"Shooter\"; source \"Operation Wolf\"; series \"\" (the franchise has the source's own name); players \"1–4\";\ncontrols \"Mouse or stick aims · click/R2 fires · right click/L2 grenade · R/□ reload\"; tags [\"first-person\", \"arcade\",\n\"co-op\", \"pixel art\", \"retro\", \"boss fights\"]. `tests/run.mjs` parses the file and checks every key is there.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Build order and milestones\n\nEach milestone ends with the test command green (`npm test`) and the listed checks. Build systems before content, and Op\n1 completely before the other ops.\n\n| # | Milestone | Build | Exit criteria |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **M0** | Setup and spike (**de-risk the renderer, hits and bundle first**) | the dev folder; the engine and hub copies; `manifest.json`; `dev/index.html`; a Mode 7 test scene: floor painter, Backdrop, 30 Humanoids at depths 60–900, a jeep shape driving, palms; the mouse crosshair; hit shapes with the debug overlay; rig height calibration (`WP.RIG_H`); `tools/build.mjs` producing the single file with session.js and the metas; `tests/run.mjs` skeleton | a screenshot shows correct depth scaling; hit shapes line up with rigs at 4 depths and in 3 poses (screenshot); the bundle opens over file:// with no errors; the harness loads the bundle (a stub `connect`/`ready`) |\n| **M1** | Core loop | input adapters (mouse, pad, keys), aim assist, the weapon (fire, bloom, magazines, reload, auto-reload), grenades and explosions, RIFLEMAN (cross, popup) with telegraph and fire, the damage meter and DOWN, pickups (MAG, GRENADE, RATION), crates and barrels, FX v1 (dust, sparks, explosion), the gun overlay, HUD v1, SFX v1; the `range` scene | the range is playable for 2 minutes; T-core, T-proj, T-weapon, T-hit, T-input pass |\n| **M2** | The stage framework and Op 1 | the stage schema, rail and holds, beats and spawns, quotas and reinforcements, layout helpers and floor painters, the Op 1 shapes, GRENADIER, KNIFE, OFFICER, SNIPER, MORTAR, BRUTE, PARATROOPER, jeep, truck, VULTURE, the grenade, knife, rocket, missile and mortar projectiles, FURY, props (sandbags, masts), BIG EAR; the radio and voice v1; music `op1`; the op card, tally and continue | Op 1 plays from the card to the tally; T-enemy-*, T-boss-1 and T-stage-1 (god bot, then fair bot on RECRUIT) pass |\n| **M3** | The game's frame | title (logo art), menus, settings, glyph default and the mirror, pause items, help, briefing, map, high scores (`E.Arcade`), continue, the ending skeleton for all 6 variants, About, the attract mode with the bot, touch-only mode, the dev screen (engine changes 2–4) | the title → Op 1 → tally → map flow works; attract starts at 10 s and any input ends it; dev sliders change play live and reset; T-flow (partial), T-attract, T-touch, T-dev pass |\n| **M4** | Multiplayer | local co-op (join, panels, crosshairs, shared quotas, DOWN and return); AI Hub: card, roles, codec, rate limiter, interpolation, server mode, time-up, leave, end, finish | T-coop and T-hub-mock pass; **the real harness passes** in all 4 configurations (17.3) |\n| **M5** | Op 2 and the interrogation | the river floor and forward rail, bob, skiffs, patrol boat, the bridge, carriers in trees, CROCODILE, the interrogation cutscene, music `op2` | T-stage-2, T-boss-2, the cutscene test |\n| **M6** | Ops 3 and 4 | windows and doors (clip), civilians and their penalties, the reporter, RPG, APC, DYNAMITE, WARTHOG and the village perk; the depot, chains, the cargo plane, forklift, IRON HOG and the refill perk; music `op3`, `op4` | T-stage-3/4, T-boss-3/4, T-perks |\n| **M7** | Ops 5 and 6 and the endings | the darkness mask, searchlights and SPOTTED, rain, FLARE, the breakout escort, TUSK; the airfield, tank, the boarding escort, the part B cut, altitude Mode 7, HYENA ONE; all endings, credits, loop 2; music `op5`, `op6`, `ending` | T-stage-5/6, T-boss-5/6, T-endings, **T-playthrough** (the whole campaign, headless) |\n| **M8** | Polish and balance | the full audio pass (every song, sound and voice), animation polish (9.2 list, filmstrips), FX polish, the HUD and 10-foot pass, aim assist tuning in the range, balance from bot statistics (damage taken per op, quota ÷ spawns, ammo curve: no fair-bot DRY on VETERAN), the attract playlist finished, the About text | every op looks right in screenshots (a list: 17.4); a fair bot finishes VETERAN with ≥ 3 hostages in ≥ 2 of 3 seeds; no look notes from `check.mjs` left unhandled |\n| **M9** | Ship | the final bundle; the whole test command; the harness; the browser smoke on the final file; `exit-interview.json`; the About pages filled; the chat reply | section 18's checklist is all ticked |\n\n---\n\n## 16. Risks and how to de-risk them\n\n| Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Mode 7 as a first-person gallery** (scale, sorting, cost) | It was built for karts: rigs at k up to ~4, big set pieces, many shapes; anchors that sort wrongly; the shape sprite cache churning (300 entries) | M0 spike with screenshots at 4 depths; scenery at fixed depth keeps the same k (cache hits); raise the cache size in the engine if needed; give covers and openings their own depth bias; test the worst screen (Op 4 chains + 40 entities) early. Performance has no budget, but frames must still be drawn correctly |\n| **Hit shapes not matching what is drawn** | Rig heights vary by preset and pose; Mode 7 quantizes the view's scale | calibrate (7.2) instead of guessing; the debug overlay; a test that projects a known rig and checks the head shape lies in the top 15% of its drawn box (using the calibration table) |\n| **Lighting under Mode 7** | Mode 7 draws as an overlay, so the engine's `game.lights` and particles don't apply | own world FX through `m7.add` and an own screen-space darkness mask with dithered light holes (`px.ddisc`), planned from M1 (FX) and M7 (night); verify Op 5's readability by screenshot |\n| **Netcode in a shared world** | Rate limits, 1100-byte unreliable messages, host leave, server mode, interpolation | the protocol in 13.2 is the design; M4 builds a Node mock bus first (latency, jitter, loss) with assertions on rate and size, then the real harness in all configurations before any more content |\n| **Session rules colliding with engine defaults** | The engine pauses on hidden tabs and menus, offers Quit, and may use storage | engine change 3 (non-pausing menu), `autoPause: false`, menu items hidden in sessions; T-hub checks that nothing pauses the host sim |\n| **Pad aiming feels bad** | A stick is not a light gun | the range scene with a time-to-target readout; acceleration, friction, magnetism and snap; difficulty-scaled assist; tune in M1 and again in M8 |\n| **Gibberish voices and synthesized guns sound cheap** | Everything is chip synthesis | a dev soundboard (dev screen: PLAY SOUND select) from M1; layered sounds; the per-letter voice hook from M2 |\n| **Content volume** (6 ops, 6 bosses, about 90 beats) | Time, and stubs creeping in | data-first stage files, beat macros and layout helpers; finish Op 1 to \"done\" in M2 so later ops copy a working pattern; a test that every beat of every op fires and every op clears |\n| **Bundling** | `session.js` must be first and unmodified; `</script>` inside inlined code breaks the page | the bundler escapes `</script` as `<\\/script` in inlined code only (never inside session.js; check it has none) and compares session.js's hash; T-bundle |\n| **Determinism drift** | Rigs or FX reading the sim's random stream; `Math.random` sneaking in | separate streams (`sim`, `loot`, `ai`, `fx`); a test that runs the same seed twice and compares a hash of the snapshots; a lint step in `run.mjs` that fails on any `Math.random` in `src/` |\n| **Touch detection false positives** | Touch laptops have fine pointers and keyboards | the `any-pointer: fine` check, recovery on keydown or gamepadconnected; T-touch with stubbed `matchMedia` |\n| **Disk space** | `/tmp` was full when this was planned | keep clones, Playwright output and temp files in the dev folder (`TMPDIR=./.tmp` for the test runs) |\n\n---\n\n## 17. Testing\n\n### 17.1 The one command\n\n`npm test` (= `node tests/run.mjs`) prints **only failures** and then **one line**: `412 passed, 0 failed (38.2 s)`.\nOptions: `--quick` (headless suites only), `--only <suite>` (for example `--only weapon`), and `--changed` (only the suites\nwhose `covers` files changed since the last green run; a stamp file in `tests/.last`). Rerun a suite only after changing\ncode it covers. Each suite declares `covers: ['src/31-weapon.js', …]`. As TASK.md says, don't use subagents or workflows\nto debate, review, judge or audit; the tests and your own screenshots are the checks.\n\nHeadless suites load `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and the `src/` files from `manifest.json` into a `node:vm` context with small\nstand-ins (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`, `navigator`, `matchMedia`, `performance`), as the handoff's\n`game/test.mjs` and `kits/test.mjs` do. Then they drive the game with `game.advance(seconds)`, `input.tap/hold/feed`,\ninjected frames (`game.debug.frames`), and read `game.debug.snapshot()`. Every suite also fails on `game.errors`.\n\n### 17.2 Suites (what each proves)\n\n| Suite | Checks |\n|---|---|\n| T-core | fixed-step determinism: two runs, same seed and the same frames, give the same snapshot hash after 60 s of bot play; no `Math.random` anywhere in `src/` (lint) |\n| T-proj | `project` and `toFloor` round trips; `halfWidth`; a rig's hit shapes against its calibrated drawn box at depths 60/200/400/800 and in 3 poses |\n| T-input | mouse (`input.feed('move')`) moves the crosshair absolutely; keyboard movement from `held` codes; stick velocity through an injected stick; aim assist friction and snap pick the right target; `input.label('fire')` gives \"R2\" (PlayStation), \"RT\" (Xbox) and \"Left click\" (mouse) |\n| T-weapon | 11 rounds in a second held; magazine count; auto-reload after .12 s and a 1.0 s reload; part-used magazines kept; empty clicks; FURY doubles the rate and uses no ammo; bloom stays ≤ 7 px |\n| T-hit | head vs body vs legs; a headshot ×2 (×4 on BRUTE); cover blocks; nearest first; projectiles intercepted; pickups go to the shooter; the floor puff on misses |\n| T-grenade | the count; range clamp; the blast kills inside the radius and spares outside; vehicles take damage; civilians inside are penalized; barrel chains |\n| T-enemy-<type> | every type in 8.4 and 8.5: spawns, telegraphs (ring time per difficulty), fires (ignored → damage rises by the expected amount ± the accuracy roll with a fixed seed), dies when shot, counts toward the right quota; OFFICER calls 3 (2 after the perk); paratrooper chute; vehicles' weak points and wrecks |\n| T-friendlies | civilian hit: +8 damage, −1000, streak reset; hostage grab and recapture; lost and rescued counts; animals drop and flee, never die |\n| T-pickups | each effect; expiry at 6 s; the supply director's weights move with need; the emergency drop by difficulty; the DRY rule (DOWN on ARCADE) |\n| T-boss-1…6 | each boss's phases advance when its weak points die (`debug.tune('oneHit')` or targeted frames); armored parts take no damage; defeat leads to the tally |\n| T-stage-1…6 | with the god bot: every beat fires, every hold releases, the quotas reach 0, the boss comes, the op clears within its time budget; with damage off for vehicles, the reinforcement loop spawns vehicles until the quota is met |\n| T-perks | quotas ×.8 after Op 1; −40 after Op 3; the refill and pouch +2 after Op 4; n hostages carried into Op 6 |\n| T-flow | title → briefing (skip) → map → opcard → play → tally → … → ending → credits → initials → title; continue restores the op-start state; all 6 endings by hostage count; loop 2 raises the multipliers; Mission Select unlocks after a clear |\n| T-cutscenes | each cutscene runs to its end at speed and can be skipped by holding confirm |\n| T-coop | `game.addPlayer({ pad: 1 })` gives a second player; separate ammo and damage; pickups to the shooter; quotas scale; DOWN, then back at the next op with 50; all DOWN → continue |\n| T-attract | 10 s idle on the title → demo; the bot kills enemies and hits no civilian or hostage across the whole playlist; `tap('confirm')` or a mouse move returns to the title; the scores table shows |\n| T-touch | with stubbed `matchMedia` and `maxTouchPoints`: the notice and the settings button show, taps don't start a game, attract runs; a keydown turns it off |\n| T-dev | the pause menu has DEV MODE; changing `spawnDensity` to 2 doubles a beat's spawns; `railSpeed` changes the time to reach a beat; RESET TO DEFAULTS restores every slider; JUMP reaches the right op and beat; the cheats work |\n| T-hub-mock | a Node mock of `AIHub` (connect, ready, card, start, send, on, time, rng, finish) with an in-memory bus (150 ms latency, 50 jitter, 5% loss), 1 host and 3 clients: clients see the host's entities within 250 ms; client hits kill on the host; every unreliable message < 1100 bytes; ≤ 18 messages a second per copy; time-up → exactly one `finish`; a leave removes a slot; server mode runs with no local player; `end` stops input and sound |\n| T-bundle | the final file exists with the exact name; session.js is the first script right after `<meta charset>`, byte-identical to `hub/session.js`; all `hub:` metas are present; no `WebSocket`, `RTCPeerConnection`, `fetch(`, `XMLHttpRequest`, `alert(`, `confirm(`, `prompt(`, `window.open` in the game's code; `exit-interview.json` parses with every key and no empty value |\n| T-playthrough | **the whole game:** a fair bot on RECRUIT, no cheats, from the title (press start) through all 6 ops, the cutscenes and the ending, to the initials; asserts the ending is reached, the rank exists, ≥ 3 hostages, no errors. A god-bot run on VETERAN asserts the same, faster |\n| T-browser (not in `--quick`) | Playwright on the **final file** over `file://`: boot with no console errors; the title canvas isn't empty; attract after 10 s; deep links `#op1`…`#op6`, `#ending/5` load and report the right `debug.snapshot().scene`; `node engine/tools/check.mjs <final>.html#op1` passes with no errors |\n| T-hub-harness (not in `--quick`) | 17.3 |\n\n### 17.3 The real AI Hub harness\n\nCopy the final .html and `hub/harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` into `tests/.serve/`. Start\n`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there, read the port from its first line, and **keep its PID**. With\nPlaywright, open `http://127.0.0.1:PORT/harness.html?game=<final>.html&…` for each configuration:\n`players=1&auto=1`, `players=2&auto=1`, `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`,\n`players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1`, `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. Wait for\n`document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. First confirm that the frames\nhold our game (`document.title` is \"Operation Wolfpack\" inside a frame) before trusting a result. Print the checklist only\non failure. Stop the server by its PID, and only that one: never `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k`, or kill whatever holds a\nport.\n\n### 17.4 Screenshots (only for what a script can't check)\n\nLook, readability at 10 feet, animation quality and lighting. Use `node engine/tools/check.mjs` and\n`node engine/tools/filmstrip.mjs` on deep links into `shots/`, and review: each op's opening screen, each boss, the\nbreakout at night, the takeoff at altitude, the HUD with 1 and 4 players, the title, the map, the tally, the About pages,\nthe hub card, the touch notice, plus filmstrips of a rifleman's death, a grenade throw, a knife throw, the reload, an\nexplosion and the mast toppling. Act on every look note `check.mjs` prints. Retake a screenshot only after changing what\nit shows.\n\n---\n\n## 18. Definition of done\n\n- [ ] `./OperationWolfpack-OperationWolf-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174746.html` is one file that runs over `file://`\n      and in the AI Hub harness; every dev file is in the dev folder.\n- [ ] Every system in section 7 and every screen in section 10 works; all six operations, six bosses, every cutscene in\n      8.8 and all six endings play; no TODO, placeholder text or stubbed feature (`run.mjs` fails on `TODO|FIXME|placeholder|lorem` in\n      `src/` and on an empty `WP.TEXT` value).\n- [ ] Keyboard and mouse, keyboard only and a standard pad all play the whole game; prompts follow the last device;\n      PlayStation glyphs by default and Xbox in Settings; the mouse hovers and clicks every menu.\n- [ ] Attract mode starts after 10 s idle on the title and menus, shows every op, and stops on any input; touch-only\n      devices show the notice, the settings button and the attract mode.\n- [ ] The dev mode opens from the pause menu, with live sliders (11.1), reset to defaults, toggles, jumps, spawns and the\n      data tools.\n- [ ] Local co-op for 1–4 and AI Hub shared-world sessions for 1–4; the harness passes in all five configurations.\n- [ ] All music, sound and voices are synthesized in code (no audio files); voices are gibberish with subtitles.\n- [ ] `npm test` is green: failures only, plus one count line; the headless whole-game playthrough passes.\n- [ ] The About/Credits screen and the chat reply carry Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt\n      Feedback (\"unknown\" where you can't confirm); `./exit-interview.json` parses in the exact shape.\n- [ ] `engine/CHANGES.md` lists every engine edit; the research clone and any servers you started are cleaned up.\n","numLines":350,"startLine":1170,"totalLines":1519}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NB1qeMnmLTXrxC2ibdsKDA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
