{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PPJ4LgLjMRQprPGmFFiG8a","type":"tool_result","content":"139:- `E.ctx2d(c)`: a canvas's 2D context with smoothing off (crisp pixels)\n163:- `E.hex(h)`: '#rrggbb' or '#rgb' (or an [r, g, b] array) -> [r, g, b]\n164:- `E.hsl(hh, s, l)`: '#rrggbb' from hue (degrees), saturation and lightness (0..1)\n169:- `E.mix(h1, h2, t)`: the color t of the way from h1 to h2 ('#rrggbb')\n170:- `E.mkCanvas(w, h)`: a new canvas of w x h pixels (scratch images and sprite sheets). With no document (Node: a headless game) a stand-in whose drawing does nothing, so sprites and other images made while a game loads don't stop it\n171:- `E.noise2(x, y)`: smooth value noise 0..1 over the plane (one bump per whole unit): blotches, clouds, wobble\n179:- `E.rng(s)`: a seeded random stream: const R = E.rng(42); R() gives 0..1, the same numbers for the same seed (mulberry32)\n181:- `E.shade(h, a)`: shade('#336699', -0.3) darker, (+0.3) lighter. Hue-shifted like painted pixel art: darker drifts cool, lighter drifts warm\n190:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward warm yellow (strength 0..2, default 1).\n197:- `px.blend(g, a, mode, fn)`: draw fn() at alpha a (stepped, like PS1 hardware) with a blend mode: 'normal', 'add', 'multiply', 'screen' (E.style.trans = 'dither' dithers instead)\n199:- `px.ddisc(g, cx, cy, r, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: soft disc that fades toward its edge (glows, smoke, dust): stepped alpha rings, or dithering in 'dither' style\n200:- `px.disc(g, cx, cy, r, c)`: a filled circle\n201:- `px.dot(g, x, y, c)`: one pixel\n202:- `px.ell(g, cx, cy, rx, ry, c)`: a filled ellipse\n204:- `px.line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, w = 1)`: a line w pixels thick, no smoothing\n205:- `px.poly(g, pts, c)`: a filled polygon through [[x, y], ...]\n206:- `px.polyDither(g, pts, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: translucent polygon: a = 0..1 opacity (stepped alpha, or a dither pattern in 'dither' style). wx/wy = world pixel offset for the pattern\n207:- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`: a filled rectangle, snapped to whole pixels\n359:- `E.font.text(g, s, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o = '#0b0814')`: draw text at (x, y) (its top-left; align: 'center' or 'right' moves it) in color. o: an outline color, or { outline, shadow, gradient, scale, align, wrap, font }; returns { w, h }\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n361:- `E.font.width(s, o)`: width in pixels of the widest line. opts: a scale number or { font, scale }\n559:- `E.PLAYER_COLORS: #4a8aff, #ff4a4a, #4ad860, #ffd040` †: the players' colors: player 1 blue, 2 red, 3 green, 4 yellow (game.players)\n1102:- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item's shape seen at an angle. r.sprite stands it on its feet (foot: [x, y] in the sprite) unless an anchor is given","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0704575-f16b-44ea-a24d-907e9c278025","uuid":"24878969-dcf3-4f6f-834f-26de99469879","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:33:35.887Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"139:- `E.ctx2d(c)`: a canvas's 2D context with smoothing off (crisp pixels)\n163:- `E.hex(h)`: '#rrggbb' or '#rgb' (or an [r, g, b] array) -> [r, g, b]\n164:- `E.hsl(hh, s, l)`: '#rrggbb' from hue (degrees), saturation and lightness (0..1)\n169:- `E.mix(h1, h2, t)`: the color t of the way from h1 to h2 ('#rrggbb')\n170:- `E.mkCanvas(w, h)`: a new canvas of w x h pixels (scratch images and sprite sheets). With no document (Node: a headless game) a stand-in whose drawing does nothing, so sprites and other images made while a game loads don't stop it\n171:- `E.noise2(x, y)`: smooth value noise 0..1 over the plane (one bump per whole unit): blotches, clouds, wobble\n179:- `E.rng(s)`: a seeded random stream: const R = E.rng(42); R() gives 0..1, the same numbers for the same seed (mulberry32)\n181:- `E.shade(h, a)`: shade('#336699', -0.3) darker, (+0.3) lighter. Hue-shifted like painted pixel art: darker drifts cool, lighter drifts warm\n190:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward warm yellow (strength 0..2, default 1).\n197:- `px.blend(g, a, mode, fn)`: draw fn() at alpha a (stepped, like PS1 hardware) with a blend mode: 'normal', 'add', 'multiply', 'screen' (E.style.trans = 'dither' dithers instead)\n199:- `px.ddisc(g, cx, cy, r, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: soft disc that fades toward its edge (glows, smoke, dust): stepped alpha rings, or dithering in 'dither' style\n200:- `px.disc(g, cx, cy, r, c)`: a filled circle\n201:- `px.dot(g, x, y, c)`: one pixel\n202:- `px.ell(g, cx, cy, rx, ry, c)`: a filled ellipse\n204:- `px.line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, w = 1)`: a line w pixels thick, no smoothing\n205:- `px.poly(g, pts, c)`: a filled polygon through [[x, y], ...]\n206:- `px.polyDither(g, pts, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: translucent polygon: a = 0..1 opacity (stepped alpha, or a dither pattern in 'dither' style). wx/wy = world pixel offset for the pattern\n207:- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`: a filled rectangle, snapped to whole pixels\n359:- `E.font.text(g, s, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o = '#0b0814')`: draw text at (x, y) (its top-left; align: 'center' or 'right' moves it) in color. o: an outline color, or { outline, shadow, gradient, scale, align, wrap, font }; returns { w, h }\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n361:- `E.font.width(s, o)`: width in pixels of the widest line. opts: a scale number or { font, scale }\n559:- `E.PLAYER_COLORS: #4a8aff, #ff4a4a, #4ad860, #ffd040` †: the players' colors: player 1 blue, 2 red, 3 green, 4 yellow (game.players)\n1102:- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item's shape seen at an angle. r.sprite stands it on its feet (foot: [x, y] in the sprite) unless an anchor is given","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174807__x5c5240/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1978,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1978,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":4550,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"3c819b0f-1b18-471b-b765-9dcf56869a17\",\"uuid\":\"82077a98-92f6-42d6-9580-fb4d7fb6849f\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":4650,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"3c819b0f-1b18-471b-b765-9dcf56869a17\",\"uuid\":\"14891082-3352-4f4c-9ddc-20d281763950\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":4750,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"3c819b0f-1b18-471b-b765-9dcf56869a17\",\"uuid\":\"3d9932d2-c172-4e3e-99a2-dfce869ed917\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":4850,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"3c819b0f-1b18-471b-b765-9dcf56869a17\",\"uuid\":\"57d7fb88-5cc8-4918-836a-dc263ce1b787\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174834__x4394d1/work/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1309,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1309,"newLines":12,"lines":[" "," ## 7. Content"," ","+In a football game the usual content words map like this. **Levels** are the 5 cup rounds, each in its own stadium","+with its own weather and events (§7.2), plus the training ground. **Enemies** are the 5 opposing clubs, each with its","+own tactics and gimmick; the final's Olympique Opulence is the boss team, with a boss keeper and a boss captain","+(§7.1). The referees are the neutral hazard. **Items** are the unlockable balls, the stickers and the team-talk buffs;","+there are no pickups in matches (§6.31). **Story beats** are in §7.3.","+"," Tone everywhere: British football broadcasting and tabloid back pages, turned up. That means puns (fish puns for the"," Kippers), commentary clichés, deadpan replies, affectionate and never mean. National stereotypes are off-limits: the"," opponents' jokes come from their **football philosophies**, their food, weather and stadiums. All names are original;"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/index.html","hunks":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":7,"newStart":2,"newLines":7,"lines":[" <style>body{font:14px system-ui;margin:16px;background:#fff;color:#111}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}"," th,td{padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;text-align:left;white-space:nowrap}th{cursor:pointer;background:#f4f4f4;position:sticky;top:0}"," .failed{color:#b00}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{background:#111;color:#eee}th{background:#222}td,th{border-color:#333}a{color:#8bf}}</style>","-<h1>Matrix runs (472)</h1><p>Static copy. For