{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3VfZ1Esg4sDPC1TkyN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G6PibZtgwwVyodKhT6Ze5w","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='27-props.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"  if (e.dead && !(tp.cover && e.type === 'sandbags' && false)) return;\",\"  if (e.dead || e.fallen) return;\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='10-view3d.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  onScreen(sx, sy, m = 0)\"\"\",\"\"\"  /** the world point on the view ray through (sx, sy) at depth D (impact effects) */\n  atDepth(sx, sy, D) {\n    const P = this.P, kx = (sx - P.cx) / P.f, ky = (P.cy - sy) / P.f;\n    const dir = [P.fx * P.cp + P.rx * kx + P.fx * P.sp * ky, P.fy * P.cp + P.ry * kx + P.fy * P.sp * ky, -P.sp + P.cp * ky];\n    const fd = dir[0] * P.fx + dir[1] * P.fy, t = D / Math.max(1e-4, fd);\n    return [P.x + dir[0] * t, P.y + dir[1] * t, P.h + dir[2] * t];\n  }\n  onScreen(sx, sy, m = 0)\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"atDepth\" 10-view3d.js","description":"Patch prop shapes and add view atDepth helper"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8013,"cache_read_input_tokens":295357,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8013},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0704575-f16b-44ea-a24d-907e9c278025","uuid":"ab9e00f1-e1f7-435e-9230-38a6ed2051a9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:46:52.199Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3VfFPQFQ5bsHnmZLob","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01G6PibZtgwwVyodKhT6Ze5w":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='27-props.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"  if (e.dead && !(tp.cover && e.type === 'sandbags' && false)) return;\",\"  if (e.dead || e.fallen) return;\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='10-view3d.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  onScreen(sx, sy, m = 0)\"\"\",\"\"\"  /** the world point on the view ray through (sx, sy) at depth D (impact effects) */\n  atDepth(sx, sy, D) {\n    const P = this.P, kx = (sx - P.cx) / P.f, ky = (P.cy - sy) / P.f;\n    const dir = [P.fx * P.cp + P.rx * kx + P.fx * P.sp * ky, P.fy * P.cp + P.ry * kx + P.fy * P.sp * ky, -P.sp + P.cp * ky];\n    const fd = dir[0] * P.fx + dir[1] * P.fy, t = D / Math.max(1e-4, fd);\n    return [P.x + dir[0] * t, P.y + dir[1] * t, P.h + dir[2] * t];\n  }\n  onScreen(sx, sy, m = 0)\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"atDepth\" 10-view3d.js","description":"Patch prop shapes and add view atDepth helper"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G6PibZtgwwVyodKhT6Ze5w","type":"tool_result","content":"34:  atDepth(sx, sy, D) {","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0704575-f16b-44ea-a24d-907e9c278025","uuid":"260ee89c-0772-4cb0-8a55-5c3e206a3d2b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:46:57.101Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"34:  atDepth(sx, sy, D) {","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2390,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2390,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01RJ7LtBu3ozHzHoqHpUgC5z\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"489\\t  - Mage: dagger and spellbook (Spark Dart, Find Seams, Slumber), plus a Traveller's Robe.\\n490\\t  - Thief: short sword, darts ×6, leather armour, Lockpicks.\\n491\\t  - Everyone gets 1 Ration and starts at food 100%.\\n492\\t- **Begin the Descent** starts the intro cutscene.\\n493\\t\\n494\\t### 4.5 Items, inventory, equipment and the Hand\\n495\\t\\n496\\t- **Slots for each member.** `head, neck, body, arms` (bracers), `main, off` (hands), `ring1, ring2, feet, quiver`, plus a **backpack of 12**.\\n497\\t  - Two-handed items fill main and lock off.\\n498\\t  - Ammo (bolts, arrows, sling stones) and darts stack up to 30; nothing else stacks.\\n499\\t  - There is no weight.\\n500\\t- **The Hand.** The party holds one item at a time, as the source held one on the mouse cursor. With the mouse it follows the cursor; otherwise it sits above the cards, bottom centre, with its name.\\n501\\t  - **Use ✕** with an item in the Hand:\\n502\\t    - facing an alcove, it places the item;\\n503\\t    - facing a keyhole with a fitting key, it inserts it;\\n504\\t    - with no target, it stows the item in the first free pack slot (the selected member first).\\n505\\t  - **Hold ✕ for 0.4 s** (**H** on the keyboard) puts it down on the front cell's floor, or on your own cell if the front is blocked. Putting it down on a plate presses the plate; putting it into a pit drops it to the landing.\\n506\\t  - **Throw ○** (**G**) sends it forward up to ★4 cells (+1 at STR 16+).\\n507\\t    - It passes over pits and plates.\\n508\\t    - It stops before walls and closed doors and lands in the last open cell, pressing a plate if it lands on one.\\n509\\t    - It stops at the first monster and hits it: thrown weapons do their dice plus STR; other items do 1d2. It then drops in that cell.\\n510\\t- **Picking up.** Picking up (✕ with nothing in the Hand) takes the top item in the front cell if it is open and free of monsters, otherwise in your own cell. Floor items show at the 4 quadrant spots; a fifth item and more show as a little pile.\\n511\\t- **Use** (□ in the Party screen):\\n512\\t  - eat a ration, drink a potion;\\n513\\t  - read a scroll (a mage casts it at once, or uses Scribe at camp to learn it);\\n514\\t  - read a note;\\n515\\t  - zap a wand (as a hand action when it is held).\\n516\\t- **Monster drops.** Each monster has a drop table rolled on the `loot` stream (§7.6). Named monsters have fixed drops. Thieving Latchkins drop what they stole.\\n517\\t- **Rust.** A Rustling's hit can rust a metal main-hand weapon (−2 damage, up to −4, shown as \\\"Rusted\\\"). It is permanent; spare weapons are placed.\\n518\\t\\n519\\t### 4.6 Combat (real time)\\n520\\t\\n521\\t- **Every hand is an action.** Using a hand does what its item does:\\n522\\t\\n523\\t  | Item in the hand | What using it does |\\n524\\t  |---|---|\\n525\\t  | weapon | attacks the front cell, if the member's row may reach it |\\n526\\t  | missile weapon | fires ammo from the quiver along the facing line, up to 6 cells |\\n527\\t  | thrown weapon (dagger, darts, hand axe, spear) | throws it |\\n528\\t  | spellbook or holy symbol | opens the cast menu |\\n529\\t  | wand | zaps |\\n530\\t  | shield | **Brace**: +3 Defense for 2 s |\\n531\\t  | nothing | punches (1d2) |\\n532\\t\\n533\\t  Using a hand starts its cooldown: the weapon's speed (§7.7) × ★attack cooldown × (1 − 0.04 × DEX modifier). Casting a spell puts **both** of the caster's hands on 2.5 s.\\n534\\t- **Party Strike** (□, Space, right-click in the view). Every member whose main hand is ready, and whose main-hand item can act from their row, acts at once:\\n535\\t  - the front row melees;\\n536\\t  - row 2 attacks with reach weapons;\\n537\\t  - anyone holding a missile or thrown weapon fires it.\\n538\\t\\n539\\t  Spellbooks and holy symbols are skipped, because a spell needs a choice. With nothing in front, the front row \\\"swings at the air.\\\"\\n540\\t- **To-hit.** d20 + to-hit bonus (class) + STR modifier (melee and thrown) or DEX modifier (missile) + weapon bonus + ★party to-hit + buffs ≥ the target's Defense.\\n541\\t  - A natural 20 always hits for double dice; a natural 1 always misses.\\n542\\t  - Damage is the weapon's dice + STR modifier (1.5× for two-handed weapons), × ★party damage, at least 1.\\n543\\t  - A miss shows MISS on the hand slot.\\n544\\t- **Party Defense.** 10 + armour + shield + DEX modifier + helm, bracers and rings + buffs.\\n545\\t- **Monster attacks.** A monster's attack roll is d20 + its attack bonus ≥ the member's Defense; its damage is its dice × ★monster damage.\\n546\\t- **Who gets hit.** It depends on where the attacker stands relative to the party's facing:\\n547\\t  - from the front: a random conscious member of the front-most occupied row;\\n548\\t  - from the left: the left column (places 1, 3, 5), front-most first;\\n549\\t  - from the right: the right column (2, 4, 6);\\n550\\t  - from behind: the back-most occupied row.\\n551\\t\\n552\\t  The HUD shows red chevrons on the edge the hit came from (§5.2), and the hit sound is panned.\\n553\\t- **Projectiles** (bolts, arrows, darts, thrown items, Spark Darts, Locking Bolts) move cell by cell at their own speed (8 cells/s for missiles, 6 for Spark Dart, 5 for monster bolts) and hit the first creature in their path.\\n554\\t  - A monster bolt reaching the party's cell hits the party, through the side it came from.\\n555\\t  - A party projectile hits the monster in the target cell's slot nearest the shooter's column.\\n556\\t  - Spent ammo drops in the cell where it stopped, with a 50% chance to be recovered.\\n557\\t- **Statuses** (seconds left, in `member.status` and `mon.status`):\\n558\\t\\n559\\t  | Status | Effect |\\n560\\t  |---|---|\\n561\\t  | Poisoned | 1 HP every 6 s for 60 s, or until Purge or an Antidote |\\n562\\t  | Held | can't act for 4 to 10 s; Free Hinge or the Lidless Ward prevents it |\\n563\\t  | Asleep (monsters) | wakes when damaged; takes ×2 damage |\\n564\\t  | Slowed | intervals ×1.5 |\\n565\\t  | Blessed / Steady | +1 to-hit and +1 to saves |\\n566\\t  | Warded | an absorb pool |\\n567\\t  | Floating | over pits; no plates |\\n568\\t  | Seeing | secrets glint |\\n569\\t  | Turned | undead flee |\\n570\\t\\n571\\t  A **save** is a d20 roll ≥ 15 − level/2 − WIS or CON modifier.\\n572\\t\\n573\\t### 4.7 Monsters and their AI\\n574\\t\\n575\\t#### 4.7.1 Size and cells\\n576\\t- Small monsters take 1 of 4 units in a cell, medium 2 and large 4; a cell holds 4 units.\\n577\\t- Monsters never enter the party's cell or walls, closed doors or pits. Fliers ignore pits and plates.\\n578\\t- Small monsters don't weigh plates; medium and large ones do.\\n579\\t\\n580\\t#### 4.7.2 Minds (per type in §7.6)\\n581\\t- **States.**\\n582\\t  - `asleep`: placed sleeping; noise wakes it.\\n583\\t  - `idle` and `patrol`: a list of cells to walk.\\n584\\t  - `hunt`: paths to the party with `E.Grid` A*. Cells that are full are blocked, so others take the side and back cells, and **flanking happens on its own**.\\n585\\t  - `engage`: next to the party it faces, winds up and strikes.\\n586\\t  - `ranged`: in line with a clear view and in range, it shoots.\\n587\\t  - `keepAway`: casters hold 3 cells off and step back if you close in.\\n588\\t  - `flee`: cowards below 25% HP run for 6 s; thieves flee after a steal.\\n589\\t  - `turned`, `held`, `asleep`.\\n590\\t- **Awareness.**\\n591\\t  - A monster becomes aware when the party's cell is in its sight radius (★sight) and its field of view (E.Fog-style shadowcasting from the monster, or the symmetric check `fog.visible` from the party, as the kit does).\\n592\\t  - **Noise** (combat, doors, levers, falls) wakes monsters within 4 cells; hounds hear to 6.\\n593\\t  - A monster forgets the party after 12 s out of sight and goes back to `patrol`.\\n594\\t- **Movement.** One cell per `move` seconds (per type), drawn as a glide.\\n595\\t\\n596\\t#### 4.7.3 Attacks\\n597\\t- **Every melee attack telegraphs.** The wind-up (★0.5 s; heavy monsters 0.8 s) is a visible animation with a sound. The strike lands only if the party is still next to the monster when the wind-up ends; otherwise \\\"The rat's bite snaps on air.\\\" **This makes the sidestep a skill.**\\n598\\t- **Re-engaging.** After the party changes cell, a monster next to it waits ★0.6 s before starting a new wind-up (the \\\"dance\\\" is fair but not free).\\n599\\t- **Intervals.** Each type has its own interval × ★monster interval.\\n600\\t\\n601\\t#### 4.7.4 The Bolt-Holder (boss, floor 4)\\n602\\t\\n603\\tIt hovers over the arena's centre cell (6,3) with **HP ★320** and Defense 15. It is immune to Hold, Sleep and Poison, and it **absorbs lightning**: Forked Lightning heals it for half, and it gloats \\\"The Bolt-Holder drinks the lightning!\\\"\\n604\\t\\n605\\t| Phase | When | Behaviour |\\n606\\t|---|---|---|\\n607\\t| **1: Caged** | the start | It takes ×0.2 damage through the cage and attacks every 3.5 s. Each of the 3 **Great Locks** (west, east and north walls) turned with ✕ (2.0 s, during which the party can't act) slides out 2 of its 7 bolts (\\\"The Bolt-Holder shrieks!\\\"). When all 3 are turned, the cage opens. |\\n608\\t| **2: Unbolted** | all locks turned | It takes full damage, attacks every 2.8 s and **drifts** one cell toward the party's flank every 4 s (it never enters pillar cells). At 50% HP it **relocks** one lock at random (\\\"It wrenches a bolt home!\\\"): damage taken is ×0.5 until that lock is turned again. |\\n609\\t| **3: Wrath** | HP below 25% | It attacks every 2.2 s and summons 2 Gazers every 12 s (4 at most). |\\n610\\t\\n611\\tIts attacks, picked by its position and line of sight:\\n612\\t- **Chain Lightning** (any phase): telegraphed for 0.8 s by a cyan glow and a flicker along the row or column toward the party. The bolt runs along the line until a pillar or wall: 3d6 to 2 members. Leave the line, or put a pillar between you, to dodge it.\\n613\\t- **Locking Gaze:** the iris narrows for 1.0 s, then 1 or 2 members without the Lidless Ward or Free Hinge are Held for 4 s (\\\"Your joints lock!\\\"). It needs line of sight, and pillars block it.\\n614\\t- **Bolt Rain:** marks the party's cell and 2 open neighbouring cells with glowing rings (`world.arc`) for 1.5 s, then iron bolts slam down: 2d6 to 2 members if the party is still in a marked cell.\\n615\\t- **Cage Slam** (adjacent only): 2d8 to the side facing it.\\n616\\t\\n617\\tOn death the Eye cracks, the bolts fly off, and the north lock wall becomes the **Stair to the Light** (✕ there starts the ending).\\n618\\t\\n619\\t### 4.8 Magic\\n620\\t\\n621\\t- **Mages** cast from their **spellbook** (an off-hand item). The book holds the spells they know; new ones come from scrolls through Camp → Scribe, which always succeeds and uses up the scroll.\\n622\\t- **Clerics** need their **holy symbol** in a hand. They may prepare any prayer of a level they can cast.\\n623\\t- **Memorizing.** Both choose what fills their slots in Camp → Memorize or Pray. The choice persists (\\\"same as before\\\" is the default), and slots refill after a full rest. Casting spends a slot.\\n624\\t- **Scrolls.** A mage can cast a scroll directly, and the scroll is used up. The Scroll of Raising works for clerics and paladins.\\n625\\t- **Wands** have charges and anyone can use one.\\n626\\t- **Slots by caster level, 1 to 8:**\\n627\\t\\n628\\t  | Caster | Spell level | Lv1 | Lv2 | Lv3 | Lv4 | Lv5 | Lv6 | Lv7 | Lv8 |\\n629\\t  |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n630\\t  | Mage | 1 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 4 | 4 | 4 |\\n631\\t  | Mage | 2 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 |\\n632\\t  | Mage | 3 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 3 |\\n633\\t  | Cleric | 1 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 3 | 4 | 4 |\\n634\\t  | Cleric | 2 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 3 |\\n635\\t  | Cleric | 3 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 2 |\\n636\\t\\n637\\t  Bonus slots come from INT and WIS (§4.3) and from the Robe of the Lintel (+1 level-1 slot).\\n638\\t- **Targets.**\\n639\\t  - `front`: the cell in front.\\n640\\t  - `line`: down the facing line.\\n641\\t  - `member`: picked on the cards.\\n642\\t  - `party`.\\n643\\t  - `door`: the door in front.\\n644\\t- **Spell effects** are × ★spell power. The spell list is in §7.8.\\n645\\t\\n646\\t### 4.9 Camp, rest and food\\n647\\t\\n648\\t- **Camp** (L3, C, or the HUD's camp icon) is refused while any aware monster is within 6 cells: \\\"You may not rest with enemies near.\\\"\\n649\\t- **Camp menu tiles:** Rest, Memorize, Pray, Scribe, Formation, Eat, Save Game, Load Game, Settings and Leave Camp.\\n650\\t- **Resting.** An hour passes every 0.4 s of real time. Each hour every conscious member heals ★1 + CON modifier (at least 1) × ★rest heal.\\n651\\t  - After 8 hours, slots refill to the prepared spells, Lay on Hands returns, and Down members wake at 1 HP.\\n652\\t  - During rest, clerics first cast their prepared Mends on the wounded (as the source let the party do), then pray to restore them.\\n653\\t  - Rest stops early when everyone is full and every slot is ready, or when ○ is pressed.\\n654\\t- **Interruptions.** Each hour has a ★4% chance (0 in safe rooms and once the floor's wanderer budget is spent: floor 1: 3, floor 2: 3, floor 3: 4, floor 4: 0) of spawning a wanderer group from the floor's spawn list, 2 cells away and aware. \\\"You are awakened by something moving!\\\" The camp closes.\\n655\\t- **Food** runs 0 to 100 for each member.\\n656\\t  - It drains −1 every ★60 s of play and −15 per full rest. ★Hunger rate scales it.\\n657\\t  - At 25: \\\"Cobb is hungry.\\\" At 0: \\\"Cobb is starving!\\\" A starving member loses 1 HP every 30 s and heals nothing from rest.\\n658\\t  - A Ration gives +50 and an Iron Ration +100. Loaves of the Hearth fills everyone.\\n659\\t  - **Eat** at camp feeds every member below 60% from the party's smallest food items.\\n660\\t\\n661\\t### 4.10 Experience, levels and hidden deeds\\n662\\t\\n663\\t- **XP for kills** is split evenly among conscious members, then × class and race multipliers and × ★XP gain.\\n664\\t- **Base thresholds:** level 2 at 100, 3 at 250, 4 at 500, 5 at 900, 6 at 1500, 7 at 2400 and 8 at 3600 (the demo's cap).\\n665\\t- **Discoveries.** A found secret gives +25 to each member and plays the `secret` sting. There are 3, marked `secret: true` in the floor data: the floor 1 closet (SW1/H1), the floor 1 illusory wall (I1) and the floor 2 catch (SW2). A hidden deed (special quest) gives +100 to each member, plays a jingle and shows \\\"A hidden deed is done!\\\". There are 3 deeds in all; Journal → Deeds counts them.\\n666\\t- **Level-up.** On the next rest or at once (the default is at once, with the \\\"level up\\\" sting): new HP, to-hit and slots, a portrait smile and a toast \\\"Brannoc has reached level 3!\\\".\\n667\\t- **Target pace** (the bot checks it, §14): about level 3 at the end of floor 1, 4 at the end of floor 2, 5 on floor 3, and 5 or 6 at the boss.\\n668\\t\\n669\\t### 4.11 Down, death, raising and game over\\n670\\t\\n671\\t- **Down.** At 0 HP a member is **Down**: unconscious, greyed portrait, can't act. A Down member hit again becomes **Dead** (bones on the card).\\n672\\t- **Waking.** Healing wakes a Down member at the healed amount; a full rest wakes them at 1 HP.\\n673\\t- **Raising the dead.** Raise from Rest (cleric spell level 3), the Scroll of Raising (2 placed) or the **Shrine of the Threshold** (floor 2 Vault, one use) brings a dead member back at 1 HP.\\n674\\t- **Game over.** If no member is conscious, the screen reads \\\"THE PARTY IS LOST\\\" over the frozen view, with Load last save, Load game and Title.\\n675\\t\\n676\\t### 4.12 NPCs, dialogue and choices\\n677\\t\\n678\\t- **Recruits.** Three NPCs can join, up to 6 in the party: **Tamsin Pell** (floor 1), **Durgan Copperhand** (floor 2) and **Sister Veil** (floor 3). Their scripts are in §7.9.\\n679\\t- **Dismissing.** Dismiss is in the Party screen, behind a confirm. A dismissed NPC goes home and is gone for good.\\n680\\t- **How it runs.** Dialogue is `E.Story` nodes through `E.Dialog`:\\n681\\t  - the speaker's live rig portrait, its mouth moving as it speaks;\\n682\\t  - a **babble voice** (§6.5);\\n683\\t  - choices picked with the d-pad and ✕, or a click;\\n684\\t  - story flags kept in the save (`story.state()`).\\n685\\t- **Veil's choice** changes floor 3 (§7.4.3).\\n686\\t- **Barks.** Short, non-modal lines (`modal: false, auto: 2`) for Snick, the Bolt-Holder and party barks.\\n687\\t\\n688\\t### 4.13 Messages, Examine, Journal, notes and hints\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40\",\"uuid\":\"5bd7d10b-2213-4830-bd17-bacb43d03767\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:46:49.817Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work/PLAN.md\",\"content\":\"  - Mage: dagger and spellbook (Spark Dart, Find Seams, Slumber), plus a Traveller's Robe.\\n  - Thief: short sword, darts ×6, leather armour, Lockpicks.\\n  - Everyone gets 1 Ration and starts at food 100%.\\n- **Begin the Descent** starts the intro cutscene.\\n\\n### 4.5 Items, inventory, equipment and the Hand\\n\\n- **Slots for each member.** `head, neck, body, arms` (bracers), `main, off` (hands), `ring1, ring2, feet, quiver`, plus a **backpack of 12**.\\n  - Two-handed items fill main and lock off.\\n  - Ammo (bolts, arrows, sling stones) and darts stack up to 30; nothing else stacks.\\n  - There is no weight.\\n- **The Hand.** The party holds one item at a time, as the source held one on the mouse cursor. With the mouse it follows the cursor; otherwise it sits above the cards, bottom centre, with its name.\\n  - **Use ✕** with an item in the Hand:\\n    - facing an alcove, it places the item;\\n    - facing a keyhole with a fitting key, it inserts it;\\n    - with no target, it stows the item in the first free pack slot (the selected member first).\\n  - **Hold ✕ for 0.4 s** (**H** on the keyboard) puts it down on the front cell's floor, or on your own cell if the front is blocked. Putting it down on a plate presses the plate; putting it into a pit drops it to the landing.\\n  - **Throw ○** (**G**) sends it forward up to ★4 cells (+1 at STR 16+).\\n    - It passes over pits and plates.\\n    - It stops before walls and closed doors and lands in the last open cell, pressing a plate if it lands on one.\\n    - It stops at the first monster and hits it: thrown weapons do their dice plus STR; other items do 1d2. It then drops in that cell.\\n- **Picking up.** Picking up (✕ with nothing in the Hand) takes the top item in the front cell if it is open and free of monsters, otherwise in your own cell. Floor items show at the 4 quadrant spots; a fifth item and more show as a little pile.\\n- **Use** (□ in the Party screen):\\n  - eat a ration, drink a potion;\\n  - read a scroll (a mage casts it at once, or uses Scribe at camp to learn it);\\n  - read a note;\\n  - zap a wand (as a hand action when it is held).\\n- **Monster drops.** Each monster has a drop table rolled on the `loot` stream (§7.6). Named monsters have fixed drops. Thieving Latchkins drop what they stole.\\n- **Rust.** A Rustling's hit can rust a metal main-hand weapon (−2 damage, up to −4, shown as \\\"Rusted\\\"). It is permanent; spare weapons are placed.\\n\\n### 4.6 Combat (real time)\\n\\n- **Every hand is an action.** Using a hand does what its item does:\\n\\n  | Item in the hand | What using it does |\\n  |---|---|\\n  | weapon | attacks the front cell, if the member's row may reach it |\\n  | missile weapon | fires ammo from the quiver along the facing line, up to 6 cells |\\n  | thrown weapon (dagger, darts, hand axe, spear) | throws it |\\n  | spellbook or holy symbol | opens the cast menu |\\n  | wand | zaps |\\n  | shield | **Brace**: +3 Defense for 2 s |\\n  | nothing | punches (1d2) |\\n\\n  Using a hand starts its cooldown: the weapon's speed (§7.7) × ★attack cooldown × (1 − 0.04 × DEX modifier). Casting a spell puts **both** of the caster's hands on 2.5 s.\\n- **Party Strike** (□, Space, right-click in the view). Every member whose main hand is ready, and whose main-hand item can act from their row, acts at once:\\n  - the front row melees;\\n  - row 2 attacks with reach weapons;\\n  - anyone holding a missile or thrown weapon fires it.\\n\\n  Spellbooks and holy symbols are skipped, because a spell needs a choice. With nothing in front, the front row \\\"swings at the air.\\\"\\n- **To-hit.** d20 + to-hit bonus (class) + STR modifier (melee and thrown) or DEX modifier (missile) + weapon bonus + ★party to-hit + buffs ≥ the target's Defense.\\n  - A natural 20 always hits for double dice; a natural 1 always misses.\\n  - Damage is the weapon's dice + STR modifier (1.5× for two-handed weapons), × ★party damage, at least 1.\\n  - A miss shows MISS on the hand slot.\\n- **Party Defense.** 10 + armour + shield + DEX modifier + helm, bracers and rings + buffs.\\n- **Monster attacks.** A monster's attack roll is d20 + its attack bonus ≥ the member's Defense; its damage is its dice × ★monster damage.\\n- **Who gets hit.** It depends on where the attacker stands relative to the party's facing:\\n  - from the front: a random conscious member of the front-most occupied row;\\n  - from the left: the left column (places 1, 3, 5), front-most first;\\n  - from the right: the right column (2, 4, 6);\\n  - from behind: the back-most occupied row.\\n\\n  The HUD shows red chevrons on the edge the hit came from (§5.2), and the hit sound is panned.\\n- **Projectiles** (bolts, arrows, darts, thrown items, Spark Darts, Locking Bolts) move cell by cell at their own speed (8 cells/s for missiles, 6 for Spark Dart, 5 for monster bolts) and hit the first creature in their path.\\n  - A monster bolt reaching the party's cell hits the party, through the side it came from.\\n  - A party projectile hits the monster in the target cell's slot nearest the shooter's column.\\n  - Spent ammo drops in the cell where it stopped, with a 50% chance to be recovered.\\n- **Statuses** (seconds left, in `member.status` and `mon.status`):\\n\\n  | Status | Effect |\\n  |---|---|\\n  | Poisoned | 1 HP every 6 s for 60 s, or until Purge or an Antidote |\\n  | Held | can't act for 4 to 10 s; Free Hinge or the Lidless Ward prevents it |\\n  | Asleep (monsters) | wakes when damaged; takes ×2 damage |\\n  | Slowed | intervals ×1.5 |\\n  | Blessed / Steady | +1 to-hit and +1 to saves |\\n  | Warded | an absorb pool |\\n  | Floating | over pits; no plates |\\n  | Seeing | secrets glint |\\n  | Turned | undead flee |\\n\\n  A **save** is a d20 roll ≥ 15 − level/2 − WIS or CON modifier.\\n\\n### 4.7 Monsters and their AI\\n\\n#### 4.7.1 Size and cells\\n- Small monsters take 1 of 4 units in a cell, medium 2 and large 4; a cell holds 4 units.\\n- Monsters never enter the party's cell or walls, closed doors or pits. Fliers ignore pits and plates.\\n- Small monsters don't weigh plates; medium and large ones do.\\n\\n#### 4.7.2 Minds (per type in §7.6)\\n- **States.**\\n  - `asleep`: placed sleeping; noise wakes it.\\n  - `idle` and `patrol`: a list of cells to walk.\\n  - `hunt`: paths to the party with `E.Grid` A*. Cells that are full are blocked, so others take the side and back cells, and **flanking happens on its own**.\\n  - `engage`: next to the party it faces, winds up and strikes.\\n  - `ranged`: in line with a clear view and in range, it shoots.\\n  - `keepAway`: casters hold 3 cells off and step back if you close in.\\n  - `flee`: cowards below 25% HP run for 6 s; thieves flee after a steal.\\n  - `turned`, `held`, `asleep`.\\n- **Awareness.**\\n  - A monster becomes aware when the party's cell is in its sight radius (★sight) and its field of view (E.Fog-style shadowcasting from the monster, or the symmetric check `fog.visible` from the party, as the kit does).\\n  - **Noise** (combat, doors, levers, falls) wakes monsters within 4 cells; hounds hear to 6.\\n  - A monster forgets the party after 12 s out of sight and goes back to `patrol`.\\n- **Movement.** One cell per `move` seconds (per type), drawn as a glide.\\n\\n#### 4.7.3 Attacks\\n- **Every melee attack telegraphs.** The wind-up (★0.5 s; heavy monsters 0.8 s) is a visible animation with a sound. The strike lands only if the party is still next to the monster when the wind-up ends; otherwise \\\"The rat's bite snaps on air.\\\" **This makes the sidestep a skill.**\\n- **Re-engaging.** After the party changes cell, a monster next to it waits ★0.6 s before starting a new wind-up (the \\\"dance\\\" is fair but not free).\\n- **Intervals.** Each type has its own interval × ★monster interval.\\n\\n#### 4.7.4 The Bolt-Holder (boss, floor 4)\\n\\nIt hovers over the arena's centre cell (6,3) with **HP ★320** and Defense 15. It is immune to Hold, Sleep and Poison, and it **absorbs lightning**: Forked Lightning heals it for half, and it gloats \\\"The Bolt-Holder drinks the lightning!\\\"\\n\\n| Phase | When | Behaviour |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **1: Caged** | the start | It takes ×0.2 damage through the cage and attacks every 3.5 s. Each of the 3 **Great Locks** (west, east and north walls) turned with ✕ (2.0 s, during which the party can't act) slides out 2 of its 7 bolts (\\\"The Bolt-Holder shrieks!\\\"). When all 3 are turned, the cage opens. |\\n| **2: Unbolted** | all locks turned | It takes full damage, attacks every 2.8 s and **drifts** one cell toward the party's flank every 4 s (it never enters pillar cells). At 50% HP it **relocks** one lock at random (\\\"It wrenches a bolt home!\\\"): damage taken is ×0.5 until that lock is turned again. |\\n| **3: Wrath** | HP below 25% | It attacks every 2.2 s and summons 2 Gazers every 12 s (4 at most). |\\n\\nIts attacks, picked by its position and line of sight:\\n- **Chain Lightning** (any phase): telegraphed for 0.8 s by a cyan glow and a flicker along the row or column toward the party. The bolt runs along the line until a pillar or wall: 3d6 to 2 members. Leave the line, or put a pillar between you, to dodge it.\\n- **Locking Gaze:** the iris narrows for 1.0 s, then 1 or 2 members without the Lidless Ward or Free Hinge are Held for 4 s (\\\"Your joints lock!\\\"). It needs line of sight, and pillars block it.\\n- **Bolt Rain:** marks the party's cell and 2 open neighbouring cells with glowing rings (`world.arc`) for 1.5 s, then iron bolts slam down: 2d6 to 2 members if the party is still in a marked cell.\\n- **Cage Slam** (adjacent only): 2d8 to the side facing it.\\n\\nOn death the Eye cracks, the bolts fly off, and the north lock wall becomes the **Stair to the Light** (✕ there starts the ending).\\n\\n### 4.8 Magic\\n\\n- **Mages** cast from their **spellbook** (an off-hand item). The book holds the spells they know; new ones come from scrolls through Camp → Scribe, which always succeeds and uses up the scroll.\\n- **Clerics** need their **holy symbol** in a hand. They may prepare any prayer of a level they can cast.\\n- **Memorizing.** Both choose what fills their slots in Camp → Memorize or Pray. The choice persists (\\\"same as before\\\" is the default), and slots refill after a full rest. Casting spends a slot.\\n- **Scrolls.** A mage can cast a scroll directly, and the scroll is used up. The Scroll of Raising works for clerics and paladins.\\n- **Wands** have charges and anyone can use one.\\n- **Slots by caster level, 1 to 8:**\\n\\n  | Caster | Spell level | Lv1 | Lv2 | Lv3 | Lv4 | Lv5 | Lv6 | Lv7 | Lv8 |\\n  |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n  | Mage | 1 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 4 | 4 | 4 |\\n  | Mage | 2 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 |\\n  | Mage | 3 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 3 |\\n  | Cleric | 1 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 3 | 4 | 4 |\\n  | Cleric | 2 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 3 |\\n  | Cleric | 3 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 2 |\\n\\n  Bonus slots come from INT and WIS (§4.3) and from the Robe of the Lintel (+1 level-1 slot).\\n- **Targets.**\\n  - `front`: the cell in front.\\n  - `line`: down the facing line.\\n  - `member`: picked on the cards.\\n  - `party`.\\n  - `door`: the door in front.\\n- **Spell effects** are × ★spell power. The spell list is in §7.8.\\n\\n### 4.9 Camp, rest and food\\n\\n- **Camp** (L3, C, or the HUD's camp icon) is refused while any aware monster is within 6 cells: \\\"You may not rest with enemies near.\\\"\\n- **Camp menu tiles:** Rest, Memorize, Pray, Scribe, Formation, Eat, Save Game, Load Game, Settings and Leave Camp.\\n- **Resting.** An hour passes every 0.4 s of real time. Each hour every conscious member heals ★1 + CON modifier (at least 1) × ★rest heal.\\n  - After 8 hours, slots refill to the prepared spells, Lay on Hands returns, and Down members wake at 1 HP.\\n  - During rest, clerics first cast their prepared Mends on the wounded (as the source let the party do), then pray to restore them.\\n  - Rest stops early when everyone is full and every slot is ready, or when ○ is pressed.\\n- **Interruptions.** Each hour has a ★4% chance (0 in safe rooms and once the floor's wanderer budget is spent: floor 1: 3, floor 2: 3, floor 3: 4, floor 4: 0) of spawning a wanderer group from the floor's spawn list, 2 cells away and aware. \\\"You are awakened by something moving!\\\" The camp closes.\\n- **Food** runs 0 to 100 for each member.\\n  - It drains −1 every ★60 s of play and −15 per full rest. ★Hunger rate scales it.\\n  - At 25: \\\"Cobb is hungry.\\\" At 0: \\\"Cobb is starving!\\\" A starving member loses 1 HP every 30 s and heals nothing from rest.\\n  - A Ration gives +50 and an Iron Ration +100. Loaves of the Hearth fills everyone.\\n  - **Eat** at camp feeds every member below 60% from the party's smallest food items.\\n\\n### 4.10 Experience, levels and hidden deeds\\n\\n- **XP for kills** is split evenly among conscious members, then × class and race multipliers and × ★XP gain.\\n- **Base thresholds:** level 2 at 100, 3 at 250, 4 at 500, 5 at 900, 6 at 1500, 7 at 2400 and 8 at 3600 (the demo's cap).\\n- **Discoveries.** A found secret gives +25 to each member and plays the `secret` sting. There are 3, marked `secret: true` in the floor data: the floor 1 closet (SW1/H1), the floor 1 illusory wall (I1) and the floor 2 catch (SW2). A hidden deed (special quest) gives +100 to each member, plays a jingle and shows \\\"A hidden deed is done!\\\". There are 3 deeds in all; Journal → Deeds counts them.\\n- **Level-up.** On the next rest or at once (the default is at once, with the \\\"level up\\\" sting): new HP, to-hit and slots, a portrait smile and a toast \\\"Brannoc has reached level 3!\\\".\\n- **Target pace** (the bot checks it, §14): about level 3 at the end of floor 1, 4 at the end of floor 2, 5 on floor 3, and 5 or 6 at the boss.\\n\\n### 4.11 Down, death, raising and game over\\n\\n- **Down.** At 0 HP a member is **Down**: unconscious, greyed portrait, can't act. A Down member hit again becomes **Dead** (bones on the card).\\n- **Waking.** Healing wakes a Down member at the healed amount; a full rest wakes them at 1 HP.\\n- **Raising the dead.** Raise from Rest (cleric spell level 3), the Scroll of Raising (2 placed) or the **Shrine of the Threshold** (floor 2 Vault, one use) brings a dead member back at 1 HP.\\n- **Game over.** If no member is conscious, the screen reads \\\"THE PARTY IS LOST\\\" over the frozen view, with Load last save, Load game and Title.\\n\\n### 4.12 NPCs, dialogue and choices\\n\\n- **Recruits.** Three NPCs can join, up to 6 in the party: **Tamsin Pell** (floor 1), **Durgan Copperhand** (floor 2) and **Sister Veil** (floor 3). Their scripts are in §7.9.\\n- **Dismissing.** Dismiss is in the Party screen, behind a confirm. A dismissed NPC goes home and is gone for good.\\n- **How it runs.** Dialogue is `E.Story` nodes through `E.Dialog`:\\n  - the speaker's live rig portrait, its mouth moving as it speaks;\\n  - a **babble voice** (§6.5);\\n  - choices picked with the d-pad and ✕, or a click;\\n  - story flags kept in the save (`story.state()`).\\n- **Veil's choice** changes floor 3 (§7.4.3).\\n- **Barks.** Short, non-modal lines (`modal: false, auto: 2`) for Snick, the Bolt-Holder and party barks.\\n\\n### 4.13 Messages, Examine, Journal, notes and hints\",\"numLines\":200,\"startLine\":489,\"totalLines\":2131}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01RJ7LtBu3ozHzHoqHpUgC5z\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40\",\"uuid\":\"8615c5bc-45c0-4750-aba5-539bc968b768\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":200,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40\",\"uuid\":\"76fef16f-3048-44b9-84c3-98afffcf9179\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":350,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40\",\"uuid\":\"3998817c-0de0-4adc-bc3e-0714331c2b90\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2391,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2391,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":7200,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"265f694a-5cb7-42ac-ba5a-ef2efc9a6dbf\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":7400,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":200,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"517e29ff-228b-477d-8588-35db1112ac45\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":7550,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"edcb582e-737f-4c16-a672-7b90b8df5083\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":7700,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"dd3f2996-649d-4306-8743-08e4ef7560a2\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":7850,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"ccb79183-2fc7-40e2-b115-aa1a54153681\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174822__x21985c/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2207,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2207,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":100,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a\",\"uuid\":\"875200b0-dab8-4e73-8c20-47d6f85597be\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":350,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":250,\"session_id\":\"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a\",\"uuid\":\"d14a49f8-6945-4e1c-9c8f-0aa5b58758b2\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":650,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":300,\"session_id\":\"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a\",\"uuid\":\"6729bf83-93e0-4c4a-93f0-5a959471f031\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":800,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a\",\"uuid\":\"37526666-ceed-4261-8f57-1e99780d5ec0\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":950,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a\",\"uuid\":\"27e32cf1-cb17-4189-b5f6-ac7530a9bfda\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174831__x898ed5/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2146,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2146,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh3VRHWcng1wiRMxptzX\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01FqD7JHwPhoe6wqTbDmwzaA\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"COIN_TOSS\\\\*\\\\*\\\\|PLAN_PART_END\\\\|Fiasco rules\\\\*\\\\*\\\\|One yard is one tile\\\\|secrets.randbelow\\\" PLAN.md | head; sed -n '1,12p' PLAN.md\",\"description\":\"Check distinctive phrases and the opening lines\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2848,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":533856,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2848},\"output_tokens\":4,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"c28e7abf-db6e-401a-a911-43ba9983a968\",\"uuid\":\"e3bbb916-1447-4362-8a47-8029dfaa2ffd\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:46:37.611Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh3VR4cmUdUWRf8Q29g8\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01FqD7JHwPhoe6wqTbDmwzaA\":{\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174831__x898ed5/work && grep -n \\\"COIN_TOSS\\\\*\\\\*\\\\|PLAN_PART_END\\\\|Fiasco rules\\\\*\\\\*\\\\|One yard is one tile\\\\|secrets.randbelow\\\" PLAN.md | head; sed -n '1,12p' PLAN.md\",\"description\":\"Check distinctive phrases and the opening lines\"}},\"wire_ingest_context\":{\"toolu_01FqD7JHwPhoe6wqTbDmwzaA\":{\"cwd\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174831__x898ed5/work\"}}}"," {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01FqD7JHwPhoe6wqTbDmwzaA\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"15:with a real random number generator: Python `secrets.randbelow(50)`, which uses OS entropy, gave index 33, which is\\n85:**Fiasco rules** (arcade simplifications, said on the loading tips and the Help screen): 7 per side; 4 downs to gain\\n334:**One yard is one tile, 16 world units.** The engine's own scale is 16 units = 1 m and a 26-unit hero, so players\\n417:- **COIN_TOSS** (1.5 s): the home mascot flips a giant coin (cosmetic). The winner is `FF.rng.sim`'s, or the\\n# AMERICAN FOOTBALL FIASCO\\n\\n**The build plan.** Source: American football (over-the-top arcade style). Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the\\nhandoff package). Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1. Planned on 2026-11-03 by claude-opus-5-5 (reasoning effort max)\\nfrom `TASK.md` and `STAGE.md`. This plan is for the developers who will build the game from `TASK.md` and this file\\nalone, possibly other AI models working without the planner. Every engine and hub name it uses was checked against\\nthe real files during planning (engine commit `4390a9852fe0`, hub commit `f8835e4824fb`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Read this first\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"c28e7abf-db6e-401a-a911-43ba9983a968\",\"uuid\":\"07c51bb4-45f2-45c7-ad07-be3fdb27c3ed\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:46:37.628Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"15:with a real random number generator: Python `secrets.randbelow(50)`, which uses OS entropy, gave index 33, which is\\n85:**Fiasco rules** (arcade simplifications, said on the loading tips and the Help screen): 7 per side; 4 downs to gain\\n334:**One yard is one tile, 16 world units.** The engine's own scale is 16 units = 1 m and a 26-unit hero, so players\\n417:- **COIN_TOSS** (1.5 s): the home mascot flips a giant coin (cosmetic). The winner is `FF.rng.sim`'s, or the\\n# AMERICAN FOOTBALL FIASCO\\n\\n**The build plan.** Source: American football (over-the-top arcade style). Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the\\nhandoff package). Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1. Planned on 2026-11-03 by claude-opus-5-5 (reasoning effort max)\\nfrom `TASK.md` and `STAGE.md`. This plan is for the developers who will build the game from `TASK.md` and this file\\nalone, possibly other AI models working without the planner. Every engine and hub name it uses was checked against\\nthe real files during planning (engine commit `4390a9852fe0`, hub commit `f8835e4824fb`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Read this first\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01FqD7JHwPhoe6wqTbDmwzaA\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"c28e7abf-db6e-401a-a911-43ba9983a968\",\"uuid\":\"640210a0-4003-4d92-8a11-9b1049b0f9a1\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":150,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"c28e7abf-db6e-401a-a911-43ba9983a968\",\"uuid\":\"a93e1488-b2a9-4f4f-b135-6edc64323b74\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":300,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"c2