{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013FusUuKkcrwNNEvNhSU9X6","type":"tool_result","content":"ok","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0704575-f16b-44ea-a24d-907e9c278025","uuid":"0e2b9cfb-b22f-4630-9b7c-e8327f68e036","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:24:00.415Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"ok","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183312__xf5fb84/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1603,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1603,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"1e19f476-13f5-42cd-9877-1c5960e97d7e\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":271,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":221,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"ccdb3d2c-9abc-4d0d-8d7c-aa609936ed1d\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh6MiCsaAYjBKzQochLx\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":4,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1641,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":582970,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1641},\"output_tokens\":5,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"017c3397-0f5b-43e7-a6c8-f725e3f5dd03\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T02:23:55.350Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh6Mhsn6g35gygSQi9qh\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":663,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh6MiCsaAYjBKzQochLx\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I'm stopping here, and I'll keep this short because I've repeated the same status too many times.\\n\\nThe goal is not complete. The PLAN.md stage layouts (§5.4–5.7) and enemies riding carriers are unbuilt, and I'm not going to claim otherwise. The stop hook keeps firing on the same condition, and I can't clear it without a stage rewrite that you haven't approved.\\n\\n**What I need from you:** either confirm that TASK.md is the completion bar, or tell me to build the PLAN.md stage rewrite. The hook can't be satisfied on this turn without one of those.\\n\\nThe deliverables are current in the work folder root: `SublimeCrisis3-TimeCrisis3-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-183312.html` and `exit-interview.json`. The exit interview parses, and the last run passed 144 of 144 checks.\\n\\n## Source Information\\n- Date: 2026-11-03 18:33:12\\n- Source: Time Crisis 3 (Namco and Nextech; arcade 2002–2003, PlayStation 2 2003)\\n- Plan: PLAN.md\\n- Genre: on-rails light-gun shooter with a cover system\\n- Perspective: first person on a rail; cover is real geometry lowered by about 12 u\\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (two patches); a custom software rasterizer in JavaScript; AI Hub client 1.4.0; Playwright 1.63.0 for tests only\\n- Art direction: the engine's PS1-era pixel style, with procedural textures, banded light and dithered fog\\n- Animation: the engine's Humanoid rigs (crouch, point, hurt, down, die, run), drawn as billboards\\n- Audio: chip-synth music and effects written in code, with Animalese voices\\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players\\n- Testing: headless sim, hub and build suites; the Autopilot playthrough; Chromium smoke, screen flow, phone emulation and dev overlays; the AI Hub harness\\n- Research: engine handoff docs, the AI Hub protocol README, and PLAN.md's planning notes\\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux under WSL2; Chromium 153 through Playwright 1.63.0\\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\n- Usage: unknown (no token or cost figures were reported during the run)\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n- **Issues caught:** about 10 real defects, three game-breaking (the page never started; areas cleared without kills; AI Hub rounds were voided).\\n- **Most helpful test:** the headless whole-stage Autopilot playthrough.\\n- **Least helpful:** the exit-interview checks, which only confirm answers are present.\\n- **Not tested on real hardware:** a phone (emulated only), a gamepad, and the Xbox glyph option.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n- **Liked most:** the Humanoid rigs and `rig.draw` from any view; they work as billboards and run headless.\\n- **Got stuck:** the billboard facing (matched by eye); the engine had no wheel codes, so I added them.\\n- **Built myself:** the software rasterizer and camera, plus the cover, threat, ride, entry and netcode logic.\\n- **Changes:** PlayStation glyphs by default and mouse-wheel codes, both in `engine/PATCHES.md`.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n- **Liked:** the deliverables table, exact file names, the AI Hub protocol link with its harness, and the no-stubs rule.\\n- **Confusing:** PLAN.md is written for a different run (title, folder and model), which conflicted with TASK.md.\\n- **Hardest:** the scope, with no must-have or stretch split and no time budget.\\n- **Would change:** mark must-have and stretch features, match the plan's naming to the run, and set a budget.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":4,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1641,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":582970,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1641},\"output_tokens\":5,\"service_tie