{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SNVL6hu1DRwfVTMNb6xJxX","type":"tool_result","content":"still mine: 1680815 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183009__xe162c9/work/OperationWolfpack-OperationWolf-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183009\ntotal 1860\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 micha micha    4096 Nov  3 20:20 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 micha micha    4096 Nov  3 18:30 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 10 micha micha    4096 Nov  3 20:29 OperationWolfpack-OperationWolf-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183009\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha 1738976 Nov  3 20:25 OperationWolfpack-OperationWolf-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183009.html\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha  124494 Nov  3 18:30 PLAN.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha     347 Nov  3 18:30 STAGE.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    8757 Nov  3 18:30 TASK.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    7922 Nov  3 20:25 exit-interview.json\nexit-interview ok: ['sourceInformation', 'testingFeedback', 'engineFeedback', 'promptFeedback', 'aiHub'] 15\n# Engine changes (my-3D2dge v0.85.2, handoff copy) made for Operation Wolfpack\n\nEvery edit to `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, and why.\n\n1. **Mode 7 views reuse whole-degree pitches** (`Mode7.view`). The view a billboard is drawn with was keyed by the\n   camera's exact pitch, so a bobbing camera (the river op's boat) made a new `E.View` every frame, and every shape\n   sprite cached on a view was rebuilt every frame. The pitch is now rounded to whole degrees for the drawing view.\n2. **Stereo pan for sound effects** (`audio.sfx(voice, { pan: -1..1 })`). A `StereoPannerNode` per call between the\n   voices and the effects bus, so gunfire, rotors and explosions sit left or right of the screen. Without `pan` nothing\n   changes.\n3. **PlayStation glyphs by default** (the standard `glyphs` setting). The task designs for a DualSense first, with an\n   Xbox option: the setting now defaults to `'playstation'`, offers PlayStation and Xbox only, and applies to every\n   local player's input.\n4. **Settings rows on any Shell screen** (`shell.show(name, { rows: [[heading, [keys]]] })`). A screen of the game's own\n   can list settings rows (sliders, toggles, selects) drawn by the Shell's own `_row`, with pad, key and mouse focus: the\n   dev screen's live sliders are settings in a group of their own.\n5. **Hidden setting groups** (`E.Shell.hiddenGroups = ['Dev']`). The standard Settings screen skips those groups, so the\n   dev sliders live in `game.settings` (saved, checked, reset by `settings.reset('Dev')`) without crowding Settings.\n6. **PlayStation button symbols in the 5x7 font** (✕ ○ □ △, the middle dot · and a check ✓). `input.label()` returns them for a\n   DualSense, but the pixel font had no glyphs for them, so every canvas prompt drew \"?\".","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0704575-f16b-44ea-a24d-907e9c278025","uuid":"838ba12b-19ba-48bc-b9f0-0f9000d45370","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:29:17.358Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"still mine: 1680815 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183009__xe162c9/work/OperationWolfpack-OperationWolf-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183009\ntotal 1860\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 micha micha    4096 Nov  3 20:20 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 micha micha    4096 Nov  3 18:30 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 10 micha micha    4096 Nov  3 20:29 OperationWolfpack-OperationWolf-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183009\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha 1738976 Nov  3 20:25 OperationWolfpack-OperationWolf-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183009.html\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha  124494 Nov  3 18:30 PLAN.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha     347 Nov  3 18:30 STAGE.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    8757 Nov  3 18:30 TASK.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    7922 Nov  3 20:25 exit-interview.json\nexit-interview ok: ['sourceInformation', 'testingFeedback', 'engineFeedback', 'promptFeedback', 'aiHub'] 15\n# Engine changes (my-3D2dge v0.85.2, handoff copy) made for Operation Wolfpack\n\nEvery edit to `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, and why.\n\n1. **Mode 7 views reuse whole-degree pitches** (`Mode7.view`). The view a billboard is drawn with was keyed by the\n   camera's exact pitch, so a bobbing camera (the river op's boat) made a new `E.View` every frame, and every shape\n   sprite cached on a view was rebuilt every frame. The pitch is now rounded to whole degrees for the drawing view.\n2. **Stereo pan for sound effects** (`audio.sfx(voice, { pan: -1..1 })`). A `StereoPannerNode` per call between the\n   voices and the effects bus, so gunfire, rotors and explosions sit left or right of the screen. Without `pan` nothing\n   changes.\n3. **PlayStation glyphs by default** (the standard `glyphs` setting). The task designs for a DualSense first, with an\n   Xbox option: the setting now defaults to `'playstation'`, offers PlayStation and Xbox only, and applies to every\n   local player's input.\n4. **Settings rows on any Shell screen** (`shell.show(name, { rows: [[heading, [keys]]] })`). A screen of the game's own\n   can list settings rows (sliders, toggles, selects) drawn by the Shell's own `_row`, with pad, key and mouse focus: the\n   dev screen's live sliders are settings in a group of their own.\n5. **Hidden setting groups** (`E.Shell.hiddenGroups = ['Dev']`). The standard Settings screen skips those groups, so the\n   dev sliders live in `game.settings` (saved, checked, reset by `settings.reset('Dev')`) without crowding Settings.\n6. **PlayStation button symbols in the 5x7 font** (✕ ○ □ △, the middle dot · and a check ✓). `input.label()` returns them for a\n   DualSense, but the pixel font had no glyphs for them, so every canvas prompt drew \"?\".","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SNVL6hu1DRwfVTMNb6xJxX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
