irm = R2 □ ✕\nPASS UX: a Settings option shows Xbox glyphs (A B X Y) -- Settings > Game > Button symbols = Xbox -> RT X A\nPASS UX: keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse -- fire: Left click / Space; grenade: Right click / G; reload: R; snap: Q; pause: Esc/P; aim: mouse or WASD/arrows\nPASS UX: prompts follow the input used last -- input.lastDevice: pad press -> gamepad, key press -> keyboard; every prompt uses input.label(action)\nPASS UX: the mouse aims (absolute, like a light gun) -- pointer (123,77) -> crosshair (123,77)\nPASS UX: the mouse hovers to move the focus and clicks menu items -- hover over HIGH SCORES -> focus 3; click -> scores\nPASS UX: 10-foot sizes, not dense web-style screens -- canvas menus at scale 2 with a pulsing chevron; Shell CSS 20 px body, 34 px titles, 52 px buttons; About split into 8 screens\nPASS Touch-only: no touch controls; \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the settings button -- touch-only detected, no touch buttons, notice shown, a tap on SETTINGS opens settings\nPASS Touch-only: the attract mode runs -- after 11 s: play (demo)\nPASS Done: no TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features in the game code -- no TODO/FIXME/placeholder/stub text and no empty function bodies in src/\nPASS Source Information + feedback in an in-game About/Credits screen -- SOURCE INFORMATION (1/3) | SOURCE INFORMATION (2/3) | SOURCE INFORMATION (3/3) | TESTING FEEDBACK | ENGINE FEEDBACK (1/2) | ENGINE FEEDBACK (2/2) | PROMPT FEEDBACK | CREDITS\nPASS Exit interview: parses, exact shape, every value filled -- 15 source fields, 4/6/4 answers, aiHub Operation Wolfpack / Shooter / 1–4\n34 passed, 0 failed","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TRrnizJvYtJmRMU39ueMxB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
