{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghCuL1xk342f4aBGqRvC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game is done, and I have no further way to strengthen the evidence. Every check that remains possible here was written by me, and no independent verifier is available in this environment. Here is what the transcript does show:\n\n- **STAGE.md and TASK.md:** after the earlier truncation I printed both files again in full (`cat STAGE.md` and `cat TASK.md`), and every requirement in them has a matching check below.\n- **Dev sliders:** TASK.md asks for \"the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults\" and names no count. The 23 sliders cover weapon, ammo, grenades, aim assist, enemy toughness and aggression, spawns, pacing, drops, penalties, healing and game speed. A run set each one and confirmed it changed the game immediately, and that reset restored them all.\n- **No stubs:** beyond the text search, I listed every empty function in the game code and removed all five, so none remain. The full test suite then passed again, including two complete headless playthroughs of all six operations, bosses, cutscenes and ending.\n- **Touch-only, co-op and Xbox prompts:** besides the headless tests, I drove the shipped `.html` in a real browser like a player. That run covered an emulated phone, two virtual DualSense pads with the second pressing Options to join mid-operation, and clicking the real Settings screen to switch to Xbox. All 8 checks passed, and the screenshots match.\n\nThe final runs were `npm test` with 255 passed and 0 failed (headless suites, browser checks, and the real AI Hub harness in all 5 configurations), and `npm run audit` with 34 passed and 0 failed. `tools/verify-browser.mjs` passed all 8 checks.\n\nThe game is `OperationWolfpack-OperationWolf-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183009.html` in this folder's root, with `exit-interview.json` beside it. Balance was tuned against a bot rather than real players. Online play passed the hub's test harness and a simulated session, but hasn't been played by people on separate machines.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:30:09\n- **Source:** Operation Wolf (Taito, 1987), the arcade light-gun shooter with the mounted submachine gun.\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md, written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort. Where it differed from TASK.md (file names), TASK.md won.\n- **Genre and Perspective:** a light-gun rail shooter with bosses, hostage escorts and drop-in co-op. It's first person on a scripted rail: sideways, forward up a river, and backward off a plane's ramp.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2, the full engine from the handoff package, with 6 edits logged in `engine/CHANGES.md`. Also the AI Hub session client 1.4.0, and plain JavaScript in one HTML file. Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 are used for tests and tools only.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native procedural pixel art, plus 66 new shapes, 35 sprites and 23 dressed character rigs. The Mode 7 floors are painted per pixel, and the setting (the Brimstone Coast) is original.\n- **Animation:** the engine's character rig system, plus new poses: hands up, bound hostages, panic, the officer's whistle, the rocket on the shoulder, the collar grab and the villain's cackle. Vehicles, the first-person gun and effects are animated procedurally.\n- **Audio:** all synthesized in code with no audio files. That covers 17 songs and stings, 58 sound effects with stereo pan, and Animalese-style gibberish voices with subtitles, barks and a wolf howl.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in shared-world mode for 1–4 players. The host runs the world and clients report their hits. It handles the game's own pre-round card, time-up, players leaving and the round ending. Local drop-in co-op supports 1–4 controllers.\n- **Testing:** allowed were headless tools, scripted playthroughs and screenshots for looks only, with no subagents. Used:\n  - `npm test`: 22 suites and 255 checks, printing only failures and one count line;\n  - `npm run audit`: one line per TASK.md requirement;\n  - `tools/verify-browser.mjs`: player-style checks on the shipped file.\n- **Research:** none of my own beyond the given plan (which cites Wikipedia and arcade-history.com) and the engine's and hub's docs.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); headless Chromium 153 through Playwright for the checks.\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh.\n- **Usage:** cost and token count are unknown (not visible to me). The session time is about 2 hours 15 minutes, estimated when I wrote the About pages; the final checks ran later than that.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 30. Most came from the headless suites, the playthroughs and the per-operation damage reports. The rest came from screenshots and the browser.\n2. **How many would be considered critical / game breaking?** About 10:\n   - two bosses never arrived;\n   - the CROCODILE gunboat couldn't be killed;\n   - grenades and mortar shells couldn't be shot down;\n   - four crashes: at boot, in the takeoff's HUD, in the takeoff cutscene, and on a hub client;\n   - the playthrough bot lost its input after the first operation.\n3. **What was the most helpful test?** The headless whole-game playthrough by a bot with human-like reaction times, on the easiest difficulty with no cheats.\n4. **What was the least helpful test?** The projection round-trip test. It never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** Exact headless determinism, which lets the whole campaign run as a test in seconds. Mode 7 with the character rigs gives real depth cheaply, and the standard menus came free.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n   - `m7.shape` ignores shape parameters and materials;\n   - the engine reads a scene's `view` field, which clashed with a name I used;\n   - `game.go` fails during boot steps, and timers are cleared on scene change;\n   - `E.store` doesn't persist when running headless;\n   - the font lacked the PlayStation symbols that `input.label` returns;\n   - `E.Menu` has no scale option for text readable from 10 feet.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The light-gun layer on Mode 7. That's hit shapes calibrated to the drawn rigs, plus a deterministic game simulation (rail, beats, telegraphed attacks, shootable projectiles, six phased bosses). It also needed the bot and the shared-world netcode.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Making what you hit match what Mode 7 draws, and lighting the night stages under Mode 7.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?** Six edits:\n   - Mode 7 views keyed by whole-degree camera pitch, so a bobbing camera stops rebuilding every shape sprite each frame;\n   - stereo pan for sound effects;\n   - PlayStation button symbols by default, with Xbox as an option;\n   - Shell settings rows usable on any screen, for the dev sliders;\n   - hidden setting groups;\n   - the glyphs ✕ ○ □ △ · ✓ added to the font.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** Make Mode 7 a first-class depth renderer: shapes with parameters, materials and a hit flash, a lighting pass, and a `pick()` hit test for its billboards.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** A clear, testable definition of done, freedom of design, a detailed plan, and one quiet test command.\n2. **What was confusing?** The plan used another run's file names. The random-title rule conflicted with STAGE.md's \"use the plan's title\". And \"read only what you need\" sat oddly with docs that had to be read.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** The scope in one sitting, and balancing it so a fair player can finish.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Split the AI Hub integration from the single-player build, or give a target demo length. Also let the task file carry the run-specific name tokens."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3183,"cache_read_input_tokens":892534,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3183},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0704575-f16b-44ea-a24d-907e9c278025","uuid":"7b14d205-8c1a-4bcc-b6c7-f2f67f04cdaa","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:50:10.983Z","request_id":"req_011CghCuKh7jSko9wgrRdx7m"}
