{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghD3nSS8orwdeaVruCYC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ran the engine author's checker, `engine/tools/check.mjs`, on the shipped file. It reports **no errors** on the title screen, through pressing Start into the briefing, and in Operation 3 gameplay. That operation shows no look notes. The title run has four notes that 40–42% of the screen is one flat colour, and they come from the dark night-sea briefing. This checker, the hub's own test harness (all 5 configurations passed) and the browser itself are the only verifiers available here that I didn't write.\n\nEvery other feature check is my own work. I can't produce a verifier that isn't mine. If that limit is acceptable to you, the goal can be cleared now; otherwise tell me what independent check you'd accept.\n\n- **The game:** `OperationWolfpack-OperationWolf-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183009.html` is in the folder's root.\n- **The exit interview:** `exit-interview.json` parses and has every field filled.\n- **My test runs:** `npm test` passes 255 checks, `npm run audit` passes 34 TASK.md checks, and the player-style run on the shipped page passes 8. That last one covers touch-only, a second controller joining and the Xbox prompts.\n- **Your specific points:** 23 dev sliders is my choice, since TASK.md names no count. The no-stubs result is a text search plus removing every empty function, not a review of each feature by hand.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:30:09\n- **Source:** Operation Wolf (Taito, 1987), the arcade light-gun shooter.\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort); TASK.md won where they disagreed.\n- **Genre and Perspective:** light-gun rail shooter with bosses, hostage escorts and drop-in co-op. First person on a scripted rail: sideways, forward up a river, and backward off a plane's ramp.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 with 6 edits logged in `engine/CHANGES.md`; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; plain JavaScript in one HTML file; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests only.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native procedural pixel art, plus 66 shapes, 35 sprites and 23 dressed character rigs. The setting, the Brimstone Coast, is original.\n- **Animation:** the engine's character rigs plus new poses, with vehicles, the first-person gun and effects animated procedurally.\n- **Audio:** all synthesized in code, no audio files: 17 songs and stings, 58 sound effects, and Animalese-style gibberish voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in shared-world mode for 1–4 players, plus local drop-in co-op for 1–4 controllers.\n- **Testing:** allowed were headless tools, scripted playthroughs and screenshots for looks only, with no subagents. Used: `npm test` (255 checks), `npm run audit` (34), `tools/verify-browser.mjs` (8), the engine's `check.mjs`, and the hub harness.\n- **Research:** none of my own beyond the plan (which cites Wikipedia and arcade-history.com) and the engine's and hub's docs.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); headless Chromium 153 through Playwright.\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh.\n- **Usage:** cost and tokens unknown. The session time is an estimate of about 2 hours 15 minutes, made while writing the About pages; the final checks ran longer than that.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 30.\n2. **How many were critical or game-breaking?** About 10: bosses that never arrived or couldn't be killed, projectiles that couldn't be shot down, four crashes, and the playthrough bot losing its input.\n3. **Most helpful test:** the headless whole-game playthrough by a bot with human-like reaction times.\n4. **Least helpful test:** the projection round-trip test, which never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** exact headless determinism; Mode 7 with rigs giving cheap depth; standard menus for free.\n2. **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n   - `m7.shape` ignores shape parameters and materials.\n   - The engine reads a scene's `view` field, which clashed with my code.\n   - `game.go` fails inside boot steps, and timers are cleared on a scene change.\n   - Saved data doesn't persist headless.\n   - The font lacked the PlayStation button symbols.\n   - `E.Menu` has no scale option.\n3. **Most important thing I built myself:** the light-gun layer on Mode 7: calibrated hit shapes, a deterministic game simulation, six bosses, the bot and the netcode.\n4. **Hardest part:** making what you hit match what Mode 7 draws, and lighting the night stages under Mode 7.\n5. **What I changed in the engine:** six edits: Mode 7 view caching by whole-degree pitch, stereo pan, PlayStation button symbols by default, settings rows on any Shell screen, hidden setting groups, and the font glyphs ✕ ○ □ △ · ✓.\n6. **One thing I'd change:** make Mode 7 a first-class depth renderer with lighting and a `pick()` hit test.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** a clear, testable definition of done, freedom of design, a detailed plan, and one quiet test command.\n2. **What was confusing:** the plan used another run's file names; the random-title rule conflicted with STAGE.md's \"use the plan's title\"; and \"read only what you need\" sat awkwardly with docs that had to be read.\n3. **Hardest thing:** the scope in one sitting, and balancing it so a fair player can finish.\n4. **What I'd change:** split the AI Hub integration from the single-player build, or give a target demo length, and have the task file carry the run-specific name tokens."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2218,"cache_read_input_tokens":902542,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2218},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0704575-f16b-44ea-a24d-907e9c278025","uuid":"9171cb1a-5900-43fc-a804-0c5cdc6c3f10","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:51:58.395Z","request_id":"req_011CghD3n1t3ppZBhNtzsi74"}
