t, which never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** exact headless determinism, Mode 7 with character rigs giving depth cheaply, and the standard menus for free.\n2. **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n   - `m7.shape` ignores shape parameters and materials.\n   - A scene's `view` field clashed with a name I used.\n   - `game.go` fails inside boot steps, and timers are cleared on a scene change.\n   - `E.store` doesn't persist when running headless.\n   - The font lacked the PlayStation button symbols.\n   - `E.Menu` has no scale option.\n3. **The most important thing I built myself:** the light-gun layer on Mode 7: calibrated hit shapes, the deterministic simulation, six bosses, the bot and the netcode.\n4. **Hardest part:** making what you hit match what Mode 7 draws, and lighting the night stage under it.\n5. **What I changed in the engine:** six edits. Mode 7 caches its views by whole-degree pitch, sound effects get stereo pan, and PlayStation symbols are the default. Shell screens can show settings rows, setting groups can be hidden, and the font gains ✕ ○ □ △ · ✓.\n6. **One thing I'd change:** make Mode 7 a first-class depth renderer with lighting and a `pick()` hit test.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** a clear, testable definition of done, freedom of design, a detailed plan, and one quiet test command.\n2. **What was confusing:** the plan carried another run's file names, and the random-title rule conflicted with STAGE.md's \"use the plan's title\". The \"read only what you need\" rule also sat oddly with docs that had to be read.\n3. **Hardest thing:** the scope in one sitting, and balancing it so a fair player can finish.\n4. **What I'd change:** split the AI Hub integration from the single-player build, or give a target demo length. Have the task file carry the run-specific name tokens."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_to