{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghDF16jZ79VMdSyqYJDN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The goal check is asking for something no further work here can provide. It wants proof that every feature works, from a verifier other than me, and none exists in this environment. I've already run the only two independent checkers here, and both pass on the shipped game: the AI Hub project's own harness and the engine author's checker. So I'm not running more checks; the evidence below is final. If it's enough for you, `/goal clear` ends this loop; if not, tell me what independent check you'd accept.\n\nThe game, `OperationWolfpack-OperationWolf-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183009.html`, is in this folder's root, and `exit-interview.json` beside it parses with every field filled. My own test suites pass, but they test what I understood TASK.md to ask:\n\n- `npm test`: 255 checks, including two full playthroughs.\n- `npm run audit`: 34 checks, one per TASK.md requirement.\n- `tools/verify-browser.mjs`: 8 player-style checks in a real browser.\n\nBalance was tuned against a bot, not real players, and online play hasn't been tried by people on separate machines.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:30:09\n- **Source:** Operation Wolf (Taito, 1987).\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (claude-opus-5-5, max effort); TASK.md won where they differed.\n- **Genre and Perspective:** light-gun rail shooter with bosses, hostage escorts and co-op. First person on a scripted rail: sideways, forward up a river, and backward off a plane's ramp.\n- **Tech:**\n  - my-3D2dge v0.85.2, with 6 edits logged in `engine/CHANGES.md`.\n  - The AI Hub session client 1.4.0.\n  - Plain JavaScript in one HTML file.\n  - Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0, for tests only.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's procedural pixel art, plus 66 new shapes, 35 sprites and 23 dressed character rigs. The setting, the Brimstone Coast, is original.\n- **Animation:** the engine's character rigs plus new poses; vehicles, the first-person gun and effects are procedural.\n- **Audio:** all synthesized in code: 17 songs and stings, 58 sound effects, and Animalese-style gibberish voices. No audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world mode, 1–4 players; plus local drop-in co-op for 1–4.\n- **Testing:**\n  - Allowed: headless tools, scripted playthroughs, screenshots for looks only, no subagents.\n  - Used: `npm test` (255 checks), `npm run audit` (34), `tools/verify-browser.mjs` (8), the engine's `check.mjs`, and the hub harness.\n- **Research:** none beyond the plan and the engine and hub docs.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); headless Chromium 153.\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh.\n- **Usage:** cost and tokens unknown. About 2 h 15 min had passed when I wrote the About pages; the final checks ran past that.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 30.\n2. **How many were critical?** About 10: bosses that never arrived or couldn't be killed, grenades and shells that couldn't be shot down, four crashes, and the bot losing its input.\n3. **Most helpful test:** the headless whole-game playthrough.\n4. **Least helpful test:** the projection round-trip test, which never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** exact headless determinism; cheap depth from Mode 7 with rigs; standard menus for free.\n2. **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n   - `m7.shape` ignores shape parameters and materials.\n   - The scene `view` field clashed with my code.\n   - `game.go` fails during boot.\n   - Timers are cleared on scene change.\n   - Saved data doesn't persist headless.\n   - The font lacks the PlayStation button symbols.\n   - `E.Menu` has no scale option.\n3. **Most important thing I built myself:** the light-gun layer on Mode 7: hit detection, the simulation, the bosses, the bot and the netcode.\n4. **Hardest part:** matching what you hit to what Mode 7 draws, and lighting at night.\n5. **What I changed in the engine:** six edits:\n   - Mode 7 view caching.\n   - Stereo pan.\n   - PlayStation button symbols as the default.\n   - Shell settings rows.\n   - Hidden setting groups.\n   - New font glyphs.\n6. **One thing I'd change:** make Mode 7 a first-class depth renderer with lighting and a `pick()` hit test.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** a clear, testable definition of done, freedom of design, a detailed plan, and a single quiet test command.\n2. **What was confusing:** the plan used another run's file names; the random-title rule conflicted with STAGE.md; and \"read only what you need\" sat oddly with docs that had to be read.\n3. **Hardest thing:** the scope in one sitting, and balancing it for a fair player.\n4. **What I'd change:** split the AI Hub work from the single-player build, or give a target demo length; and let the task file carry the run-specific name tokens."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2743,"cache_read_input_tokens":913473,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2743},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0704575-f16b-44ea-a24d-907e9c278025","uuid":"ccbe4aa7-3eed-46cc-9d13-fb5e46b69a81","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:54:28.266Z","request_id":"req_011CghDEzhg695GaUqnDThZW"}
